      "name": "CancelScreenFade",
      "signature": "void CancelScreenFade(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Cancels any active screen fade effect by clearing the fade timeout\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear global fade end time variable to zero\n2. Return immediately to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\nFunction can be called safely even when no fade is active\nImmediate effect - any running ProcessScreenFadeOverlay will detect cancellation\n\nError Handling:\nNone required - simple memory store operation cannot fail\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x0 - Zero value indicating no active fade timeout\n0x6fbe8f14 - Address of g_dwFadeEndTime global variable",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:b2d0a8e1ba034e64cb61108e4c3a640aac6026ba1aeab5836ac6d47161a6c336",
