      "name": "PollBnetLoginCredentialValidation",
      "signature": "int PollBnetLoginCredentialValidation(void * pUnused)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Polling callback for MessagePumpLoop during Battle.net login credential validation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call BnclientInterface vtable offset 0x64 (credential check operation)\n2. If credential check returns non-zero, call StopMessageLoop to signal completion\n3. Check if g_bBnetLoggedIn is non-zero; if so, skip to step 7\n4. Call BnclientInterface vtable offset 0x74 (connection status check)\n5. If connected, call FUN_6fa77540 to check login state\n6. If login state check fails, exit early\n7. Call BnclientInterface vtable offset 0x10 (process tick)\n8. Call StopMessageLoop to end the loop\n9. Return 1 (always continue message pump until StopMessageLoop called)\n\nParameters:\n    pUnused - Unused context pointer passed from MessagePumpLoop (IMPLICIT: ECX points to stack)\n\nReturns:\n    1 - Always returns 1 to continue message pump polling\n\nCaller Context:\n    Called from FUN_6fa71430 via MessagePumpLoop(FUN_6fa71190) after initiating\n    credential validation with BnclientInterface+0x60\n\nBnclientInterface Virtual Table Offsets Used:\n    +0x10: Process/tick operation\n    +0x64: Credential validation check\n    +0x74: Connection status check\n\nGlobal References:\n    g_pBnclientInterface (0x6fa96c64): Battle.net client COM interface pointer\n    g_bBnetLoggedIn (0x6fa96c6c): Flag indicating logged-in state\n    g_dwGameStateFlags (0x6fa96c68): Game state flags checked for abort condition\n\nNote: Function body extends from 0x6fa71190 to 0x6fa711db (76 bytes) but Ghidra\nanalysis is incomplete. Raw disassembly shows RET 4 at end confirming __stdcall.",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
