      "name": "DispatchPendingControlHandlers",
      "signature": "undefined DispatchPendingControlHandlers(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Dispatch all pending control handler requests to their respective handlers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load count of pending handlers from g_nPendingControlHandlerCount\n2. If count <= 0, clear counter and return (early exit)\n3. Initialize loop counter nIndex to 0\n4. For each pending handler in g_aPendingControlHandlers:\n   a. Get current handler pointer (array element)\n   b. Call DispatchInventoryItemHandler with handler pointer\n   c. Increment loop counter\n   d. Advance to next array element (4 bytes per element)\n   e. Loop while nIndex < count\n5. Clear g_nPendingControlHandlerCount to 0\n6. Return\n\nParameters:\nNone (no explicit parameters)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If pending count is 0 or negative, handler clears counter and returns immediately\n- Counter is always reset to 0 before return (prevents double-dispatch)\n- Loop processes elements sequentially from g_aPendingControlHandlers array\n\nGlobals Used:\n- g_nPendingControlHandlerCount (int @0x6fa97c5c): Count of pending handlers to process\n- g_aPendingControlHandlers (uint[256] @0x6fa977a4): Array of handler pointers/IDs\n\nCalled Functions:\n- DispatchInventoryItemHandler (@0x6fa852a8): Processes individual handler\n\nCalling Context:\nCalled during:\n- InitializeBnetConnectionState (@0x6fa71c50): Initial connection setup\n- InitializeCharacterSelectionPanel (@0x6fa74340): Panel initialization\n- FUN_6fa79ef0 (@0x6fa79ef0): Unknown context\n- FUN_6fa83a50 (@0x6fa83a50): Unknown context\n\nMemory Model:\n- No stack parameters or local variables\n- Uses ESI as loop counter (preserved across CALL via register allocation)\n- Uses EDI as current handler pointer\n- Operates on global data structures\n- Calling convention: __stdcall (no parameters)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
