      "name": "CleanupAndReinitializeGameState",
      "signature": "undefined CleanupAndReinitializeGameState(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Cleanup and reinitialize game state for new games or scene transitions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load UI object count and iterate through g_apUIObjects array\n2. Dispatch each pending UI object handler via DispatchInventoryItemHandler\n3. Load pending control handler count from g_nControlObjectCount\n4. Iterate through g_apControlObjects and dispatch each via DispatchInventoryItemHandler\n5. Reset all handler counts to 0 (g_dwUIObjectCount, g_nControlObjectCount)\n6. Set baseline configuration via SetGlobalConfig(0)\n7. Check g_fPaletteNeedsReinit flag to determine if palette reinitialization needed\n8. If flag set: build palette paths via wsprintfA using format \"%s\\%s\" with DATA\\GLOBAL prefix\n9. Compare two palette buffers byte-by-byte for equality using ANSI string comparison\n10. Store comparison result as boolean (1=equal, 0=different) in g_apControlObjects[0x5a]\n11. Initialize palette with constructed paths via InitActPalette()\n12. Clear palette reinit flag g_fPaletteNeedsReinit back to 0\n13. Release all game units and game object resources via ReleaseAllUnits()\n14. Clear unit hash table and cleanup structures via ClearHashTableAndCleanup()\n15. Mark state as cleaned via SetStoredValue(1)\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Palette reinitialization is conditionally triggered by g_fPaletteNeedsReinit flag\n- Uses 2x260-byte stack buffers (szPalettePath1, szPalettePath2) for constructing palette file paths\n- Palette comparison uses 2-byte stride for ANSI string comparison\n- No error handling; assumes all subsystem cleanup succeeds\n\nGlobal State Modified:\n- g_apUIObjects, g_dwUIObjectCount (UI object list cleared)\n- g_apControlObjects, g_nControlObjectCount (handlers cleared)\n- g_apControlObjects[0x5a] = palette equality flag\n- g_fPaletteNeedsReinit (palette reinit flag, set to 1 then 0)\n- g_szActPalettePath1, g_szActPalettePath2 (palette path sources)\n- Unit tracking and hash table state (all units released)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.04b",
