      "name": "TextBoxAddTextMultiline",
      "signature": "undefined4 TextBoxAddTextMultiline(undefined4 param_1, undefined4 param_2, undefined4 param_3, undefined4 param_4)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Adds a multiline Unicode text string to a textbox, splitting by newlines.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 1024-wchar buffer on stack (szTextBuffer)\n2. Initialize buffer with default Unicode constructor (1024 times)\n3. Copy input text to buffer using Unicode::strncpy() (max 1024 chars)\n4. Iterate through buffer character-by-character:\n   - When L'\n' (newline) found: null-terminate, call TextBoxAddText(), continue\n   - Continue until null terminator L'\\0' found\n5. If remaining text after last newline, call TextBoxAddText() on remainder\n6. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  pTextBox (ECX): void* - Pointer to TextBox structure/instance\n  lpszText (EDX): wchar_t* - Input Unicode string to process\n  dwStyle (Stack+4): dword - Style/formatting flags for TextBoxAddText()\n  bFlags (Stack+8): byte - Additional flags for TextBoxAddText()\n\nReturns:\n  EAX: dword = 1 (indicates success)\n\nPurpose:\n  Convenience wrapper around TextBoxAddText() that handles multiline text.\n  Automatically splits input by newlines and adds each line separately,\n  allowing proper formatting/styling of multiline content in a textbox.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Empty string: Returns immediately without calling TextBoxAddText()\n  - Single line (no newlines): Calls TextBoxAddText() once on entire string\n  - Trailing newline: Last empty line is handled, not added to textbox\n  - Text > 1024 chars: Truncated by Unicode::strncpy()\n\nCalled From:\n  ShowCustomErrorDialog, ShowTitleMessageButtonDialog, and other dialog functions\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset  Size  Field              Type        Description\n  -----   ----  -----              ----        -----------\n  -0x800  2048  szTextBuffer[1024] wchar_t[]   Stack buffer for processing",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
