      "name": "IsValidIdentifierCharacter",
      "signature": "bool IsValidIdentifierCharacter(undefined4 param_1, undefined4 param_2, char * param_3)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Validates whether a character is suitable for use in an identifier string.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load first character from input string pointer\n2. Switch on character value to detect reserved special characters\n3. If reserved character found, return false (invalid)\n4. Check if character is less than '!' (0x21) - control char, return false\n5. Check if character is less than DEL (0x7F) - valid ASCII range, return true\n6. Character >= 0x7F, return false (extended ASCII invalid)\n\nParameters:\n- p (void*): Unused context pointer, not examined\n- dw (dword): Unused reserved parameter\n- lpsz (char*): Pointer to string; only first character examined\n\nReturns:\n- byte: Non-zero (true) if character is valid identifier character\n       Zero (false) if character is reserved, control, or extended ASCII\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uninitialized/invalid pointer: Undefined behavior (caller must validate)\n- String length: Only first character examined, remainder irrelevant\n- NULL pointer: Will access invalid memory, undefined behavior\n\nReserved Characters (0x22, 0x23, 0x25, 0x2A, 0x2C, 0x2F, 0x3C, 0x3E, 0x3F, 0x5C):\nQuote, Hash, Percent, Asterisk, Comma, Slash, LessThan, GreaterThan, Question, Backslash",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
