      "name": "ValidateAndDisplayLocalIPAddress",
      "signature": "undefined ValidateAndDisplayLocalIPAddress(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Validates the local IP address against stored value and updates UI display accordingly.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve current local IP address via GetLocalIPAddress()\n2. Clear existing text from display object\n3. Perform byte-by-byte comparison of local IP vs stored IP address\n   - Loop compares characters at even and odd positions\n   - If all chars match and null terminator reached, IPs are equal\n   - SBB-based result code: 0 if match, non-zero if mismatch\n4. Based on comparison result:\n   If IPs match (result == 0):\n     - Load localized string ID 0x1404 (e.g., \"localhost\")\n     - Display localized text in display object\n     - Clear control handler state flags (0x43, 0x51, 0x50)\n   If IPs mismatch (result != 0):\n     - Convert actual IP string to Unicode\n     - Display actual IP in display object\n     - Set control handler state flags (0x43, 0x51, 0x50)\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty IP string treated as null terminator, triggers match condition\n- String comparison is case-sensitive byte comparison\n- Three control handler indices modified: 0x43, 0x51, 0x50\n- Uses g_szLocalHostIPAddress global for comparison baseline\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1404: String ID for localized \"localhost\" or similar text\n- 0x43, 0x51, 0x50: Control handler slot indices\n\nError Handling:\n- No error checking on IP address retrieval\n- Assumes both strings are null-terminated\n- No validation of control handler array bounds\n\nData Flow:\n- Input: System local IP (from GetLocalIPAddress)\n- Global: g_szLocalHostIPAddress, g_pDisplayTextObject, g_aPendingControlHandlers\n- Output: Updated display text and control handler state",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:7ef62ecde168d5bef73bacd0c8307f4f6020e7f20ee5f0505b94136d43e9eb8c",
