      "name": "UpdateControlHandlerBitState",
      "signature": "undefined4 UpdateControlHandlerBitState(int param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Updates the bit state of a control handler based on a flag field in the Control structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract the flag field from pControl at offset 0x0C\n2. If the flag is non-zero, set bit 0x57 in g_aPendingControlHandlers to 1\n3. If the flag is zero, clear bit 0x57 in g_aPendingControlHandlers to 0\n4. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  pControl: Pointer to Control structure (Control *)\n\nReturns:\n  1 on completion (always succeeds)\n\nControl Structure Layout:\n  Offset  Size  Field                Type    Description\n  +0x00   4     (unknown)            dword   Unknown field\n  +0x04   4     (unknown)            dword   Unknown field\n  +0x08   4     (unknown)            dword   Unknown field\n  +0x0C   4     dwFlagField          int     Flag field determining control handler bit state\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Always returns 1 regardless of success/failure\n  - Uses bit index 0x57 (87 decimal) in g_aPendingControlHandlers array\n  - The array g_aPendingControlHandlers is uint[256], accommodating 256*32 = 8192 bit flags\n  - Conditional bit set/clear based on single flag value\n\nRelated Functions:\n  - SetOrClearBitMask: Helper function that performs the actual bit manipulation at 0x6fa85200",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:34559af30fefa8b4cfa3aaee3b39982ec534053b830952813c9142e00285a0ed",
