      "name": "FindUIObjectOfTypeChild",
      "signature": "int FindUIObjectOfTypeChild(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Locates the first UI object child element matching a specific type criteria.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize index counter to 0\n2. Verify UI object array exists (count > -1)\n3. Iterate through UI object array sequentially\n4. For each object, invoke type-check function (func_0x6fa8530e)\n5. Break iteration when type check returns 4 (child type match)\n6. If match found, retrieve text block field count\n7. If count > 0, navigate scrollbar to count-1 position\n8. Return success (1) or trigger fatal error if no match found\n\nParameters: None (uses global UI object array)\n\nReturns:\n  1 = Success, child object located and scrollbar positioned\n  0xFFFFFFFF = Fatal error (no child object found)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Empty UI object array (g_dwUIObjectCount < 0): Fatal error\n  - No object with type = 4: Fatal error\n  - Text block field count = 0: No scrollbar navigation needed\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  4 = Child object type identifier\n  -1 = Array boundary check (indicates empty array)\n\nError Handling:\n  Calls FogAssert and FatalErrorExit if no child object found\n  Error location: s_C__Projects_Diablo2_Source_D2Lau_6fa92aac:0xc19\n\nDependencies:\n  - func_0x6fa8530e: Type checker for UI objects\n  - GetTextBlockField58: Retrieves text block field count\n  - ScrollbarNavigateToIndex: Positions scrollbar\n  - g_pUIObjectArray: Global array of UI object pointers\n  - g_dwUIObjectCount: Number of objects in array",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
