      "name": "ValidateCharacterInputName",
      "signature": "undefined4 ValidateCharacterInputName(undefined4 param_1, int param_2, char * param_3)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Validates that the first character of input is alphabetic.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get first character from input string (szInput)\n2. Check if character is a-z or A-Z (alphabetic)\n3. If alphabetic, return 1 (valid)\n4. If not alphabetic:\n   a. Check if character is '-' or '_' AND bAllowSpecial is true\n   b. If both conditions met, get Unicode string from edit box\n   c. Convert Unicode to UTF-8 buffer\n   d. Scan buffer for '-' or '_' character\n   e. If found, return 1 (valid); else return 0 (invalid)\n5. Return 0 if character is non-alphabetic and not allowed special\n\nParameters:\n- pEditBox (int*): Pointer to edit box widget/control\n- bAllowSpecial (int): Boolean flag (0=disallow special chars, nonzero=allow)\n- szInput (char*): Input string to validate (must be null-terminated)\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Input character is valid (alphabetic or allowed special char)\n- 0: Input character is invalid (non-alphabetic, special char disallowed)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If input string is NULL, behavior is undefined\n- Special character validation only applies if bAllowSpecial is nonzero\n- Unicode string conversion is limited to 32 bytes (0x20)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
