      "name": "ValidateAndSetCharacterNameMask",
      "signature": "undefined ValidateAndSetCharacterNameMask(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Validates a character name string and sets a unit bit mask based on validation result.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve the character name from the edit box control\n2. If name is NULL, set validation flag to 0 (invalid)\n3. Convert name from Unicode to UTF-8 in local buffer (max 32 bytes)\n4. Validate name according to Diablo II naming rules:\n   - Length must be in range [2, 15] (2 <= length < 16)\n   - First character cannot be underscore or hyphen\n   - Last character cannot be underscore\n   - Name must contain valid characters (no leading/trailing special chars)\n5. If validation passes, set fIsValidName = 1, else fIsValidName = 0\n6. Call SetUnitBitMask with the validation result\n\nParameters:\n  None (uses global g_aPendingControlHandlers[0x46] to access edit box)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Null pointer from GetEditBoxChild is handled gracefully (treated as invalid)\n- String length checked before character validation to prevent buffer overrun\n- Underscore at last position is specifically rejected (position nNameLength-1)\n- Validation requires BOTH first and last characters to be valid\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x46: Index into g_aPendingControlHandlers array for character name edit box\n  0x20 (32): Size of local buffer for UTF-8 conversion\n  0x2 (2): Minimum valid name length\n  0x10 (16): Maximum valid name length (exclusive)\n  0x5f: ASCII code for underscore character '_'\n  0x2d: ASCII code for hyphen character '-'\n\nError Handling:\n- NULL pointer check at beginning prevents crash\n- All comparisons use bounds checking before character access\n- Invalid names set mask to 0; valid names set mask to 1\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Stack Frame (relative to ESP at entry):\n  Offset  Size  Field           Description\n  ------  ----  -----           -----------\n  +0x00   4     EBP/Saved       Return address\n  +0x04   4     Saved EBX       \n  +0x08   4     Saved ESI       \n  +0x0C   4     Saved EDI       \n  +0x10   32    szUtfBuffer     UTF-8 converted name (acStack_20)\n\nGlobal Data Referenced:\n  g_aPendingControlHandlers[0x46]: Handle to character name edit box control\n  DAT_6fa97664: Unit structure receiving the bit mask",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
