      "name": "ToggleControlHandlerFlag",
      "signature": "int ToggleControlHandlerFlag(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Toggles a control handler flag at offset 0x1ea.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load address of global control handler array element at index 0x53\n2. Calculate offset to flag field at +0x1ea\n3. Load current flag value (16-bit unsigned)\n4. XOR with bit mask 0x4 to toggle the flag\n5. Store updated value back to same location\n6. Return success code (1)\n\nParameters:\n(none)\n\nReturns:\nint: Success status (1)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Always operates on the same fixed global structure element (index 0x53)\n- Uses XOR with 0x4 mask to toggle bit 2\n- No error conditions\n\nStructure Layout:\ng_aPendingControlHandlers[0x53] is an array of control handler structures.\nOffset 0x1ea contains a 16-bit flag field where bit 2 (value 0x4) controls \na specific aspect of control handling.\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x53: Fixed array index into g_aPendingControlHandlers\n0x1ea: Offset within control handler structure to flag field\n0x4: Bit mask for toggling flag (bit 2 only)\n1: Success return value",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
