      "name": "InitializeTextBoxContent",
      "signature": "undefined4 InitializeTextBoxContent(int param_1)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes text box content based on control index and UI state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if initialization flag (DAT_6fa92a14) is set to -1\n2. If set and control parameter non-zero, proceed with text initialization\n3. Clear both primary and alternate text data lists (indices 0x54, 0x55)\n4. Validate and retrieve string content using string IDs (0xfab, 0x1408)\n5. Add retrieved text to respective text boxes with empty flags/options\n6. Reset initialization flag (DAT_6fa92a10) to 0\n7. Return success (1)\n8. If initialization flag already cleared, return 1 without changes\n\nParameters:\nnControlIndex (int): Control index parameter used in conditional check (compared at offset +0xc)\n\nReturns:\nint: Always returns 1 (success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If DAT_6fa92a14 != -1: Function returns early without modifying text boxes\n- If nControlIndex == 0: Skips text update but clears both text data lists if flag is unset\n- String IDs 0xfab and 0x1408 are hardcoded UI text resource identifiers\n\nGlobal References:\nDAT_6fa92a14: Initialization control flag (compared to -1)\nDAT_6fa92a10: Initialization state flag (cleared after text update)\ng_aPendingControlHandlers[0x54]: Primary text box control reference\ng_aPendingControlHandlers[0x55]: Alternate text box control reference\n\nCalled Functions:\n- ClearTextDataList(): Clears text data from UI control\n- ValidateStringId(): Validates and retrieves string by resource ID\n- TextBoxAddText(): Adds text content to text box control",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
