      "name": "CheckUIStateAndStopLoop",
      "signature": "dword CheckUIStateAndStopLoop(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Checks UI state flags and stops message loop if exit conditions met.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if g_dwUIState is non-zero\n2. If not set, check if g_dwUIExitCode is non-zero  \n3. If either flag is set, call StopMessageLoop() to halt execution\n4. Return 1 (success code)\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\ndword: 1 (always returns success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Dual condition check: Either flag being set triggers loop termination\n- Exit code checking: Secondary check provides alternative exit path\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- Return value 1: Standard success/continue indicator\npfnTickCallback parameter of MessagePumpLoop\n",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
