      "name": "ProcessNetworkClientPacket",
      "signature": "int ProcessNetworkClientPacket(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Receives and processes incoming network packets from the Bnet client connection.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 512-byte buffer on stack for packet data\n2. Call NET_ReceiveClientPacket to receive packet data\n3. On receive error (returns 0xffffffff), check if shutdown flag is set\n4. If packet received successfully:\n   - Extract packet type from first byte\n   - If type is 0xA7 (disconnect request), set shutdown flag and stop message loop\n   - If type is 0xA8 (keep-alive), clear shutdown flag\n5. If no active Bnet login session, return success\n6. Otherwise, stop the message loop\n7. Return success (1)\n\nParameters:\n(none)\n\nReturns:\nint - Always returns 1 (success) to continue message processing\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Packet type 0xA7 triggers immediate connection shutdown\n- Packet type 0xA8 is a keep-alive heartbeat that clears shutdown flag\n- If login state is inactive (g_dwBnetLoginState == 0), function returns early\n- Shutdown flag (g_dwConnectionShutdown) is checked if receive fails\n\nPacket Types:\n0xA7 - Disconnect request from server\n0xA8 - Keep-alive / heartbeat packet\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0xFFFFFFFF - NET_ReceiveClientPacket error return value\n0x200 (512) - Maximum packet buffer size\n0xA7 - Disconnect command packet type\n0xA8 - Keep-alive packet type\n\nError Handling:\nNET_ReceiveClientPacket failures are handled gracefully; function checks shutdown\nstate and returns success to allow continued processing of pending operations.\n\nGlobal State Modified:\ng_dwConnectionShutdown - Set/cleared based on packet type (0xA7/0xA8)\n\nDependencies:\n- NET_ReceiveClientPacket: Receives packet data from Bnet connection\n- StopMessageLoop: Terminates the main message processing loop\n- g_dwBnetLoginState: Indicates if player is logged into Bnet\n- g_dwConnectionShutdown: Tracks if server has requested disconnection\npfnTickCallback parameter of MessagePumpLoop\n",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
