      "name": "ProcessPendingControlHandlersAndInitializeTimer",
      "signature": "uint ProcessPendingControlHandlersAndInitializeTimer(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Processes pending control handlers for inventory items and initializes UI timer system.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Iterate through all pending control handlers (max g_dwGameObjectCount)\n2. Dispatch inventory item handler for each pending handler\n3. Reset pending control handler count to 0\n4. Validate UI object array count does not exceed MAX_CHILDREN\n5. Create new timer object through factory function\n6. Register timer as current timer data context\n7. Add timer to UI object array and increment UI object count\n8. Reset timer data to initial state\n9. Set timer context handler for input processing\n10. Return success (1)\n\nParameters:\nNone (void)\n\nReturns:\nuint - Returns 1 on success\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If g_dwUIObjectCount > 0x3f: Asserts and calls FatalErrorExit\n- Inventory handlers may modify global game state during dispatch\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x3f (63) - MAX_CHILDREN threshold for UI object array size limit\n\nError Handling:\nFatal assertion failure if UI object count exceeds capacity; triggers\nFatalErrorExit with error code 0xffffffff\n\nGlobal Dependencies:\n- g_dwGameObjectCount: Number of pending handlers to process\n- g_aPendingControlHandlers: Array of handler pointers\n- g_pUITimerObject: Factory for timer object creation\n- g_pTimerDataCurrent: Current active timer context\n- g_pUIObjectArray: Array of UI objects\n- g_dwUIObjectCount: Current count of active UI objects",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:155b66a78fbf1a0af2a714c9377e8ace6470d6c8769de0dcf4fcd81674d88bbc",
