      "name": "InitializeSaveGameFile",
      "signature": "int InitializeSaveGameFile(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes save game file by building path, formatting filename, and creating file resource.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x704 (1796) bytes of stack space for buffers\n2. Call BuildSaveGamePath() to construct base save path\n3. Call ValidateAndGetObjectField() to retrieve Unicode string from game object\n4. Convert Unicode string to UTF-8 using Unicode::toUtf() into 0x100-byte buffer\n5. Use sprintf() to format first string: template at 0x6fa5dc70 with utf8 string parameter\n6. Use sprintf() to format second string: template at 0x6fa5dc50 with formatted path and another parameter\n7. Call CreateFileWrapper() with mode 0x3 (READ_WRITE) and flags 0x8000000\n8. Check returned file handle: if handle equals -1 (INVALID_HANDLE), jump to failure path\n9. On success: close file handle with CloseResourceHandle(), set EAX to 1, return\n10. On failure: set EAX to 0 and return\n\nParameters:\nNone (void)\n\nReturns:\nint - Returns 1 if file creation succeeded, 0 if file creation failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\nFile creation failure is indicated by handle value -1 returned from CreateFileWrapper()\nBoth sprintf calls format strings into stack buffers before file operations\nUTF-8 conversion limits string to 0x100 (256) bytes maximum\nStack buffer acStack_604 (260 bytes) accommodates formatted file path plus sentinel",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:b5fd3dc0cfd7bf64c66e811956fc4d904f0411fadf42c43246d6762d6f15bfdf",
