      "name": "ResetGameStateAndCleanup",
      "signature": "undefined ResetGameStateAndCleanup(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Resets the game state and performs complete cleanup/reinitialization. Called during game session transitions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call ProcessSlots() to process active game slots\n2. Iterate through g_pUIObjectArray and dispatch inventory item handlers\n3. Clear g_dwUIObjectCount, g_nPendingControlHandlerCount, and temporary globals\n4. Iterate through g_aPendingControlHandlers and dispatch remaining handlers\n5. Call SetGlobalConfig(0) to reset configuration to defaults\n6. If palette reinitialization flag is set: compare old/new palette paths and reinitialize if different using InitActPalette()\n7. Call ReleaseAllUnits() to deallocate all game unit objects\n8. Call ClearHashTableAndCleanup() to reset hash tables and cleanup structures\n9. Call SetStoredValue(1) to update stored game state\n10. Call InitializeGameState() to reinitialize game state structure\n\nParameters:\nNone (void function using __stdcall calling convention)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function returns with no value",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.04b",
