      "name": "InvokePendingCallback",
      "signature": "int InvokePendingCallback(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Executes a pending callback function if one has been registered.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read the global callback function pointer (g_pfnPendingCallback)\n2. If the pointer is non-null, invoke the callback\n3. Return TRUE (1) indicating completion\n\nParameters:\n  None - This function takes no parameters.\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1 (TRUE) regardless of whether a callback was invoked\n\nGlobal Dependencies:\n  g_pfnPendingCallback (0x6fa977a0) - Function pointer set by various UI\n    initialization routines including dialog handlers, inventory controls,\n    BattleNet login processing, and character creation flows.\n\nNotes:\n  This is a deferred execution mechanism allowing UI components to register\n  callbacks that are invoked at a later point in the processing pipeline.\n  The callback pointer is typically set during dialog/control initialization\n  and cleared or replaced as UI state transitions occur.",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
