      "name": "LoadFrontEndUIImages",
      "signature": "undefined LoadFrontEndUIImages(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Loads all front-end UI control images and stores handles in global array.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 260-byte buffer (MAX_PATH) on stack for image path construction\n2. For each UI image element (56 total at indices 0x9c-0xd3):\n   a. Call wsprintfA to format image path with data directory prefix\n   b. Call LoadCelImage to load image from file  \n   c. Store returned image handle in g_apControlObjects array\n3. Conditionally load expansion-specific (LoD) UI variants:\n   a. Call CheckExpansionMpqExists 6 times to test for Lord of Destruction\n   b. If present, load expansion UI screens (trademark, title, credits, realm, TCP/IP)\n   c. Otherwise use base game UI variants\n\nParameters:\n(none - function uses global state only)\nIMPLICIT g_apControlObjects: uint[256] array for image handles\nIMPLICIT szDATA_GLOBAL_6fa92a7c: Data directory path string \"%sdata\\\\global\\\\\"\n\nReturns:\nvoid - All UI images loaded into g_apControlObjects at indices 0x9c-0xd3\n\nUI Image Index Map:\n0x9c: Blizzard logo (blizno)\n0x9d: Trademark screen (base/expansion variant)\n0x9f: Diablo 2 title\n0xa0-0xa3: D2 logo flames (black/fire left/right)\n0xa4: Title/game select screen (base/expansion)\n0xa5: Cursor (ohand)\n0xa6: Credits background (base/expansion)\n0xa9-0xab: Expansion-only realm/char select (conditional)\n0xac-0xb4: Various buttons and listbox\n0xb6-0xbc: Menu backgrounds, difficulty, char select\n0xbd-0xc6: Popup dialogs (OK, Cancel variants)\n0xc7-0xc9: More buttons\n0xba: Cinematics select (expansion-only)\n0xbf: Character arrow\n0xc0-0xc1: Realm select (base/expansion variant)\n0xca: Password dialog\n0xce-0xcf: Realm background, scrollbar\n0xd0: TCP/IP screen (base/expansion variant)\n0xd1-0xd3: IP box, download patch UI\n\nError Handling:\nNo error checking. Assumes all LoadCelImage calls succeed.",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.09d",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:5985abcb8c3ae3f2b5beafac9a9e0a42",
