      "name": "FlushStream",
      "signature": "int FlushStream(int * pStream)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Flushes buffered data from a FILE stream to disk.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If pStream is NULL, flush all open streams via FlushAllStreams(0)\n2. Otherwise, acquire stream lock via FUN_6fdd6f0e (critical section)\n3. Call FlushStreamInternal to perform actual flush operation\n4. Release stream lock via FUN_6fdd6f60\n5. Return result from flush operation\n\nParameters:\n- pStream (int*): FILE stream pointer to flush, or NULL to flush all streams\n\nReturns:\n- 0 on success\n- -1 on failure (error during flush or stream validation failure)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
