      "name": "OpenHandleAsStream",
      "signature": "uint OpenHandleAsStream(HANDLE param_1, uint param_2)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Opens a Windows file handle and associates it with a stream ID.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Build stream flags from open flags:\n     - If dwOpenFlags & 0x8 (O_APPEND): set flag 0x20\n     - If dwOpenFlags & 0x4000 (O_TEXT): set flag 0x80\n     - If dwOpenFlags & 0x80 (O_NOINHERIT): set flag 0x10\n  2. Call GetFileType(hFile) to determine handle type\n  3. If GetFileType returns 0 (FILE_TYPE_UNKNOWN):\n     - Call GetLastError and translate to errno\n     - Return 0xffffffff (failure)\n  4. Adjust stream flags based on file type:\n     - FILE_TYPE_CHAR (2): set flag 0x40 (character device)\n     - FILE_TYPE_PIPE (3): set flag 0x8 (pipe)\n  5. Allocate stream buffer entry via AllocateStreamBuffer\n  6. If allocation fails, set errno=0x18 (EMFILE), return 0xffffffff\n  7. Associate handle with stream via SetStreamHandle\n  8. Store stream flags at offset 0x4 in stream entry (OR with 0x1 for in-use)\n  9. Unlock stream and return stream ID\n\nParameters:\n  hFile      - Windows file HANDLE to associate with stream\n  dwOpenFlags - Open mode flags (O_APPEND=0x8, O_TEXT=0x4000, O_NOINHERIT=0x80)\n\nReturns:\n  Stream ID (dword) on success\n  0xffffffff on failure (errno set appropriately)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - FILE_TYPE_UNKNOWN (0) with GetLastError succeeding is an error\n  - Stream entry flags stored at (table_base + (id & 0x1f) * 0x24 + 4)\n  - Flag 0x1 always set to mark stream as allocated/in-use\n\nStream Flag Bits:\n  Offset  | Mask | Meaning\n  --------|------|---------------------------\n  +0x4    | 0x01 | Stream in use (always set)\n  +0x4    | 0x08 | Pipe device\n  +0x4    | 0x10 | No inherit flag\n  +0x4    | 0x20 | Append mode\n  +0x4    | 0x40 | Character device\n  +0x4    | 0x80 | Text mode",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
