      "name": "SetFileLength",
      "signature": "int SetFileLength(uint dwFileDesc, int nTargetSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Extends or truncates a file to the specified target size.\n\nSaves the current file position, calculates difference between\ntarget size and current file end, then either writes zeros to\nextend or calls SetEndOfFile to truncate.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save current file position via SeekFile(SEEK_CUR)\n2. Get file size via SeekFile(SEEK_END)\n3. Calculate difference between target and current size\n4. If target > current: write zero-filled 4KB blocks to extend\n5. If target < current: call SetEndOfFile to truncate\n6. Restore original file position\n\nParameters:\n- dwFileDesc (uint): CRT file descriptor handle\n- nTargetSize (int): Desired file size in bytes\n\nReturns:\n- 0 on success\n- -1 on failure (sets errno to EACCES on permission error)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1000 (4096): Block size for zero-fill writes\n- 0x8000: File mode flag passed to FUN_6fdddc9f\n- 0xD (13): EACCES errno value\n- 5: ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED DOS error code",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.00",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:bc349e1b971a9cf4391176eb6f2713f26688a98aab765bb25d4bb92c86320ea4",
