      "name": "InitializeUIObjects",
      "signature": "int InitializeUIObjects(void)",
      "calling_convention": "unknown",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes the UI object array by creating three UI objects and adding them to the global UI object collection.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call initialization helper FUN_6fa85070\n2. For each of 3 UI object types (DAT_6fa92530, DAT_6fa92560, DAT_6fa92590):\n   a. Check if UI object count exceeds limit (0x3F / 63)\n   b. If exceeded, trigger assertion failure and fatal error\n   c. Create UI object using CreateObjectByTypeFactory with type descriptor\n   d. Store object pointer in g_pUIObjectArray at current count index\n   e. Increment global object count\n3. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n(none)\n\nReturns:\n1 - Success\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Assertion triggered if g_dwUIObjectCount exceeds 63 elements\n- Fatal error halts execution on count overflow\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3F (63): Maximum UI object count threshold\n- 0x60D (1549): Assertion line number in source\n\nError Handling:\nExceeding UI object limit triggers FogAssert followed by FatalErrorExit with code 0xFFFFFFFF\n\nGlobal Variables:\n- g_pUIObjectArray: Dynamically allocated array storing UI object pointers\n- g_dwUIObjectCount: Current count of UI objects in array\n- DAT_6fa92530, DAT_6fa92560, DAT_6fa92590: UI object type descriptors",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
