      "comment": "Initiates a connection to Battle.net servers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Verify Bnclient interface is initialized (g_pBnclientInterface != NULL)\n  2. Assert not already connecting (g_bConnectingToBnet == 0)\n  3. Set connecting flag and reset connection attempt counter\n  4. Reset connection status and output debug string\n  5. Initialize Storm network layer (Ordinal_10001 = SNetInitialize)\n  6. Call Bnclient->Connect (vtable offset 0x10)\n  7. If connect call succeeds:\n     a. Clear logged in flag (g_bBnetLoggedIn = 0)\n     b. Initialize connection state and pump messages\n     c. Check for user cancellation (g_dwGameStateFlags)\n     d. Check connection status via Bnclient->GetStatus (vtable offset 0x4c)\n     e. If status != 0x65 (101 = connected), prepare login and retry\n     f. On success, call Bnclient->GetLoginInfo (vtable offset 0x28)\n  8. Clean up connecting flag and return result\n\nParameters:\n  None - uses global state (g_pBnclientInterface)\n\nReturns:\n  TRUE (1) - Connection established successfully\n  FALSE (0) - Connection failed or interface not initialized\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Returns FALSE immediately if g_pBnclientInterface is NULL\n  - Triggers FogAssert if already connecting (re-entrant call)\n  - Status code 0x65 (101) indicates successful connection\n  - User can cancel via g_dwGameStateFlags during message pump\n\nBnclient Interface Vtable Offsets:\n  Offset | Method\n  0x10   | Connect / Disconnect\n  0x28   | GetLoginInfo\n  0x48   | GetLoginResult\n  0x4c   | GetConnectionStatus\n  0x74   | IsLoggedIn",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
