      "name": "InsertOrUpdateHashTableEntry",
      "signature": "undefined InsertOrUpdateHashTableEntry(undefined4 param_1, undefined4 * param_2, uint param_3)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Inserts or updates an entry in a hash table with automatic expiration.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compute hash of the input key string using ComputeStringHash()\n2. Search hash table (g_pHashTableHead) for existing entry with matching hash\n3. If not found:\n   - Allocate 16-byte node (hash, data pointer, expiration, next link)\n   - Allocate buffer for data payload\n   - Copy data using DWORD loops (size >> 2) then byte loops (size & 3)\n   - Set expiration to GetTickCount() + 300000 (5 minutes)\n   - Insert new node at head of g_pHashTableHead list\n4. If found (hash collision with existing key):\n   - Free existing data with SMemFree()\n   - Allocate new data buffer\n   - Copy new data using same loop pattern\n   - Update expiration timeout\n   - Return without changing link structure\n\nParameters:\n- lpszKey (ECX): Null-terminated string key to hash and look up\n- pbData (EDX): Pointer to data buffer to insert/update (not copied into structure, only the data bytes)\n- nDataSize (Stack[0x4]): Size in bytes of data buffer to allocate and copy\n\nReturns:\n- void: Function modifies g_pHashTableHead global directly; no return value\n\nHash Table Structure (16-byte node):\n- Offset 0x0: dwHash (4 bytes) - Hash value of key string\n- Offset 0x4: pDataBuffer (4 bytes) - Pointer to allocated data\n- Offset 0x8: dwExpireTime (4 bytes) - Absolute time (GetTickCount + 300000) when entry expires\n- Offset 0xc: pNextNode (4 bytes) - Pointer to next node in collision chain\n\nMemory Model:\n- g_pHashTableHead (0x6fa97630): Global pointer always points to most recent insertion\n- New entries always inserted at head (LIFO order)\n- Hash collisions handled via linked list traversal (field +0xc)\n- Entry data allocated separately from node structure\n- All allocations via SMemAlloc with memory tracking\n- Expiration timeout is absolute millisecond value (not relative duration)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.09d",
      "method": "NOP",
