      "name": "ProcessPlayerSelection",
      "signature": "void ProcessPlayerSelection(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Processes player selection and manages player unit allocation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load player selection count from global g_dwPlayerSelectCount\n2. Return error (-1) if no players selected\n3. Iterate through player slots, finding valid player data\n4. Skip invalid or empty slots (index check)\n5. Validate player data structure and unit pointers\n6. Call external ordinal function (likely D2Client ordinal) to process unit\n7. Continue iteration until all slots processed\n8. Return success (1) on completion\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nEAX: 1 = Success, -1 = No players selected\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Handles case where player selection count is -1 (invalid)\n- Skips empty player slots during iteration\n- May have early exit on first valid player\n\nReferences:\n- g_dwPlayerSelectCount: Global player count or index variable\n- External ordinal call (D2Client): Unknown unit processing function\n- Stack-allocated buffer of 128 bytes (0x80) for player data\n\nAssembly Notes:\n- Uses ECX for player count/index\n- Uses ESI for player data pointer iteration\n- Stack frame: 128 bytes (0x80) of local storage\n- Parameter size: 4 bytes (indicated by RET 04)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
