      "name": "HandleGatewaySelectionAndRealm",
      "signature": "int HandleGatewaySelectionAndRealm(MSG * pEventMsg)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Handles gateway selection and realm configuration when minimal mouse input is detected.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve current tick count and calculate elapsed time since last call\n2. Get current cursor position and calculate delta movement (X, Y)\n3. Update stored cursor position and timestamp\n4. If mouse movement is minimal (<5 pixels) AND elapsed time <301ms AND event is WM_LBUTTONDOWN (0x201):\n   a. Get current gateway selection from UI text box field\n   b. If gateway value is not 0xffffffff (unset):\n      - Set current gateway via BNGatewayAccess\n      - Retrieve realm name for selected gateway\n      - Save realm preference to registry (HKLM\\Software\\Blizzard\\Diablo II\\Preferred Realm)\n   c. Dispatch and clear all UI object handlers (inventory items)\n   d. Dispatch and clear all game object handlers\n   e. Reset UI and game object counts\n   f. Set global configuration to 0\n   g. If palette reinit flag is set:\n      - Compare old vs new palette file data byte-by-byte\n      - Initialize act palette if different\n      - Clear palette reinit flag\n   h. Release all game units and cleanup hash tables\n   i. Initialize game menus\n\nParameters:\n- pEventMsg (MSG *): Pointer to Windows MSG structure with message type at offset +4\n\nReturns:\n- int: Always returns 1 (success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Mouse movement calculation uses signed difference arithmetic to handle negative values\n- Palette comparison uses byte-by-byte comparison with early exit on first difference\n- Realm preference saved via registry to HKEY_CLASSES_ROOT\n- Function operates as both mouse movement detector and gateway selection handler\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x201: Windows WM_LBUTTONDOWN message constant\n- 5: Minimum pixel motion threshold for input detection\n- 0x12d (301): Maximum elapsed time in milliseconds before timeout\n- 0x4f: Array index for gateway selection UI field\n- 0x5a: Array offset for palette comparison result flag\n\nError Conditions:\n- Invalid or unset gateway (0xffffffff) skips gateway selection\n- Palette reinit flag only processes if set (indicates palette data change)\n- No explicit error returns; always succeeds with return value 1\n\nDependencies:\n- BNGatewayAccess::SetCurGateway(int gwIdx): Sets active gateway\n- BNGatewayAccess::Realm(int gwIdx): Returns realm name string\n- GetTickCount(): Windows API for timer\n- GetCursorPos(POINT*): Windows API for cursor position\n- SetRegistryStringValue(): Custom registry write function\n- DispatchInventoryItemHandler(uint*): Sends UI object messages\n- ReleaseAllUnits(): Game object cleanup\n- ClearHashTableAndCleanup(): Hash table deallocation\n- SetStoredValue(int): Global state update\n- InitializeGameMenus(): Menu system initialization\n\nGlobal State Modified:\n- g_dwLastInputTickCount: Caches current tick for delta calculation\n- g_dwLastCursorX: Caches cursor X for motion detection\n- g_dwLastCursorY: Caches cursor Y for motion detection\n- g_aPendingControlHandlers: UI/game object array (dispatched and cleared)\n- g_dwUIObjectCount: UI object counter (reset to 0)\n- g_dwGameObjectCount: Game object counter (reset to 0)\n- g_bPaletteReinitFlag: Palette reinit flag (cleared after processing)\n- Registry entry: Software\\Blizzard\\Diablo II\\Preferred Realm",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:1813a2f6661307f9aa5c82d2330c244328e9d6387447bbb3c285c0fd6c503407",
