      "name": "InitializeButtonText",
      "signature": "void InitializeButtonText(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes the gateway button text with the current Battle.net gateway name.\n\nRetrieves the gateway name from the BN client interface, converts it to Unicode,\nformats it with a localized string resource template, converts to uppercase,\nand sets it as button control #10's display text.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call BN client interface method +0xa4 to get gateway accessor\n2. Get gateway name via BNGatewayAccess::Name()\n3. Copy gateway name to local ANSI buffer (256 chars max)\n4. Initialize three Unicode buffers (256 wchar_t each) via constructor loops\n5. Convert ANSI gateway name to Unicode via toUnicode()\n6. Load localized format string from resource ID 0x2a5e (10846)\n7. Format final text: sprintf(output, resourceFormat, unicodeGatewayName)\n8. Convert each character to uppercase using locale-aware lookup table\n9. Call InitButtonControl(pControl, 10, pwUppercaseText, 0)\n\nParameters:\n  None (uses global BN client interface at 0x6fa96c64)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Characters >= 0x100 bypass uppercase conversion (non-ASCII passthrough)\n  - Empty gateway name produces empty button text\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0xa4      - Offset to gateway accessor method in BN client vtable\n  0x100     - Buffer size in wchar_t (256 Unicode characters)\n  0x2a5e    - String resource ID for button format template\n  0x0a      - Button control ID (10 decimal)\n  0x6fa96c64 - Global pointer to BN client interface\n  0x6fa978b8 - Global pointer to button control structure\n\nCalled By:\n  InitializeGameMenus, InitializeNetworkInterfaceUI",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
