      "name": "ProcessBnetLoginAndGameInitialization",
      "signature": "uint ProcessBnetLoginAndGameInitialization(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Processes Battle.net login and game initialization sequence.\n\nThis function orchestrates the complete login and game initialization workflow:\n1. Retrieves edit box content (server connection string)\n2. Parses connection parameters using ScanStringWithFormat\n3. Resolves hostname to IP address if needed\n4. Clears inventory slots via DispatchInventoryItemHandler\n5. Creates game objects via CreateObjectByTypeFactory (type 0xD7/0xF0)\n6. Sets unit flags and initializes game state\n7. Starts message pump loop for network initialization\n8. Handles palette file loading for act transitions\n9. Performs final game state cleanup and initialization\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Fetch edit box text containing server connection string\n  2. Early exit if connection string is empty (0x6fa80660)\n  3. Parse connection string format: host:port,param1,param2,param3\n  4. If parse fails (!=4 args), attempt hostname resolution\n  5. Copy resolved IP to global game config buffer\n  6. Process all inventory slots in cleanup loop\n  7. Branch based on g_dwGameMode flag (0x6fa9790c):\n     - Mode set: Create type 0xF0,0xF3,0xF2 objects\n     - Mode clear: Create type 0xD7,0xD8,0xD9 objects\n  8. Call SetUnitFlags for each created object\n  9. Initialize UI via ValidateStringId (0x147B)\n  10. Execute MessagePumpLoop with tick callbacks\n  11. Initialize D2Net client with parsed connection info\n  12. On failure: cleanup and display error dialog (0x145B)\n  13. On success: Initialize game state, process palettes\n  14. Set stored value and complete initialization\n\nParameters:\n  None - This is a void function with no explicit parameters\n\nReturns:\n  uint - Always returns 1 (TRUE) indicating completion\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x147B - String ID for main game UI initialization\n  0x145B - String ID for connection error dialog\n  0xD7,0xD8,0xD9 - Object type IDs for standard mode\n  0xF0,0xF2,0xF3 - Object type IDs for alternate mode\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Empty connection string causes immediate exit\n  - Failed hostname resolution triggers error dialog path\n  - g_dwGameMode determines object creation type set",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
