      "comment": "Initializes the CD Key error dialog and validates user input fields.\n\nThis function sets up a dialog for CD key-related error handling. It retrieves text from\nedit box controls, validates string lengths, and configures UI controls for error display.\nThe function handles reconnection logic when CD key validation fails.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if error code is valid (non-zero), otherwise call error handler and return\n2. Retrieve edit box children for account name, password, and confirm fields\n3. Copy text from edit boxes to control buffers using unicode2Win\n4. Validate account name length (must be 2-15 characters)\n5. If length invalid, validate string ID 0x1460 or 0x1461 based on range\n6. Validate password fields via strcmp - if mismatch, validate string ID 0x1462\n7. Validate password length (must be 2-20 characters) - if invalid, use 0x1463/0x1464\n8. Create sub-controls for various dialog elements (IDs 0x4C, 0x62, 0x63, 0x5E, 0x5F, 0x60, 0x61)\n9. Configure text boxes with localized strings (IDs 0x146B-0x146E)\n10. Set active fonts and compute division for text box positioning\n11. Set unit flags and last inventory items for dialog state\n12. Store callback function pointer at g_pDialogCallback (0x6fa977a0)\n\nParameters:\nnErrorCode - Error code from CD key validation (0 = invalid, triggers error handler)\n\nReturns:\n1 - Always returns 1 (success) after initialization\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x100 - Buffer size for unicode conversion\n0x88, 0xA0 - Offsets into control structure for text buffers\n0x1460-0x1464 - String IDs for validation error messages\n0x146B-0x146E - String IDs for dialog text labels\n0x4C, 0x5E-0x63 - Control IDs for sub-controls\n0xD7, 0xDA, 0xD9 - Alternate control IDs for non-flagged path\n0xF0, 0xF1, 0xF2 - Control IDs for flagged path\n\nError Handling:\n- If nErrorCode is 0, HandleCdKeyErrorReconnect is called immediately\n- Invalid string lengths trigger specific error string display via ValidateStringId",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
