      "name": "ValidateBNetLoginCredentials",
      "signature": "int ValidateBNetLoginCredentials(int nInitializationFlag)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Validates Battle.net login credentials and initializes game state upon successful authentication.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if nInitializationFlag is zero - if so, call HandleCdKeyErrorReconnect and return 1\n2. Extract username (control 0x4e), account (0x44), password confirm (g_pPasswordConfirmEditBox), password (0x4d) from edit boxes\n3. Convert all Unicode strings to Windows ANSI encoding using unicode2Win (256 byte buffers)\n4. Validate username length: minimum 2 chars (error 0x1460), maximum 16 chars (error 0x1461)\n5. Compare password confirmation with password field (error 0x1462 if mismatch)\n6. Validate password length: minimum 2 chars (error 0x1463), maximum 21 chars (0x15) (error 0x1464)\n7. Clear pending control handler state flag g_apControlObjects[0x9b]\n8. Call PerformBnetLogin with account structure and flags (0, 1)\n9. On login failure, check if g_apControlObjects[0x9b] was set - if so reinit UI and return\n10. On login success: store account name to registry under \"Last BNet\" key\n11. Dispatch inventory handlers for all control objects and UI objects (3 cleanup loops)\n12. Reset control/UI object counts and state flags to zero\n13. Call SetGlobalConfig(0), ReleaseAllUnits, ClearHashTableAndCleanup, SetStoredValue(1), InitializeGameState\n14. If palette needs reinit (g_fPaletteNeedsReinit), format paths and call InitActPalette\n15. On validation failure, show error dialog and create appropriate sub-controls based on g_apControlObjects[0x5a]\n\nParameters:\n    nInitializationFlag - Initialization state flag; 0 triggers CD key error handler path\n\nReturns:\n    int - Always returns 1 (success or error handled, allows caller to continue)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n    - CD key error path: nInitializationFlag==0 calls HandleCdKeyErrorReconnect\n    - Login cancelled: g_apControlObjects[0x9b] set during login triggers UI reinit without state cleanup\n    - Palette reinit: Compares path strings byte-by-byte to determine if palette reload needed\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n    0x4e - Username edit box control index\n    0x44 - Account edit box control index  \n    0x4d - Password edit box control index\n    0x53 - Account structure base index\n    0x5a - UI mode flag (0=normal controls, 1=alternate controls)\n    0x9b - Pending control handler state flag\n    0x88 - Username offset within account structure\n    0xa0 - Password offset within account structure\n    0x100 - String buffer size (256 bytes)\n    0x1460-0x1464 - Error string IDs for validation failures\n    0xd7/0xda/0xd9 - Normal sub-control type indices\n    0xf0/0xf1/0xf2 - Alternate sub-control type indices\n\nError Handling:\n    String ID 0x1460: Username too short (less than 2 chars)\n    String ID 0x1461: Username too long (more than 16 chars)\n    String ID 0x1462: Password confirmation mismatch\n    String ID 0x1463: Password too short (less than 2 chars)\n    String ID 0x1464: Password too long (more than 21 chars)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:78f22960aa8eb70a4e317386905e8f6bd0c3147ffaa3c30be1634fe8815f1ed0",
