      "name": "CheckGameResourceInitialization",
      "signature": "undefined4 CheckGameResourceInitialization(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Validates game resource initialization status during BattleNet login.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load and check BattleNet login state (g_dwBnetLoginState)\n2. If login active: set initialized flag, stop loop, return success\n3. If resources not init: query init status via Ordinal_10055()\n   (Ordinal_10055 = GetResourceHandle - returns handle or 0 if not ready)\n4. If status success: create wait handle, poll for availability (0ms timeout)\n5. Check wait result for success (0) or timeout (0x102) condition\n6. Stop message loop and return success\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nint: 1 (always returns success for loop continuation)\n\nNotes:\n- Non-blocking resource check (timeout=0)\n- BattleNet login takes precedence\n- WaitForSingleObject: 0=ready, 0x102=timeout\n- DVar1 is assembly-only temporary (EAX register reuse)\npfnTickCallback parameter of MessagePumpLoop\n",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.04b",
