      "name": "ProcessGameInitialization",
      "signature": "int ProcessGameInitialization(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initialize game state after character selection.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Attempt BNet login with current account (g_aPendingControlHandlers[0x53])\n2. If login fails and error flag set (g_aPendingControlHandlers[0x9b]), handle CD key error and reconnect\n3. If login succeeds:\n   a. Store BNet account name in registry (HKEY_CURRENT_USER\\Software\\Blizzard Entertainment\\Diablo II\\Last BNet)\n   b. Get save directory path for character slot data\n   c. Build save file path pattern (s__d2s)\n   d. Check if save files exist via FindFirstFileA\n   e. If found, process saved character slots\n   f. Dispatch inventory item handlers for UI objects (count: g_dwUIObjectCount)\n   g. Dispatch inventory item handlers for game objects (count: g_dwGameObjectCount)\n   h. Clear object counters and UI state\n   i. Set global config (param 0)\n   j. Handle palette reinitialization if flag set:\n      - Build palette path strings using wsprintf\n      - Compare old vs new palette paths\n      - Update ActPalette if paths differ\n      - Clear reinitialization flag\n   k. Release all game units and cleanup hash tables\n   l. Store completion state and initialize game engine\n4. If save files not found or load skipped, initialize character select screen\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nint - Always returns 1 (success status)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- CD key error handling: Triggers reconnection workflow\n- Palette path comparison: Character-by-character string comparison for reinitialization decision\n- Multiple object handler dispatches: Iterates through UI and game object arrays\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x9b: Control handler error flag offset\n- 0x53: Control handler account info offset\n- 0x5a: Control handler palette reinit flag offset\n- 0x88: Offset into account struct for account name\n- 0x400 (1024): Save directory path buffer size\n- 260: Maximum filename length for FindFirstFileA\n\nError Handling:\n- Failed BNet login causes character select screen reinitialization\n- FindFirstFileA failure (no save files) initiates fresh game setup\n- Registry operations may silently fail (non-critical path)\n\nMemory Model:\n- Local stack buffers: 2560+ bytes total for find data and path strings\n- Global arrays modified: g_aPendingControlHandlers, g_pPaletteDatPath\n- Allocations managed by called functions (ProcessSlots, ReleaseAllUnits)\n- No caller-owned memory passed as parameters",
