      "name": "InitializeStringHashCache",
      "signature": "undefined InitializeStringHashCache(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes the string hash cache with precomputed hashes for common game strings.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compute hash of the \"Header\" configuration string using ComputeStringHash\n2. Store computed hash value in global g_dwHeaderStringHash for cache lookup\n3. Compute hash of the \"Game_Time\" game state string using ComputeStringHash\n4. Store computed hash value in global g_dwGameTimeStringHash for cache lookup\n5. Return to caller after both hashes are cached\n\nParameters: (void)\nNo parameters - initialization function called during game startup\n\nReturns: void\nNo return value; function performs initialization side effects only\n\nPurpose:\nPre-computes string hashes for frequently used game configuration and state strings\nto improve performance during runtime string lookups and comparisons. This caching\nmechanism avoids repeatedly hashing the same strings during game execution.\n\nGlobals Modified:\n  g_dwHeaderStringHash    - Hash of \"Header\" configuration string\n  g_dwGameTimeStringHash  - Hash of \"Game_Time\" game state string\n\nDependencies: ComputeStringHash function for hash computation\nCalled By: Initialization sequence (likely game startup)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.04b",
      "method": "STR",
