      "name": "InitializeBnetConnectionState",
      "signature": "undefined InitializeBnetConnectionState(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes Battle.net connection state on successful login.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Record current tick count as connection initialization timestamp\n2. Call FUN_6fa76560 (pre-initialization handler)\n3. Call FUN_6fa76350 (initialization callback with flag=1)\n4. Retrieve and configure three inventory slots (0xdb, 0xdc, 0xdd):\n   - Get unit from table via FUN_6fa76510\n   - Set last inventory item (only for first slot 0xdb)\n   - Set unit flags to 1 for all three slots\n5. Retrieve fourth inventory slot (0xdd) and add text to TextBox:\n   - Validate string ID 0x1433\n   - Call TextBoxAddText with retrieved unit and validated string\n6. Configure two additional unit slots (0xde, 0xdf):\n   - Retrieve units from table\n   - Store in globals g_pUnitSlotDE and g_pUnitSlotDF\n   - Set unit flags to 1 for both\n7. Initialize connection tracking globals:\n   - Set g_dwSelectedUnitId to 0xffffffff (no selection)\n   - Set g_dwConnectionState to 0 (idle)\n8. Register disconnect handler callback at address LAB_6fa710e0\n9. Tail call to FUN_6fa71d20 (post-initialization handler)\n\nParameters:\nNone. Operates on global connection context.\n\nReturns:\nvoid. Modifies global connection state as side effect.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- TextBoxAddText receives uninitialized output from ValidateStringId (common pattern for text validation/localization)\n- Unit slots 0xdb-0xdf correspond to specific game entity types accessed from global table\n- Function does not validate return values from FUN_6fa76510 - assumes all slots exist\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0xdb, 0xdc, 0xdd, 0xde, 0xdf: Unit slot indices for connection state UI\n- 0x1433: String ID for connection-related text (game strings table)\n- 0xffffffff: Invalid/uninitialized unit ID sentinel\n- Flag value 1: Unit active/visible flag for connection UI slots\n\nError Handling:\nNo explicit error handling. Assumes all calls succeed. If any FUN_6fa76510 call returns null, subsequent SetUnitFlags calls will fail. Consider defensive checks before calling TextBoxAddText.\n\nGlobals Modified:\n- g_dwConnectionInitTime: Set to GetTickCount() result (connection start time)\n- g_pUnitSlotDE, g_pUnitSlotDF: Set to unit pointers from table\n- g_dwSelectedUnitId: Set to 0xffffffff\n- g_dwConnectionState: Set to 0",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.09d",
