      "comment": "Handles realm selection and character loading during connection initialization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if game state is GAME_STATE_RUNNING (value 1)\n   - Return 1 (success) if not in correct state\n2. Call FUN_6fa7b690() to perform realm initialization\n3. Call FUN_6fa7b650() to get realm count\n   - If returns -1: disconnect and show error 0x14e3\n   - If returns 0: disconnect and show error 0x14aa\n4. For return value > 0:\n   - Allocate and initialize timer data structure (ordinal 0x79)\n   - Configure timer context handler\n   - Allocate additional data structures (ordinals 0x93, 0x94, 0x68, 0x6a, 0x6b, 0x69)\n   - Add intro text to text box (string 0x2a67)\n5. Retrieve preferred realm from registry:\n   - Read \"Preferred Realm\" value from registry\n   - If found, search character list for matching realm\n   - Return 1 if found\n6. Query current realm from BnetClient interface:\n   - Call GetUnitX() to get realm gateway access\n   - Copy realm name to g_tCharacterHashTable\n   - Save realm to registry\n7. Search for matching character in list\n   - Loop through character count from FUN_6fa7b650()\n   - Compare each character name using SStrCmpNI\n   - Return 1 if found\n8. Select first available character:\n   - If character list non-empty: select character at index 0\n   - If character list empty: use NULL pointer\n   - Copy selection to registry storage\n   - Save to registry \"Preferred Realm\"\n\nParameters:\n   None\n\nReturns:\n   int: 0 = Connection failure (error dialog shown), 1 = Success (realm/character selected)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n   - Early disconnection if game state incorrect\n   - Dual character search: first by preferred realm, then by realm gateway\n   - Graceful fallback to NULL character if list empty\n   \nMagic Numbers:\n   0x79 = Ordinal for main timer data structure\n   0x93, 0x94, 0x68, 0x6a, 0x6b, 0x69 = Resource ordinals for UI components\n   0x2a67 = String ID for intro text\n   0x14aa = String ID for connection error (generic)\n   0x14e3 = String ID for connection error (GetRealms failed)\n   0x7fffffff = Max string length (effectively unlimited)\n\nError Handling:\n   - FUN_6fa7b650() returning -1 triggers \"Connection failed\" dialog\n   - FUN_6fa7b650() returning 0 triggers \"No realms available\" dialog\n   - Registry failures silently continue (defensive programming)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
