      "name": "InitializeGameplayScreen",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameplayScreen(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes the gameplay screen UI and loads character save data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call initialization routines for game state and sky palette\n2. Clear all gameplay state globals (unit counts, character slots)\n3. Create UI objects for character selection (types 0xa0-0xa6, 0x9b)\n4. Configure scrollbar and button controls with string IDs\n5. Loop through expansion character slots (0x83-0x8a range)\n6. Check expansion MPQ exists; create expansion UI elements if present\n7. Call HandleRealmSelectionAndCharacterLoad for connection setup\n8. Based on game state (singleplayer=1, multiplayer=0/2/3):\n   - Release existing unit list and free composite units\n   - Compute name hash and search for matching character\n   - Show appropriate error dialog if character not found\n9. For non-singleplayer: scan save directory for .d2s files\n   - Validate filename length (2-16 chars) and format\n   - Create player game unit for each valid save file\n10. Update UI state and expansion display\n11. Adjust scrollbar position based on player count\n12. Initialize music track if music enabled\n\nParameters:\n  None (void function)\n\nReturns:\n  void - All state changes applied to globals\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If HandleRealmSelectionAndCharacterLoad fails, exits early\n  - If expansion MPQ missing, shows error dialog with appropriate message\n  - Filenames starting with underscore or ending with dash are skipped\n  - Character name must be 2-16 characters\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n  0xa0-0xa6, 0x9b, 0x95: UI object type IDs for character select screen\n  0x5524, 0x58ca: String table IDs for scrollbar labels\n  0x1419, 0x141a, 0x141b: Error message string IDs\n  0x489: Memory allocation size for unit data\n  0x29c: Memory allocation size for secondary unit\n  0x1b8, 0x1c8: Offsets in composite unit structure (unit ptr, next ptr)\n  0x1b4: Offset for unit validity flag\n\nStructure Layout (Composite Unit at ESI):\n  Offset  Size  Field              Description\n  0x1b4   4     dwValidityFlag     Non-zero if unit is valid\n  0x1b8   4     pUnitData          Pointer to unit data structure\n  0x1c8   4     pNextUnit          Pointer to next unit in list\n\nGlobals Modified:\n  0x6fa9760c: dwCurrentUnitCount\n  0x6fa97610: dwTotalUnitCount\n  0x6fa97604: pUnitListHead\n  0x6fa97608: pSecondaryUnitNode\n  0x6fa975f8: dwRealmConnectionState\n  0x6fa97628: dwValidPlayerCount\n\nPhantom Variables (assembly-only, cannot be renamed):\n  extraout_var, extraout_var_00: High bytes of partial register assignments (AL->EAX)\n  abSearchPathBuffer: Stack buffer at [-0x900] for FindFirstFile path construction",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
