      "name": "ShowTitleMessageButtonDialog",
      "signature": "undefined ShowTitleMessageButtonDialog(Unicode * param_1, undefined4 param_2, undefined4 param_3)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Displays a modal dialog with title message and configurable buttons for disconnect handling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Dispatch pending inventory item handlers (loop through g_adwHandlerSlots)\n2. Create title dialog panel via CreateObjectByTypeFactory(g_TitleDialogPanelConfig)\n3. Register panel in handler slot array and set unit flags\n4. Create message textbox via CreateObjectByTypeFactory(g_MessageTextboxConfig)\n5. Create button textbox via CreateObjectByTypeFactory(g_ButtonTextboxConfig)\n6. Initialize 1024-element wchar_t buffer via Unicode default constructor loop\n7. Copy pszMessage to buffer via Unicode::strncpy\n8. Parse message text for newlines (L'\n'), adding segments to textbox\n9. If pDisconnectHandler provided with button text:\n   a. Create NO button via CreateObjectByTypeFactory(g_NoButtonConfig)\n   b. Parse button text by newlines into button textbox\n   c. Create secondary button (control 0xE9) with callback\n10. Else (single OK button path):\n    a. Create OK button via CreateObjectByTypeFactory(g_OkButtonConfig)\n    b. Parse button text into button textbox\n11. Store pDisconnectHandler in g_pDisconnectHandler global\n\nParameters:\n  pszMessage (ECX): Unicode string containing dialog message, supports embedded newlines\n  dwBufferSize (EDX): Size of message buffer (typically 0x400 = 1024 wchar_t elements)\n  pDisconnectHandler (Stack+0x4): Callback function pointer for disconnect handling, NULL for single OK button\n\nReturns:\n  void - Dialog is displayed modally\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If pDisconnectHandler is NULL or empty, displays single OK button\n  - If pDisconnectHandler has button text, displays YES/NO button pair\n  - FogAssert triggered if handler slot count reaches 0x40 (64)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x400 (1024): Maximum buffer size for Unicode text\n  0x40 (64): Maximum handler slot count before assertion\n  0x5f6 (1526): Assert line number\n  0xE9 (233): Secondary button control ID\n  0x0A (10): Newline character (L'\n')",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.09d",
