      "name": "ShowCustomErrorDialog",
      "signature": "undefined ShowCustomErrorDialog(Unicode * param_1, undefined4 param_2, Unicode * param_3, undefined4 param_4)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Creates and displays a custom error dialog with four text areas.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Dispatch pending control handlers and reset handler queue\n2. Create four GUI controls (label, two textboxes, button)\n3. Parse title text at newlines, add each line to first textbox\n4. Parse message text at newlines, add each line to second textbox\n5. Parse footer text at newlines, add each line to third textbox\n6. Create button control and store callback handler\n\nParameters:\n  ECX/lpszTitle (Unicode*): Dialog title text (newline-separated)\n  EDX/dwReserved (uint): Reserved parameter (currently unused)\n  [ESP+0x10]/lpszMessage (Unicode*): Main message text (newline-separated)\n  [ESP+0x818]/pdwCallback (uint): Button callback handler\n\nReturns: void (callback stored globally)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Text is split on '\n' (0x000A) to create multi-line text boxes\n- Empty text fields are skipped\n- Handler queue is flushed before creating new controls\n- Validates queue size against max 0x40 entries\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x804: Stack buffer size for text processing (2052 bytes)\n  0x400: Max text length (1024 wide characters)\n  0x40: Max pending handlers queue size (64 entries)\n  0xef: Button control type ID\n  0x6fa92290, 0x6fa922c0, 0x6fa922f0, 0x6fa92320, 0x6fa92350: Control type factory IDs\n\nError Handling:\n- Asserts if handler queue exceeds 0x40 entries\n- Calls FatalErrorExit(0xffffffff) on queue overflow\n\nStructure Layout:\nDialog contains these controls in order (stored in g_aPendingControlHandlers):\n  [0] Label control (type 0x6fa92290)\n  [1] First text box (type 0x6fa922c0) - title text\n  [2] Second text box (type 0x6fa922f0) - message text\n  [3] Third text box (type 0x6fa92320) - footer text\n  [4] Button control (0xef) - callback trigger\n\nKnown Issues:\n- unaff_EBX and unaff_retaddr appear to be decompiler-only temporaries\n  (not accessible via assembly for type-setting)",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.09d",
