      "name": "InitializeGameUIAndRecreateObjects",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameUIAndRecreateObjects(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes the game UI system and recreates all UI objects.\n\nThis function performs a complete UI teardown and rebuild sequence. It disconnects\nfrom Battle.net, dispatches pending inventory handlers, clears game state, initializes\npalettes, and creates all standard UI objects using the factory pattern.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set Bnet active flag and disconnect from Battle.net\n2. Dispatch all pending inventory item handlers for existing UI objects\n3. Dispatch all pending control handlers\n4. Clear global UI state counters\n5. Initialize act palette if palette flag is set\n6. Release all game units and clear hash tables\n7. Set timer context and stored value\n8. Build sky and fecha palette paths via wsprintfA\n9. Compare sky palette with fecha palette paths byte-by-byte\n10. Initialize act palette with comparison result\n11. Create 10 UI objects via CreateObjectByTypeFactory:\n    - Base UI object (g_UIObjectTypeConfig_Base)\n    - TextBox object with string ID 0x13fd (g_UIObjectTypeConfig_TextBox)\n    - Handler object with string ID 0x1401 (g_UIObjectTypeConfig_Handler)\n    - Panel objects 4-5 (g_UIObjectTypeConfig_Panel4/5)\n    - Status bar objects with string ID 0x1402 (g_UIObjectTypeConfig_StatusBar/2)\n    - Input item object (g_UIObjectTypeConfig_InputItem)\n    - Timer object (g_UIObjectTypeConfig_Timer)\n    - Final UI object (g_UIObjectTypeConfig_Final)\n12. Register timer handlers and set current input item\n13. Call UI configuration finalization\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Asserts if UI object count exceeds 0x40 (64) at any creation step\n- Palette comparison determines whether sky and fecha paths match\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x40 (64): Maximum UI object count limit\n- 0x60d (1549): Assert line number for overflow check\n- 0x13fd (5117): TextBox string resource ID\n- 0x1401 (5121): Handler string resource ID\n- 0x1402 (5122): Status bar string resource ID\n- 0x208: Stack frame size (two 260-byte path buffers)\n\nPhantom Variables (assembly-only):\n- local_104: char[260] buffer for fecha palette path (Stack[-0x104])\n- local_208: char[260] buffer for sky palette path (Stack[-0x208])",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
