      "name": "UpdateUIElementsOnTextChange",
      "signature": "undefined UpdateUIElementsOnTextChange(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initialize and display the realm character error dialog UI.\n\nThis function creates a complete error dialog interface displayed when character login fails on Battle.net. It instantiates all UI components including title, header, error message, instructions, warnings (conditional), and input controls for character name and password retry.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FUN_6fa85070 (initialization hook)\n2. Create and register TitlePanel UI object\n3. Create and register HeaderPanel UI object  \n4. Create and register unnamed panel (0x6fa8fb00)\n5. Create ErrorMessageText object and populate with string 0x1468\n6. Create InstructionText object and populate with string 0x1469\n7. Create unnamed text object (0x6fa8fbf0) and populate with string 0x146a\n8. Check if expansion MPQ exists via CheckExpansionMpqExists()\n9. If expansion missing: Create and populate ExpansionWarningText (string 0x1466)\n10. Create StandardWarningText object and populate with string 0x1467\n11. Create character name edit control (index 0x4e), set max length 0x10, populate from g_aPendingControlHandlers[0x53]+0x88\n12. Create account password edit control (index 0x44), set max length 0xd, populate from g_aPendingControlHandlers[0x53]+0xa0\n13. Create unnamed edit control (index 0x4d), set max length 0xd\n14. Set initial focus based on field content (name \u2192 password \u2192 unnamed priority)\n15. Link edit controls in circular doubly-linked list for tab navigation\n16. Create two final UI objects (0x6fa906d0, 0x6fa90700)\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If g_dwUIObjectCount exceeds 0x3f (63), calls FogAssert and FatalErrorExit\n- Initial input focus depends on character name field: if empty, focus on name; if name filled but password empty, focus on password; otherwise focus on unnamed control\n- Expansion warning only shown if CheckExpansionMpqExists() returns 0 (expansion missing)\n\nGlobal State Modified:\n- g_dwUIObjectCount: Incremented ~10 times (adds 10 UI objects)\n- g_aPendingControlHandlers[0x4e]: Character name edit control pointer\n- g_aPendingControlHandlers[0x44]: Password edit control pointer  \n- g_aPendingControlHandlers[0x4d]: Unnamed edit control pointer (likely \"OK\" or confirm button)\n- g_pUIObjectArray: Array of UI object pointers filled with created objects\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3f: Maximum UI object count (64 objects)\n- 0x1468: String ID for error message text\n- 0x1469: String ID for instruction text\n- 0x146a: String ID for additional warning text\n- 0x1466: String ID for expansion missing warning\n- 0x1467: String ID for standard warning\n- 0x60d: Line number in assertion check (FogAssert)\n- 0x10: Max length for character name field (16 chars)\n- 0xd: Max length for password field (13 chars)\n- 0x88: Offset in g_aPendingControlHandlers[0x53] for character name string\n- 0xa0: Offset in g_aPendingControlHandlers[0x53] for password string\n\nControl Handler Array Indices:\n- 0x4e: Character name edit control\n- 0x44: Account password edit control  \n- 0x4d: Unnamed control (likely OK/Confirm)\n- 0x53: Source structure containing character name and password fields",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
