      "name": "InitializeGameUIAndState",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameUIAndState(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes game UI elements and state by clearing existing UI/control objects,\nreinitializing palettes if needed, and creating core UI components.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Dispatch handlers for all existing UI objects in g_apUIObjects array\n2. Dispatch handlers for all existing control objects in g_apControlObjects array\n3. Clear UI state flags and reset object counts to zero\n4. Call SetGlobalConfig(0) to reset global configuration\n5. If g_bPaletteReinitRequired is set, reinitialize palette from path and clear flag\n6. Release all units via ReleaseAllUnits()\n7. Clear hash table via ClearHashTableAndCleanup()\n8. Set stored value to 1 via SetStoredValue(1)\n9. Create 5 UI objects via CreateObjectByTypeFactory with config structs:\n   - g_tUIObjectConfig1 (0x6fa8f710)\n   - g_tUIObjectConfig2 (0x6fa8f740)\n   - g_tUIObjectConfig3 (0x6fa8f7d0)\n   - g_tUIObjectConfig4 (0x6fa8f800)\n   - g_tInfoTextUIConfig (0x6fa8f770) for info text display\n10. Build palette file paths using wsprintfA into szPalettePath1 and szPalettePath2\n11. Compare palette paths byte-by-byte to detect if palette matches expected\n12. Store comparison result in g_bPaletteMatchesExpected\n13. Call InitActPalette with constructed paths\n14. Add version strings to info text UI based on expansion status:\n    - Expansion: string ID 0x557a\n    - Base game: string ID 0x13f0\n    - Second line: string ID 0x13f1\n15. Reset stored value to 0\n16. If music is enabled, initialize music track state\n\nParameters:\nNone (uses global state)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Asserts if UI object count exceeds 64 (0x40) at any creation point\n- Uses different string IDs for expansion vs base game version display\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x40: Maximum UI object count limit\n- 0x60d: Assert line number in source file\n- 0x557a: Expansion version string ID\n- 0x13f0: Base game version string ID\n- 0x13f1: Secondary version string ID\n- 0x208: Stack allocation size for palette paths (2 * 256 bytes + alignment)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
