      "name": "InitializeGameBattleNetSettingsAndObjects",
      "signature": "undefined4 InitializeGameBattleNetSettingsAndObjects(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes game battle.net settings and creates UI control objects.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Fade audio volume over duration and shutdown audio stream\n2. Set sound volume to maximum (0xFF)\n3. Call unidentified initialization function FUN_6fa85070\n4. Attempt to read registry value \"Aux\\\\Battle.net\" from \"Diablo II\" key\n5. If registry read fails, initialize with default string pattern \"d.d.d.d\" and write to registry\n6. If registry read succeeds, parse flags from string: \n   - Bit 0 = difficulty 7\n   - Bit 7 = difficulty 6\n   - Bit 4 = difficulty 5\n   - Bit 3 = difficulty 4\n   - Bit 6 = difficulty 3\n   - Bit 2 = difficulty 2 or 1 (depends on Bit 6)\n7. Check if expansion MPQ exists\n8. If MPQ does not exist (classic mode):\n   - Validate UI object count < 64\n   - Create 6 UI objects from factory (types 0xd8, 0x94, 0xf6, 0x22, 0x37, 0x38)\n   - Initialize textbox with string ID 0x13FA\n   - Apply difficulty bitmask to first 4 buttons based on parsed flags\n9. If MPQ exists (expansion mode):\n   - Cleanup and reinitialize game state\n   - Iterate through pending control handlers and dispatch them\n   - Clear pending handler count\n   - Initialize palette from \"sky.pal\" path\n   - Create 8 additional UI objects (types 0x8, 0x3C, 0x3D, 0x3E, 0x3F, 0x40, 0x41, 0x42)\n   - Create 2 more UI objects (types 0x43, 0x44, 0x45)\n   - Create loop with 2 iterations using default constructor\n   - Parse difficulty mode from registry flags (7 levels) using switch table\n   - Initialize button controls on valid difficulty buttons with control ID 0xA\n   - Initialize inventory button if selected\n\nParameters:\nNone - __stdcall function with no parameters\n\nReturns:\n1 - Always returns 1 (success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Registry string format: \"d.d.d.d\" where each d is a single digit representing difficulty flags\n- Difficulty mode is stored as lower byte of dwDifficultyMode variable\n- UI object array is global g_pUIObjectArray with count tracked in g_dwUIObjectCount\n- Game object handlers tracked in g_aPendingControlHandlers with count in g_dwGameObjectCount\n- Maximum 64 UI objects allowed (0x40)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xB4: Volume fade duration (180ms)\n- 0xFF: Maximum sound volume\n- 0x13FA: String ID for main textbox text\n- 0xA (10): Button control event ID\n- 0x40: Maximum UI object count (64)\n- 0x37, 0x38, 0x3C-0x45: UI object type IDs for expansion mode\n- 0xD8, 0x94, 0xF6, 0x22: UI object type IDs for classic mode",
      "name_source": "Classic/1.09d",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:d8ff08034dea697842e23d10bb5fcd7c0337340aabbf3dda0f65ac0ebe6c8cd0",
