      "name": "PollBnetAccountOperationStatus",
      "signature": "int PollBnetAccountOperationStatus(void * pUnused)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Polling callback for MessagePumpLoop during Battle.net account/character operations.\n\n  Algorithm:\n    1. Call BnclientInterface vtable offset 0xAC (account operation status check)\n    2. If status returns non-zero, call StopMessageLoop to signal completion\n    3. Check if g_dwGameStateFlags is non-zero; if so, skip to step 7\n    4. Call BnclientInterface vtable offset 0x74 (connection status check)\n    5. If not connected (zero), return 1 to continue polling\n    6. Call GetBnetLoginState to verify login; if zero (not logged in), return 1\n    7. Call BnclientInterface vtable offset 0x10 (process tick)\n    8. Call StopMessageLoop to end the loop\n    9. Return 1 (always returns 1 to continue message pump)\n\n  Parameters:\n    pUnused  (ESP+4) - Unused context pointer passed from MessagePumpLoop\n\n  Returns:\n    1 - Always returns 1 to continue message pump polling\n\n  Caller Context:\n    Called from FUN_6fa71430 via MessagePumpLoop(PollBnetAccountOperationStatus) after\n    initiating account operations with BnclientInterface+0xA8\n\n  BnclientInterface Virtual Table Offsets Used:\n    +0x10: Process/tick operation\n    +0x74: Connection status check\n    +0xAC: Account operation status check\n\n  Global References:\n    g_pBnclientInterface (0x6fa96c64): Battle.net client COM interface pointer\n    g_dwGameStateFlags (0x6fa96c68): Game state flags checked for abort condition\n\n  Note: Function spans 0x6fa711e0-0x6fa71227 (72 bytes). RET 4 confirms __stdcall.\n  Similar in structure to PollBnetLoginCredentialValidation but polls 0xAC instead of 0x64.",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
