      "name": "InitializeRealmPreferencesAndGameUI",
      "signature": "int InitializeRealmPreferencesAndGameUI(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Initializes realm preferences and game UI state.\n\nCopies preferred realm string to destination buffer and saves it to registry.\nIf the control objects indicate game initialization (0x59 == 1), dispatches\npending control handlers and configures visibility of various UI elements\nbased on player count conditions and expansion availability.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Copy realm preference string using SStrCopy\n2. Set \"Preferred Realm\" value in registry\n3. If g_apControlObjects[0x59] == 1 (game initialization):\n   a. Dispatch pending control handlers\n   b. Set \"Has Joined Game\" UI based on player count comparison\n   c. Set \"Player Count\" UI visibility based on g_dwPlayerCount > 0\n   d. Enable \"Show Players\", \"Other Players\", and \"Show Mercenary\" UI elements\n   e. If expansion MPQ exists, enable expansion-related UI elements\n   f. Reset g_dwPlayerSelectCount to 0\n   g. Update game UI state\n4. Clear pending state flag\n5. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n  None - This function takes no parameters.\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1 (TRUE) indicating successful initialization\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If g_apControlObjects[0x59] != 1, skips UI initialization entirely\n  - Expansion UI elements only enabled if CheckExpansionMpqExists() returns non-zero\n  - \"Has Joined Game\" UI depends on: g_dwPlayerCount > 0 AND g_dwPlayerSelectCount > g_dwPlayerNameCount",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:a181d90faa4237870a03fdd09cdfd48bffe108c492bf07e8c2fa7dc0c3995f5e",
