      "name": "ProcessGameStateChange",
      "signature": "uint ProcessGameStateChange(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Processes game state transitions and manages unit/player initialization and cleanup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear state change flag (g_dwStateChangeFlag = 0)\n2. If state == 1 (character select): Initialize character data, lookup character in hash table\n   - If hash entry not found: Check Bnet connection, show disconnect message or queue connection\n   - If hash entry found: Process character data via FUN_6fa74ff0()\n3. Else if state == 0/2/3 (game/lobby modes): Release all units from linked list\n   - Iterate through g_pUnitListHead linked list (offset 0x1c8 = next unit pointer)\n   - For each unit: ReleaseCompositeUnit() + ReleasePoolAllocation()\n4. Clear all state variables (g_dwPlayerCount, g_dwMeleeUnitCount, etc.)\n5. If current unit exists: Release if proper, clear g_pCurrentUnitData\n6. Validate expansion MPQ exists, show appropriate message if missing\n7. Call post-state hooks (FUN_6fa73380, FUN_6fa73a90, FUN_6fa729e0)\n8. If state == 1: Setup UI element visibility based on player counts\n9. Clear pending state flag (g_dwPendingStateFlag = 0), return 1\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\n1 = Success\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Hash table lookup failure triggers Bnet connection check\n- Expansion validation adjusts UI visibility (g_pHasExpansionUI)\n- Player count affects HasJoinedGame and ShowPlayers UI elements",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:83a9802f9d795501ec76f7723c30e288dfa5ba24b1908cae3b2ac055d3a8028d",
