      "name": "HandleGameStateChange",
      "signature": "uint HandleGameStateChange(int nGameState)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Handles game state transitions and cleanup when disconnecting from or joining game servers\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Retrieve selected item from item inventory list via g_pSelectedItemData\n  2. Convert item to Unicode string representation (0x80 byte limit)\n  3. Reset global state change flag to 0\n  4. If Battle.net state (g_dwGameState == 1):\n     - Clear text data list and prepare for realm connection\n     - Convert ASCII realm string to Unicode format\n     - Call realm lookup update function\n     - Search hash table for matching realm entry\n     - If realm not found: check Battle.net connection via interface+0x74\n       * On error: display dialog with string ID 0x14e3\n       * On success: set connection pending with realm data\n     - If realm found: process realm connection (call FUN_6fa74ff0)\n  5. Else disconnecting from game (states 0, 2, or 3):\n     - Iterate unit list and release all composite units\n     - Clear unit head and reset player counters\n     - Update UI callback functions\n     - Check for expansion MPQ (0xE5 magic indicates Diablo II expansion)\n     - If expansion not found: show string ID 0x1419 or 0x141a\n  6. Final cleanup: clear all message lists, reset UI bitmasks\n  7. Update expansion UI state (0x1)\n  8. Process realm name persistence via FUN_6fa7f460\n  9. Set UI join-game and player visibility states\n  10. Clear pending state flag and return success\n\nParameters:\n  nGameState [EBP+0x4] - Target game state value\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Always returns success\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Handles dual-execution paths: Battle.net vs offline game modes\n  - Releases all unit/item memory during disconnect\n  - Manages UI state persistence across state changes\n  - Syncs expansion pack availability with UI elements",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
