      "name": "GetClassNameStringId",
      "signature": "void GetClassNameStringId(Unicode * pszClassNameOut, dword nClassIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Returns the localized character class name string ID for a given class index.\n\nThis function is a dispatch table that maps character class indices (0-6) to \ntheir corresponding localized string resource IDs used in the expansion UI.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compare nClassIndex against valid range (0-6)\n2. If within valid range, dispatch to appropriate case handler\n3. For each valid class (0-6), call ValidateStringId with class-specific string ID\n4. Copy the returned Unicode string to pszClassNameOut buffer via Unicode::strcpy\n5. Return\n\nParameters:\npszClassNameOut (ECX): Unicode output buffer to receive localized class name\nnClassIndex (EDX): Character class index (0=Barbarian, 1=Sorceress, 2=Necromancer, \n                   3=Druid, 4=Assassin, 5=Paladin, 6=Druid variant, default=Unknown)\n\nReturns:\nNone. Output string written to pszClassNameOut buffer.\n\nString ID Mapping:\n0: 0xfab - Barbarian\n1: 0xfaa - Sorceress\n2: 0xfa9 - Necromancer\n3: 0xfa8 - Druid\n4: 0xfa7 - Assassin\n5: 0xfac - Paladin\n6: 0xfad - Druid (variant)\ndefault: 0x1507 - Unknown class\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- String IDs 0xfa7-0xfad: Localized class names (language-dependent)\n- 0x1507: Default \"Unknown\" string ID for out-of-range indices\n- Hex range 0xfab-0xfad and 0xfa7: Expansion module string resource pool\n\nError Handling:\nNo explicit error checking. If nClassIndex is out of valid range (7+), default case\nreturns string ID 0x1507 for \"Unknown\" class name.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- __fastcall convention: pszClassNameOut in ECX, nClassIndex in EDX\n- All execution paths return immediately after strcpy\n- Jump table optimization: EDX*4 + 0x6fa732c4 dispatch addresses",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:54d1267740c5c70bed23ba2c20c28af4a3cd1966c6bed41adce12b9cccd9fc72",
