      "name": "ProcessCharacterSelection",
      "signature": "undefined4 ProcessCharacterSelection(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Processes character selection from the character selection screen.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Early exit if expansion UI is active (g_dwExpansionUIState != 0)\n2. Clear control object flag at offset 0x20b\n3. If player selection matches name count:\n   a. If not in state 1 or state change flag is 0, trigger edit box callback\n   b. Decrement UI counter; if zero, set state change flag and return\n4. If player select count matches name count (duplicate check):\n   a. Clear text data list and add account name/password strings\n5. If valid selection index (not -1):\n   a. Iterate through character linked list to find selected entry\n   b. Check character flags for expansion/ladder status\n   c. Show error dialog if character requires expansion (0x14b8)\n   d. Extract class index from flags and initialize selection panel\n   e. Otherwise convert character name to Win format and process login\n\nParameters:\n   None (uses global state)\n\nReturns:\n   uint - Always returns 1 (TRUE)\n\nGlobals Accessed:\n   g_dwExpansionUIState - Expansion UI mode flag\n   g_apControlObjects[0x53] - Main control panel\n   g_apControlObjects[0x59] - Selection mode (0=normal, 1=pending, 2=alternate)\n   g_dwPlayerSelectCount - Currently selected character index\n   g_dwPlayerNameCount - Total character count\n   g_pUnitListHead - Head of character linked list\n   g_dwUICounter - UI processing counter\n   g_dwStateChangeFlag - State transition flag\n   g_pExpansionUI3 - Expansion UI text box control\n\nMagic Numbers:\n   0x2a71 - String ID for account name prompt\n   0x2a72 - String ID for password prompt\n   0x14b8 - String ID for expansion character error message\n   0x1a4 - Offset to character flags in character entry\n   0x1c8 - Offset to next pointer in character linked list\n   0x80 - Offset to character name (Unicode) in entry\n\nFlag Bits (offset 0x1a4):\n   Bit 2 (0x04) - Expansion character flag\n   Bit 3 (0x08) - Ladder character flag\n   Bit 5 (0x20) - Hardcore character flag\n   Bits 8-12 - Character class index (0-6)",
