      "name": "SelectPlayerUnit",
      "signature": "uint SelectPlayerUnit(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Selects a player unit from the player unit list by index.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if a valid player selection index is set (g_dwPlayerSelectCount != -1)\n2. If not set, return success (1)\n3. If set, traverse the unit list to find the unit at the specified index\n4. Starting from list head (g_pUnitListHead), traverse via offset 0x1c8 (next unit pointer)\n5. Count iterations until reaching the target index\n6. If unit pointer becomes NULL before reaching index, return success (1)\n7. If unit found at index, mark game state as player selected (0x20b = 2)\n8. Dispatch pending control handlers\n9. Convert unit name to Windows string representation\n10. Call FUN_6fa80ae0 to process the selected unit (likely updates UI/state)\n11. Return success (1)\n\nParameters:\n  none - uses global variables:\n    g_dwPlayerSelectCount: Selected player index (-1 = invalid/unset)\n    g_pUnitListHead: Head of linked list of units\n\nReturns:\n  uint: Always returns 1 (success)\n  \nSpecial Cases:\n  - If g_dwPlayerSelectCount == -1, function returns immediately (no selection)\n  - If unit pointer becomes NULL during traversal, returns early\n  \nMagic Numbers:\n  0x1c8: Offset of next unit pointer in CompositeUnit structure\n  0x80: Offset of unit name in CompositeUnit structure\n  0x1a0: Offset of character class byte in CompositeUnit structure\n  0x1a4: Offset of character level ushort in CompositeUnit structure\n  0x20b: Offset in g_pBnetGameData for player selection state flag\n  0x7f: Max length for Unicode to ASCII string conversion (127 chars)\n  2: Game state value indicating player is selected\n  \nError Handling:\n  - NULL pointer checks on unit list traversal\n  - Returns 1 even if unit not found (graceful exit)\n\nGlobals Used:\n  g_dwPlayerSelectCount: Index of player to select\n  g_pUnitListHead: Head of unit linked list\n  g_pBnetGameData: Network game data (offset 0x20b modified)",
