      "name": "ValidatePlayerSelectionAndExpansion",
      "signature": "uint ValidatePlayerSelectionAndExpansion(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Validates the selected player character for expansion content compatibility.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if expansion MPQ file exists via CheckExpansionMpqExists\n2. If expansion available, iterate through unit list to locate player at selected index\n3. For each unit, verify selectability flag (bit 0x20 at offset 0x1a4)\n4. Retrieve unit name pointer from offset 0x80 and validate non-null\n5. Convert Unicode name to Windows format using Unicode::unicode2Win\n6. Validate character name against game rules by calling InitializeBnetLoginControls\n7. If validation returns ordinal 0x7b, display specialized name conflict dialog\n8. Initialize Unicode string arrays and format localized error message\n9. Display appropriate error dialog (IDs 0x5570, 0x145b, 0x275a based on error type)\n10. On successful validation, mark unit with selection flag (OR 0x20) and update displays\n11. Clear expansion UI state global (g_dwExpansionUIState = 0) on errors\n12. Return 1 to indicate completion\n\nParameters:\nNone - uses globals g_pUnitListHead, g_dwPlayerSelectCount, g_pHasExpansionUI\n\nReturns:\n1 - Always returns 1 after validation and UI updates complete\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Handles Unicode name conversions (wchar_t to char and back)\n- Checks expansion selection count to find correct unit in list\n- Ordinal 0x7b triggers specialized localized message dialog (string ID 0x275a)\n- Stack arrays for name buffers (128 bytes + 512 wide chars)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x20 - Unit selectability/selected flag at offset 0x1a4\n0x80 - Offset to unit name Unicode string\n0x1c8 - Offset to next unit pointer in linked list\n0x7b - MCP client status indicating name conflict\n0x5570 - String ID for empty/null name error dialog\n0x145b - String ID for generic validation error dialog\n0x275a - String ID for name conflict format string\n0x7f - Max length for unicode2Win conversion (127 chars)\n\nError Handling:\n- Null unit name: Calls UpdateGameSaveFlags, shows dialog 0x5570\n- Validation failure (0x7b): Shows formatted name conflict dialog\n- Other validation errors: Shows dialog 0x145b\n- All error paths clear g_dwExpansionUIState to 0",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
