      "comment": "Scrollbar callback for adjusting melee unit count in player selection UI.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve current scrollbar position from player count scrollbar control\n2. If scrollbar position unchanged from previous value, return early (no update needed)\n3. Calculate melee unit count adjustment: multiply scroll delta by 2\n4. Add adjustment to current melee unit count\n5. Clamp melee unit count to minimum 0\n6. Clamp melee unit count to maximum (player count - 1)\n7. Store current scrollbar position as previous value\n8. Update expansion unit display UI with new melee count\n9. Update overall game UI state to reflect changes\n\nParameters:\n(none - callback function, state managed via globals)\n\nReturns:\n0 if scrollbar value unchanged (no update performed)\n1 if scrollbar value changed and melee count updated\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- First call: g_dwPrevScrollValue = 0, all scroll changes from 0 count\n- Max bounds: melee units cannot exceed available player count minus 1\n- Stride: each scroll unit affects melee count by 2 (scaling factor)\n\nGlobals Modified:\ng_dwMeleeUnitCount - total count of melee units available\ng_dwPrevScrollValue - previous scrollbar position for delta calculation\ng_dwPlayerCount - max player count (read-only for bounds checking)\ng_pPlayerCountScrollbar - scrollbar control (read-only for position retrieval)\n\nUI Functions Called:\nUpdateExpansionUnitDisplay() - refresh melee unit display in expansion UI\nUpdateGameUIState() - synchronize game UI with new unit counts",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
