      "name": "ProcessPlayerSelectionInput",
      "signature": "dword ProcessPlayerSelectionInput(dword pEventData)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Processes user input events for character/unit selection in the expansion UI.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate event structure by checking event ID field (offset +4) is not 0x102 (ignore flag)\n2. Extract command code from event data (offset +8)\n3. Process command based on code:\n   - 0x23: Initialize selection (set melee count from expansion start, select last player)\n   - 0x24: Clear selection (reset both counts to 0)\n   - 0x25: Move cursor up (decrement g_dwPlayerSelectCount with boundary check)\n   - 0x26: Move cursor left (decrement selection by 2, adjust melee bounds, update scrollbar)\n   - 0x27: Move cursor down (increment g_dwPlayerSelectCount with boundary check)\n   - 0x28: Move cursor right (increment selection by 2, adjust melee bounds, update scrollbar)\n4. Call UpdateExpansionUnitDisplay() and UpdateGameUIState() to refresh UI\n5. Return status code (1 = success/state changed, 0 = ignored event)\n\nParameters:\npEventData (dword): Pointer to event structure with format:\n  [+0x0] Unknown field\n  [+0x4] Event type/flags (0x102 = ignore this event)\n  [+0x8] Command code (0x23-0x28)\n\nReturns:\n0 = Event ignored/not processed\n1 = Event processed, UI state updated\n\nGlobal Variables Used:\ng_dwPlayerCount: Total number of player slots available\ng_dwPlayerSelectCount: Currently selected player index\ng_dwMeleeUnitCount: Count of melee units in expansion view\ng_dwExpansionPlayerStartIndex: Starting index for expansion player list\ng_pCharacterScrollbar: Scrollbar control for character list\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Event type 0x102 is filtered out and returns 0 immediately\n- Boundary checks prevent selection from exceeding g_dwPlayerCount\n- Melee unit count is adjusted based on expansion display boundaries\n- Left/right movement (0x26, 0x28) updates scrollbar position\n\nControl Flow:\n- Five command branches (0x23-0x28) with fallthrough to common cleanup\n- Cases 0x26 and 0x28 have early returns when UI is updated\n- Cases 0x25 and 0x27 share common boundary adjustment logic (LAB_6fa74e68/LAB_6fa74e77)\n- All paths converge at final UpdateExpansionUnitDisplay/UpdateGameUIState calls",
