      "name": "CreateUIObjectByTypeId",
      "signature": "void * CreateUIObjectByTypeId(int nTypeId)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void *",
      "comment": "Creates a UI object by type ID and registers it in the global object array.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate that nTypeId is less than 0x40 (max UI objects)\n2. If validation fails, trigger FogAssert and call FatalErrorExit(-1)\n3. Create object using CreateObjectByTypeFactory() with pointer to template data\n4. Store created object pointer in g_pUIObjectArray at index g_dwUIObjectCount\n5. Increment g_dwUIObjectCount\n6. Return pointer to newly created object\n\nParameters:\nnTypeId (ECX, int): Type ID for the UI object to create. Valid range: 0-63 (0x3F).\n  Each type ID corresponds to a 48-byte (0x30) structure template in g_pUIObjectTemplates.\n\nReturns:\nvoid *: Pointer to the newly created UI object. Returns value from CreateObjectByTypeFactory().\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Type IDs >= 0x40 are considered invalid and trigger assertion failure\n- FatalErrorExit(-1) is called on validation failure (never returns)\n- All created objects are stored sequentially in g_pUIObjectArray\n- g_dwUIObjectCount tracks total objects created during initialization\n\nError Handling:\n- FogAssert() is called with expected condition (dwUIObjectCount &lt; 0x40)\n- If assertion fails, FatalErrorExit(-1) terminates the process\n- No return value checking on CreateObjectByTypeFactory() output\n\nGlobal State Modified:\n- g_dwUIObjectCount: Incremented by 1\n- g_pUIObjectArray: New entry added at [g_dwUIObjectCount]\n\nNotes:\n- Called during InitializeGameState() to populate UI elements\n- Factory pattern allows type-safe object creation\n- Objects are indexed for fast lookup by UI code",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
