      "comment": "Initializes Battle.net login UI controls.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Process any pending control handlers in queue (dispatch up to g_nPendingControlHandlerCount items)\n2. Clear pending handler count and activate Battle.net connection state\n3. Check g_aPendingControlHandlers[0x5a] to determine login UI variant (A or B)\n4. Create and register config container object (CONFIG_A or CONFIG_B type)\n5. Create and register unit object (DAT_6fa91f30 or DAT_6fa92440 depending on variant)\n6. Create and register sub-config object (CONFIG_A_SUB or CONFIG_B_SUB type)\n7. Create and register text box unit object (final UI element)\n8. Set unit flags to 1 for all three created objects\n9. Validate login message string ID (0x147b)\n10. Add login message text to text box\n11. Register Battle.net disconnect handler callback (SetBnetLoginStateReady)\n\nParameters:\nNone (void)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Array bounds checking: Asserts if g_nPendingControlHandlerCount exceeds 0x3f (63 items)\n- Conditional variant selection based on g_aPendingControlHandlers[0x5a] == 0\n- Multiple error checks via FogAssert and FatalErrorExit(0xffffffff)\n\nError Handling:\n- FogAssert called if array bounds exceeded (0x6fa92a88 assertion string)\n- FatalErrorExit(-1) called on critical errors during handler registration\n\nGlobal Variables:\n- g_nPendingControlHandlerCount: Handler queue item counter\n- g_aPendingControlHandlers: Array of pending handler object pointers (0x6fa977a4 base)\n- g_dwBnetConnectionActive: Connection state flag (set to 1)\n- g_dwBnetLoginState: Login progression state (cleared to 0)\n- g_pBnetDisconnectHandler: Global callback registered (0x6fa977a0)\n\nConstants:\n- 0x40 (64): Max handlers array size\n- 0x3f (63): Max valid handler count before assertion\n- 0x5a (90): Offset into handlers array for variant check\n- 0x147b: String ID for login message\n- 0x5f6 (1526): Assertion line number",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
