      "name": "InitializePendingControlHandlers",
      "signature": "uint InitializePendingControlHandlers(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Initialize pending control handlers and setup UI state after login.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize handler index counter to 0\n2. Set disconnection handler to SetBnetLoginStateReady\n3. Process all pending control handlers in queue (dispatch each handler)\n4. Clear pending control handler count\n5. Create ConfigTypeA object via factory, add to handlers array, enforce size limit (max 0x40)\n6. Create and initialize second object (DAT_6fa924d0), add to handlers array, enforce limit\n7. Create and initialize third object (DAT_6fa92500), add to handlers array, enforce limit\n8. Convert localized error string to Unicode in final object\n9. Return success status (1)\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nuint: 1 on success\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Enforces maximum handler array size (0x3f/63 handlers)\n- Asserts if limit exceeded before Fatal error\n- Creates exactly 3 UI objects in sequence\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3f = 63 (max pending handlers before overflow)\n- Array size enforcement at 0x40 (64 maximum)\n\nError Handling:\n- FogAssert on handler overflow (size check violation)\n- FatalErrorExit(0xffffffff) on assertion failure\n\nStructure Layout:\nHandler array stores uint pointers to created objects\nEach object created via factory with configurable type specification\nObjects initialized with flags and Unicode string conversion",
