      "name": "UpdateUIElementsOnTextChange",
      "signature": "void UpdateUIElementsOnTextChange(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Updates UI elements in response to text change events in the character selection screen.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Dispatch pending inventory item handlers for all registered UI objects\n2. Clear global UI object counters (count, flags, state)\n3. Dispatch remaining pending control handlers\n4. Reset global configuration to default state\n5. If palette reinitialization flag is set:\n   a. Reinitialize palettes from stored path pointers\n   b. Clear the reinitialization flag\n6. Initialize act palette and clear hash table resources\n7. Set stored value flag and invalidate text box state globals (-1)\n8. Format palette path buffers using wsprintfA with stored paths\n9. Compare palette paths byte-by-byte to detect changes\n10. Store comparison result (1=match, 0=different) for palette caching\n11. Initialize act palette with formatted path buffers\n12. Create UI objects via CreateObjectByTypeFactory for each UI element:\n    - Main display objects (3 objects)\n    - Text display with ValidateStringId(0x1407)\n    - Special mode objects if game mode flag == 1\n    - Input field object (set as current input item)\n    - Scrollable, button, and edit control objects\n13. Configure edit control with callbacks and character name mask\n14. If expansion MPQ exists:\n    - Create expansion-specific UI objects\n    - Configure expansion checkbox, toggle, and button elements\n15. Else create fallback UI objects using CreateUIObjectByTypeId\n16. Create common UI object (type 0xaf)\n17. Initialize edit fields if initialization flag not set\n18. Clear bit masks on scrollable UI objects\n19. Create final button UI (type 0xb5)\n20. Branch based on expansion/online mode:\n    - Online: Create network-specific UI objects (0xb9, 0xba, 0xb4, 0xca, 0xbb, 0xcb, 0xb1)\n    - Offline: Create local game UI objects (0xb4, 0xb6, 0xb3, 0xb7, 0xb2)\n21. Load character select resources\n\nParameters: None (void function)\n\nReturns: void\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x40 (64): Maximum UI object count limit\n- 0x60d (1549): FogAssert line number for object limit check\n- 0x1407, 0x149c, 0x149d, 0x1405, 0x1406: String resource IDs\n- 0x58cb: Expansion-specific string ID\n- 0xaf, 0xb1-0xb7, 0xb9, 0xba, 0xbb, 0xc3, 0xc4, 0xca, 0xcb: UI object type IDs\n- 0x10 (16): Edit control configuration value\n\nError Handling:\n- FogAssert triggered if UI object count reaches 64 (0x40) limit\n- Multiple assertion checks throughout object creation sequence",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
