      "name": "InitializeGameIntroAndResources",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameIntroAndResources(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes game introduction resources including graphics, palettes, UI objects, and music.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Process pending Windows messages (WM_QUIT, WM_LBUTTONDOWN, WM_CHAR, etc.)\n2. Check CPU feature support (3DNow/MMX) and select resolution mode accordingly\n3. Copy resolution string and initialize locale settings\n4. Build video path from resolution string and locale ID\n5. Check for video file existence in MPQ archives\n6. Initialize graphics via GfxDispatchMethod38 with resolution parameters\n7. Dispatch all UI inventory item handlers (64 max objects)\n8. Reset game object counters and configuration\n9. Reinitialize palette if needed (sky palette comparison)\n10. Release all units and set stored values\n11. Create UI objects (intro, buttons, text boxes) via CreateObjectByTypeFactory\n12. Format and initialize act palette paths\n13. Initialize music track state based on expansion detection\n\nParameters: None (void)\n\nReturns: void (modifies global game state)\n\nStack Variables (phantom - cannot be typed via API):\n- szVideoPath: char[256] at Stack[-0x30c] - Video file path buffer\n- szResolution: char[8] at Stack[-0x330] - Resolution string suffix\n- dwLocaleId: uint at Stack[-0x334] - Locale identifier\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Expansion check at 0x6fa7d379 determines string IDs for intro text\n- Palette comparison uses byte-by-byte strcmp-like loop\n- Max 64 UI objects enforced by FogAssert\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x202: WM_LBUTTONUP message\n- 0x201: WM_LBUTTONDOWN message  \n- 0x12: WM_QUIT message\n- 0x102: WM_CHAR message\n- 0x40: Maximum UI object count\n- 0x60d: Line number for FogAssert\n- 0x557a/0x13f0: Expansion/Classic string IDs",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
