      "name": "InitializeCreditsDisplay",
      "signature": "dword InitializeCreditsDisplay(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Initializes the credits display by loading and parsing credits file data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get locale string and check for expansion MPQ existence\n2. Format credits file path based on locale and expansion status\n3. Open credits file asynchronously and get file size\n4. Allocate memory buffer for file contents (0x11f0 bytes)\n5. Read entire file into buffer asynchronously\n6. Close file handle and detect encoding (UTF-16 BE/LE or ANSI)\n7. Convert encoding to Unicode if needed, swap endianness for BE\n8. Strip CR/LF characters (0x0A, 0x0D) from credits data\n9. Clear text blocks (main, left, right) 50 times each\n10. Parse credits sections marked with '*' (0x2A) prefix\n11. Split name/title pairs into left/right columns\n12. Add parsed text to appropriate text blocks\n13. Add 50 blank lines and final credits text to main block\n14. Store credits text block binding state\n\nParameters:\n  None (void function)\n\nReturns:\n  uint - Always returns 1 (success)\n\nGlobals Modified:\n  g_pCreditsTextBlockMain (0x6fa97c78) - Main credits text block pointer\n  g_pCreditsTextBlockRight (0x6fa97c74) - Right column text block pointer  \n  g_pCreditsTextBlockLeft (0x6fa97c70) - Left column text block pointer\n  g_dwCreditsBindingState (0x6fa97c80) - Binding state from GetBindingState\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x11f0 (4592) - Initial buffer allocation size\n  0x104 (260) - MAX_PATH for file path buffers\n  0x32 (50) - Number of blank lines/clear iterations\n  0x400 (1024) - Unicode string buffer size (wchar_t[1024])\n  0x100 (256) - Per-line buffer sizes\n  0xfeff - UTF-16 Big Endian BOM\n  0xfffe - UTF-16 Little Endian BOM\n  0x2a ('*') - Section header marker character\n  0x80 (128) - ASCII character boundary check\n\nFile Format:\n  Credits file uses Unicode encoding with '*' as section markers.\n  Lines starting with '*' mark new sections (header text).\n  Non-header lines contain name/title pairs for left/right columns.\n\nError Handling:\n  Calls FogAssert and ReportError(-1) on allocation or file read failures.\n  Returns early if file size is less than 3 bytes.\n\nPhantom Variables:\n  abStackPadding - Stack padding variable (undefined1[4]) that cannot be retyped.",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
