      "name": "SwapWordEndianness",
      "signature": "void SwapWordEndianness(word * pWords, dword wCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Swap endianness of word (16-bit) array elements in-place.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if word count is zero; if so, return immediately\n2. For each word in the array:\n   - Load the word value from memory\n   - Swap high and low bytes (convert endianness)\n   - Store the swapped word back to the same memory location\n3. Return after processing all words\n\nParameters:\n  pWords: Pointer to array of uint16 values to swap (registers: ECX/EAX)\n  wCount: Number of uint16 elements to process (registers: EDX/ESI)\n\nReturns:\n  void - modifies array in-place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If wCount is 0, function returns immediately without processing\n  - Array must be at least wCount*2 bytes in size\n  - No bounds checking is performed\n\nAlgorithm Details:\n  The byte swap is implemented via:\n    High byte = original low byte\n    Low byte = original high byte\n  This effectively converts between little-endian and big-endian representations.\n\nUsage Context:\n  Called by InitializeCreditsDisplay - likely for converting credit text\n  or display data between platform endianness formats",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:71232d07edd69ab3e3273a05dca2f95a3e053f94dc54addaae8fcf10c3195d44",
