      "name": "ReinitializeMpqArchives",
      "signature": "BOOL ReinitializeMpqArchives(char * lpszMpqPath)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "BOOL",
      "comment": "Reinitializes the MPQ (Mo'PaQ) archive system for resource loading.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Close all currently open MPQ archives\n2. Attempt to initialize D2 MPQ data with default parameters\n3. If initialization fails (returns 0):\n   a. Close archives again as cleanup\n   b. Reinitialize MPQ files with game object handlers\n   c. Return FALSE indicating failure\n4. If initialization succeeds:\n   a. Call cleanup/reinit routine with custom MPQ path\n   b. Return TRUE indicating success\n\nParameters:\n  lpszMpqPath - char*, path string for custom MPQ location passed to cleanup routine\n\nReturns:\n  BOOL - TRUE (1) on successful MPQ reinitialization\n         FALSE (0) if InitializeD2MpqData fails\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - On failure path, archives are closed twice (initial close + failure cleanup)\n  - InitializeMpqFiles receives ProcessGameObjectHandlers and InitializeUIAndRunMessageLoop as handlers\n  - The g_apControlObjects[0x53] is passed as 4th parameter to InitializeMpqFiles\n\nCalled Functions:\n  - CloseAllMpqArchives: Releases all open MPQ file handles\n  - InitializeD2MpqData: Core MPQ initialization (LAB_6fa7f000, priority=0, expansion=0)\n  - InitializeMpqFiles: Fallback initialization with callback handlers\n  - FUN_6fa7ea30: Cleanup/reinit UI and resources with path parameter",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
