      "name": "ProcessPendingControlHandlers",
      "signature": "int ProcessPendingControlHandlers(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Processes a pending control handler from the queue.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initializes the control handler processing system via func_0x6fa85380\n2. Retrieves pending control handler at index 0x53 from g_aPendingControlHandlers array\n3. Invokes func_0x6fa8536e with parameter 0 and the retrieved handler\n4. If func_0x6fa8536e returns 0 (processing failed or condition not met), retries with same parameters\n5. Finalizes control handler state via func_0x6fa7ea30\n6. Returns 1 indicating successful completion\n\nParameters:\nNone (void)\n\nReturns:\nint - Always returns 1 to indicate function completed successfully\n\nSpecial Cases:\nArray index 0x53 (83 decimal) is a fixed queue position for control handlers. The retry mechanism allows for handling transient failures in handler processing. If first attempt returns 0, a second attempt is made.\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x53 - Fixed array index for pending control handler\n0 - Return value from func_0x6fa8536e indicating processing not completed\n1 - Success return value\n\nError Handling:\nNo explicit error conditions. Always returns 1 regardless of handler processing outcome.\n\nDependencies:\n- func_0x6fa85380 (initialization)\n- func_0x6fa8536e (handler processing/dispatch)\n- func_0x6fa7ea30 (finalization)\n- g_aPendingControlHandlers (global handler queue, 256 entries)",
