      "name": "InitializeGameWorldAndInventory",
      "signature": "uint InitializeGameWorldAndInventory(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Initializes game world state and processes inventory handler dispatch.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Sets game state config flag to 8 at global config struct offset 0x14\n2. Retrieves save directory path via GetSaveDirectoryPath()\n3. Copies path to global config struct at offset 0x32 using REPNE SCASB strlen + MOVSD/MOVSB\n4. Sets global mode flag at 0x6fa97908 to 2\n5. Sets config value at offset 0x204 to 4\n6. Calls InitializeGameState to get state string\n7. Formats file search pattern using SafeStringFormat with wildcard\n8. Searches for existing save files using FindFirstFileA into WIN32_FIND_DATA\n9. If no files found (INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE=-1), calls ReleaseAllUnits and returns 1\n10. Closes find handle via FindClose\n11. Calls InitializeGameState to reinitialize game state\n12. First loop: Dispatches inventory handlers for g_adwInventoryTable1 (0x6fa97688)\n    - Uses pdwInventoryEntry pointer, iterating while index < g_dwInventoryCount1\n    - Increments pointer by 4 bytes per iteration\n13. Resets inventory counters at 0x6fa97c60, 0x6fa97c64, 0x6fa97c58 to 0\n14. Second loop: Dispatches inventory handlers for g_adwInventoryTable2 (0x6fa977a4)\n    - Iterates while index < g_dwInventoryCount2 (0x6fa97c5c)\n15. Resets g_dwInventoryCount2 to 0\n16. Calls SetGlobalConfig(0) to clear global config\n17. If g_dwPaletteFlag (0x6fa97c84) is non-zero:\n    a. Loads palette ID strings from 0x6fa8d440 and 0x6fa8d444\n    b. Gets wsprintfA pointer from 0x6fa8d40c\n    c. Formats two palette path strings using format at 0x6fa92a74\n    d. Compares palette strings byte-by-byte with 2-byte stride\n    e. Sets g_bPaletteMatch (0x6fa9790c) to 1 if equal, 0 otherwise\n    f. Calls InitActPalette with comparison buffer and result flag\n    g. Clears g_dwPaletteFlag to 0\n18. Calls ReleaseAllUnits to release all active units\n19. Calls ClearHashTableAndCleanup to purge hash tables\n20. Calls SetStoredValue(1) to mark initialization complete\n21. Calls ProcessSlots to finalize slot processing\n\nParameters:\nNone - This function takes no parameters (__stdcall void parameter list).\n\nReturns:\nuint - Always returns 1 on success.\n    Early exit returns 1 if FindFirstFileA returns INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE.\n    Normal exit returns 1 after completing all initialization steps.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit at step 9 if no save files found (FindFirstFileA returns -1)\n- Palette comparison loop handles null-terminated strings with 2-byte stride optimization\n- Both inventory loops may execute zero times if counts are <= 0\n- String copy uses optimized MOVSD/MOVSB sequence for DWORD-aligned bulk copy\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x8: Game state initialization flag (offset 0x14)\n- 0x2: Global mode flag value at 0x6fa97908\n- 0x4: Config value at offset 0x204\n- 0x400: Path buffer size (1024 bytes)\n- 0x140: WIN32_FIND_DATAA structure size (320 bytes)\n- 0x1: Initialization success return value\n- -1 (0xFFFFFFFF): INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE from FindFirstFileA\n\nStructure Layout (Global Config at [0x6fa978f0]):\nOffset   Size   Field              Type\n0x14     4      dwStateFlag        uint\n0x32     var    szSavePath         char[]\n0x204    4      dwConfigValue      uint\n\nStack Frame Layout:\nOffset      Size    Variable           Type\n-0x400      1024    szFormattedPath    char[1024]\n-0x800      1024    szSearchPattern    char[1024]\n-0xa44      320     findData           WIN32_FIND_DATAA\n\nGlobal Variables:\n- 0x6fa978f0: g_pGameConfig - Pointer to main game config structure\n- 0x6fa97908: g_dwModeFlag - Mode state flag (set to 2)\n- 0x6fa97688: g_adwInventoryTable1 - First inventory dispatch table (array of uint)\n- 0x6fa977a4: g_adwInventoryTable2 - Second inventory dispatch table (array of uint)\n- 0x6fa97c58: g_dwInventoryCount1 - Count for first table\n- 0x6fa97c5c: g_dwInventoryCount2 - Count for second table\n- 0x6fa97c60, 0x6fa97c64: Inventory state counters (reset to 0)\n- 0x6fa97c84: g_dwPaletteFlag - Palette initialization flag\n- 0x6fa9790c: g_bPaletteMatch - Palette comparison result flag\n- 0x6fa8d440, 0x6fa8d444: Palette identifier strings\n- 0x6fa8d40c: wsprintfA function pointer\n\nNote: Stack array types (findData, szFormattedPath, szSearchPattern) cannot be\nresolved to char[N] or WIN32_FIND_DATAA due to Ghidra decompiler limitations\nwith HighVariable resolution for large stack allocations.",
