      "name": "InitializeGameUIObjectsAndPalette",
      "signature": "int InitializeGameUIObjectsAndPalette(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "InitializeGameUIObjectsAndPalette - Initialize game UI controls and palette configuration.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x208 bytes (520 bytes = 260*2) stack frame for two file path buffers\n2. Format palette file paths using wsprintf with DATA_GLOBAL directory prefix\n3. Compare palette source files (sky .pl2 vs .dat) byte-by-byte using word-aligned reads\n4. Store comparison result flag at g_apControlObjects[0x5a] (1=equal, 0=different)\n5. Initialize palette actor system with formatted file path strings\n6. Dispatch inventory item handler to initialize UI state\n7. Create 6 UI control objects from factory configurations in sequence:\n   a. g_UIConfigInventoryButton (offset +0x229) - inventory button control\n   b. g_UIConfigStatusPanel (offset +0x21d) - status panel display\n   c. g_UIConfigTextDisplay (offset +0x205) - text display with string ID 0x2a54\n   d. g_UIConfigEditControl (offset +0x211) - edit control, set as current input\n   e. g_UIConfigInputItem (offset +0x235) - input item control\n   f. g_UIConfigFinalControl (offset +0x241) - final control in sequence\n8. Each creation validates object count < 64 (MAX_CHILDREN), increments counter\n9. Initialize screenshot configuration from edit control\n\nParameters:\nNone (void function)\n\nReturns:\nint - Always returns 1 (success)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0x208 - Stack frame size (520 bytes for two 260-char path buffers)\n0x5a  - Control object array index for palette comparison flag (index 90)\n0x5b  - Control object array index for edit control data (index 91)\n0x3f  - Maximum children count (63, asserts if exceeded)\n0x5f6 - Source line number in D2Launch for assertion (1526)\n0x2a54 - String ID for text display initialization (10836)\n\nError Handling:\n- Calls FogAssert with expression/file/line if object count >= 64\n- FogAssert triggers ReportError(-1) which terminates execution",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
