      "name": "InitializeBnetLoginControls",
      "signature": "bool InitializeBnetLoginControls(void * pThis, byte * pbStringBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Initializes the Battle.net login screen UI controls and enters the message loop.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if currently loading a game (Ordinal_10002)\n2. If not loading, validate the provided string buffer (FUN_6fa83a50) to ensure valid content\n3. If validation fails (result 1-2), reset RNG and return false (game is loading)\n4. Dispatch any pending control handlers (DispatchInventoryItemHandler loop)\n5. Reset game object count to 0 and set connection state flags\n6. Branch based on whether login control [0x5a] exists in array:\n   - FALSE branch: Create TypeA/TypeA_Sub controls\n   - TRUE branch: Create TypeB/TypeB_Sub controls\n7. Create third level control (TypeA_Sub or TypeB_Sub)\n8. Set unit flags to 1 for all three controls\n9. Validate string ID 0x147b and add text to main textbox\n10. Set up message loop disconnect handler (SetBnetLoginStateReady)\n11. Perform ordinal initialization (Ordinal_10062)\n12. Enter main message pump loop with HandleMessageLoopShutdown callback\n13. Check final ordinal result (Ordinal_10046) and return success/failure\n\nParameters:\n  pThis (ECX IMPLICIT): This pointer to login manager object\n  pbStringBuffer (EDX): Pointer to string buffer for validation\n\nReturns:\n  true if message loop exited gracefully, false if validation failed or early exit\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Controls are stored in g_aPendingControlHandlers array (max 64 entries, 0x40)\n  - Array bounds are checked with FogAssert before each insertion\n  - Multiple control types available based on login state\n  - Return value inverted by final calculation: ('\\\\x01' - (iVar1 != 0))\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x5a (90): Sentinel index check in control array\n  0x3f (63): Max array size boundary check (0x40 = 64 entries)\n  0x147b (5243): String ID for login text\n  -0x1 (0xFFFFFFFF): Fatal error exit code\n\nGlobals Modified:\n  g_dwGameObjectCount: Set to 0, then incremented as controls added\n  g_dwBnetConnectionActive: Set to 1\n  g_dwBnetLoginState: Set to 0\n  g_aPendingControlHandlers[0..2]: Populated with 3 control objects\n  g_pBnetDisconnectHandler: Set to SetBnetLoginStateReady\n  _g_dwBnetConnectionActive: Set to 1 (overlapping global)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
