      "name": "ProcessCharacterSelectionInitialization",
      "signature": "int ProcessCharacterSelectionInitialization(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Initializes and processes character selection state for the game client.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calls ResetInitMode() to initialize game state\n2. Processes Windows message queue, filtering out mouse/keyboard events\n3. Checks CPU features to determine video resolution support\n4. Constructs locale-specific intro video path (data/video/<locale>/d2intro<resolution>.bik)\n5. Attempts to open intro video from MPQ archive, falls back to alternate path\n6. Dispatches video playback to graphics subsystem\n7. Iterates through UI objects, dispatching inventory handlers for each\n8. Resets UI object count and global state arrays\n9. Dispatches pending control handlers for UI event processing\n10. Resets global configuration and reinitializes palette if needed\n11. Releases all units and clears hash table for memory cleanup\n12. Asserts UI object count < MAX_CHILDREN (64), exits on failure\n13. Creates main character selection UI object from type factory\n14. Creates additional UI objects: portrait (3), stats panel (6), buttons (7)\n15. Initializes sky palette for character selection background\n16. Checks expansion pack availability and sets appropriate string IDs\n17. Adds title and subtitle text to character selection text box\n18. Initializes music track state if music is enabled\n19. Calls InitializeGraphics(1) to finalize graphics state\n20. Repeats UI object cleanup and recreation sequence for second pass\n21. Returns 1 on successful initialization\n\nParameters:\n- None (uses global state exclusively)\n\nReturns:\n- int: 1 on successful initialization (always returns 1 if function completes)\n- Function exits early via ReportError(-1) if UI object count exceeds limit\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- WM_LBUTTONDOWN (0x201), WM_LBUTTONUP (0x202): Filtered from message queue\n- WM_QUIT (0x12), WM_CHAR (0x102): Filtered from message queue\n- WM_RBUTTONDOWN (0x204), WM_RBUTTONUP (0x205): Jump table handled\n- Expansion check: Uses string 0x557a if expansion MPQ exists, 0x13f0 for classic\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n- 0x130 (304): Stack frame size for local variables\n- 0x40 (64): MAX_CHILDREN limit for UI objects\n- 0x60d (1549): Assert line number in source file\n- 0x557a (21882): Expansion string ID for title text\n- 0x13f0 (5104): Classic string ID for title text\n- 0x13f1 (5105): String ID for subtitle text\n- 3, 6, 7: UI object type IDs (portrait, stats, buttons)\n- 4: UI object type ID for text box\n\nError Handling:\n- Asserts g_dwUIObjectCount < 0x40 before creating new UI objects\n- Calls FogAssert with source file and line number on assertion failure\n- Calls ReportError(-1) to terminate on fatal errors\n\nGlobal Variables Accessed:\n- g_dwUIObjectCount: Current count of UI objects\n- g_pUIObjectArray: Array of pointers to UI objects\n- g_adwPad_6fa97c60: Padding/state array\n- g_bPaletteReinitFlag: Flag indicating palette needs reinitialization\n- g_pPaletteDatPath, g_pPalettePl2Path: Palette file paths\n- g_sz640x292Resolution, sz640x146_6fa936f8: Resolution strings",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
