      "name": "HandleBattleNetLoginDialogSetup",
      "signature": "uint HandleBattleNetLoginDialogSetup(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Initialize Battle.net login dialog and validate system resources before UI creation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract Unicode text from edit box controls (IDs 0x4e and 0x44)\n2. Convert extracted text from Unicode to Windows format using Unicode::unicode2Win()\n3. Retrieve save directory path using GetSaveDirectoryPath(acStack_c00, 0x400)\n4. Truncate path at first backslash to extract root directory\n5. Query disk free space with GetDiskFreeSpaceA() for root path\n6. Calculate total free bytes as FreeClusters * BytesPerSector * ClustersPerSector\n7. If free space < 5000 bytes, return HandleBattleNetLoginDialog() result\n8. Validate string resource ID 0x141d with ValidateStringId()\n9. Dispatch cleanup handlers for all pending objects in range [0, g_dwGameObjectCount)\n10. Reset g_dwGameObjectCount to 0\n11. Branch on g_aPendingControlHandlers[0x5a] (config flag)\n12. If config flag == 0: Create config type A + border standard + type A sub-control\n13. If config flag != 0: Create config type B + border alt + type B sub-control\n14. Verify g_dwGameObjectCount <= 0x3f after creating 3 controls; fatal error if exceeded\n15. Set unit flags to 1 for all three created controls\n16. Initialize 1026-element wide character buffer (awStack_804)\n17. Copy text from extraout_EAX to wide buffer using Unicode::strncpy()\n18. Parse buffer by newline (L'\\\n') and add each line to text box control\n19. Assign ResetGameStateAndCleanup to global disconnect handler\n20. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nuint: 1 on success, or HandleBattleNetLoginDialog return code if disk space insufficient\n\nMagic Numbers:\n4999 = Minimum free disk space (bytes) required\n0x3f = 63 maximum game object controls\n0x100 = Buffer size for text conversion (256 bytes)\n0x400 = Buffer size for directory path (1024 bytes)\n0x141d = String resource ID to validate\n0x88, 0xa0 = Offset positions in control structure for text storage\n0x4e, 0x44 = Edit box control IDs\n0x53 = Control handler structure offset\n1026 = Wide character buffer element count",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
