      "name": "UpdateUIElementsOnTextChange",
      "signature": "void UpdateUIElementsOnTextChange(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Initializes the login/character creation dialog UI with all text boxes, labels, and edit controls.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve existing character name from edit box control (handler index 0x4E)\n2. Convert character name data from Unicode to ASCII format (256 byte buffer)\n3. Invoke FUN_6fa85070 to prepare UI rendering context\n4. Create and register UI object hierarchy in sequence, validating count after each:\n   - Title Panel, Header Panel, two Content Panels\n   - Error Message, Instruction, and Caption Text boxes\n   - Conditional expansion warning or base game text\n5. Create primary edit controls: Character Name (10 char limit) and Account Name (13 char)\n6. Create Confirmation Code input (13 char) and Tab Order control\n7. Register two additional UI objects via CreateUIObjectByTypeId\n8. Link all editable controls into circular doubly-linked list for keyboard navigation:\n   CharacterName <-> AccountName <-> ConfirmationCode <-> TabControl <-> (back to CharacterName)\n9. Set initial input focus: Account Name field if Character Name is empty, otherwise Character Name field\n\nParameters:\nvoid (no parameters)\n\nReturns:\nvoid (updates global UI state)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Expansion content conditionally included based on CheckExpansionMpqExists() check\n- Initial focus logic branches on szCharacterName[0] != '\\0' check\n- Every UI object creation validates g_dwUIObjectCount against 0x3F maximum\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x4E: Character Name edit control handler index in g_aPendingControlHandlers\n0x53: Character Name data storage structure handler index\n0x44: Account Name edit control handler index\n0x4D: Tab Order control handler index\n0x88: Offset into handler structure for character name string storage\n0x100: Character name buffer size in bytes (256)\n0x3F: Maximum allowed UI objects in array (63)\n0x10: Character Name edit field 16-character limit\n0x0D: Account/Confirmation Name edit field 13-character limit\n0x1468, 0x2A60-0x2A63: String resource IDs for UI labels and text\n\nError Handling:\n- FogAssert + FatalErrorExit(0xFFFFFFFF) triggered when g_dwUIObjectCount exceeds 0x3F\n- ValidateStringId called before adding text to ensure resource ID validity\n- Error condition asserts line 0x60D with source file path for debugging\n\nGlobal State Updates:\n- g_dwUIObjectCount: Incremented after each UI object registration (12+ increments)\n- g_pUIObjectArray: Populated with created UI object pointers\n- g_aPendingControlHandlers: Updated with edit control indices (0x4E, 0x44, 0x4D)\n- DAT_6fa9766c: Confirmation Code control pointer assigned\n- SetCurrentInputPointer: Initial input focus set based on character name state",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:f9f79c4c49ce755bd33b52ed2209f0b7f3eff7769dc861e3b529c79dcb723d5b",
