      "name": "PopulateGameStateConfigBuffer",
      "signature": "void PopulateGameStateConfigBuffer(char * szPath, byte bStateFlags, void * pConfigBuffer, dword dwFlagsWord)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Populate game state configuration buffer with initialization data and string parameters.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear 0x82-byte config buffer at g_GameStateBuffer (0x6fa97cc0) using REP STOSD\n2. Calculate length of config path string (pszConfigPath) via REPNE SCASB length probe\n3. Copy config path string to buffer offset +0x8 via REP MOVSD/MOVSB\n4. Write fixed header magic (0xaa55aa55) at offset +0x0\n5. Write fixed type marker (0x57) at offset +0x4\n6. Write flags word (dwFlagsWord & 0xffff | 1) to offset +0x18\n7. Write configuration identifier (0x13f) to offset +0x1c\n8. Write version/format marker (0x10) to offset +0x1e\n9. Write buffer size (0x82) to offset +0x20\n10. Write state flags (bStateFlags, cast to ushort) to offset +0x22\n11. Call EncodeVarInt2Byte(pConfigBuffer, 7) to encode 7 at buffer start\n12. Copy 11-byte game init data block from g_abGameInitBytes to pConfigBuffer+0x2\n13. Write bStateFlags+1 to pConfigBuffer+0x3 as next state marker\n14. Fill pConfigBuffer+0x4 through 0xc with 0xff (9 slot markers)\n15. Call EncodeVarInt2Byte(pConfigBuffer+0xd, dwFlagsWord) to encode flags\n16. Call EncodeVarInt2Byte(pConfigBuffer+0x10, 0) to encode terminator\n17. Write 0xff padding to pConfigBuffer+0x12-0x14\n18. Copy null-terminated string from g_szAuxGameString to pConfigBuffer+0x15\n\nParameters:\npszConfigPath (ECX): pointer to null-terminated game config path string\nbStateFlags (DL): state/session flags byte value (0-255)\npConfigBuffer (Stack+0x4): pointer to output buffer (recommend 100+ bytes)\ndwFlagsWord (Stack+0x8): 16-bit feature flags word\n\nReturns:\nvoid - modifies pConfigBuffer contents, no return value",
