      "name": "CountValidLockContextEntities",
      "signature": "int CountValidLockContextEntities(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Counts all valid lock context entities in the global table\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call ProcessLockContextEntities with mode 1 (count mode)\n2. Return count of successfully validated entities\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nint - Count of successfully validated lock context entities (>= 0)\n\nWrapper Details:\nThis is a thunk wrapper for ProcessLockContextEntities(1) providing a\nsimplified interface for counting valid entities without exposing the\nmode parameter. Mode 1 iterates through g_ppLockContextTable, validates\nentities with active flags (0x83), and returns the success count.\n\nRelated Functions:\nProcessLockContextEntities() - Core implementation with mode parameter",
