      "name": "CloseAndCleanupDynamicStreams",
      "signature": "int CloseAndCleanupDynamicStreams(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Closes and cleans up dynamically allocated stream structures from the global stream table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire critical section index 2 for thread-safe access to stream table\n2. Iterate through stream entries starting at index 3 (skipping reserved slots 0-2)\n3. For each non-null stream entry:\n   a. Check if file flags have bits 0x83 set (read/write/error states)\n   b. If flags match, call ThreadSafeFileClose and increment closed count on success\n   c. For dynamic streams (index >= 20), also:\n      - Delete the embedded critical section at offset 0x20\n      - Deallocate the stream structure memory\n      - Clear the table entry to NULL\n4. Release critical section and return count of successfully closed files\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  int - Number of streams successfully closed (via ThreadSafeFileClose)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Indices 0-2: Reserved system streams, never processed\n  - Indices 3-19: Static streams, closed but not deallocated\n  - Indices 20+: Dynamic streams, fully cleaned up (close + delete CS + free memory)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x83 - File flag mask (read | write | error bits)\n  0x20 - Offset to embedded CRITICAL_SECTION in stream structure\n  2 - Critical section index protecting the stream table\n  3 - First non-reserved stream index\n  20 (0x14) - First dynamic stream index threshold\n\nStructure Layout (Stream Structure):\n  Offset  Size  Field              Type               Description\n  0x00    0x20  fileData           FILE               Standard C FILE structure\n  0x20    0x18  csLock             CRITICAL_SECTION   Thread synchronization",
