      "name": "InitializeCodePageLocale",
      "signature": "int InitializeCodePageLocale(int nCodePage)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Initializes character type lookup tables for a specific Windows code page.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Enter critical section 0x19 to synchronize access to global tables\n2. Resolve the code page identifier via ResolveCodePageIdentifier(nCodePage)\n3. If code page matches g_dwCachedCodePage, skip re-initialization (already loaded)\n4. If code page is 0 or invalid, handle error path\n5. For known code pages (0-5 predefined ranges), clear g_abCharacterTypeTable and load from\n   preset range tables at g_adwData_6fa9683c:\n   - Each range has start/end byte pairs that define character ranges\n   - Each byte range gets marked with flag bits (0x4 for lead bytes, 0x8 for trail bytes)\n6. For unknown code pages, call GetCPInfo API to retrieve lead byte ranges dynamically:\n   - Clear character type table\n   - Parse LeadByte pairs from CPINFO structure\n   - Mark all lead bytes with 0x4 flag, trail bytes with 0x8 flag\n   - Iterate 0x01-0xFF setting appropriate type flags\n7. Call MapCodePageIdentifier(nCodePage) to generate multi-byte handling properties\n8. Call InitializeCharacterTables() to finalize character tables\n9. Exit critical section and return 0 on success, -1 on failure\n\nParameters:\n   nCodePage (int): Windows code page identifier (932=Shift-JIS, 936=GBK, 949=Korean, etc.)\n\nReturns:\n   (int): 0 on success, -1 if code page not supported or initialization failed\n\nGlobal State Modified:\n   g_abCharacterTypeTable: 257-byte character classification array (index 0 unused)\n   g_dwCachedCodePage: Current code page cache\n   g_fMultiByteCodePage: Multi-byte character support flag (0=single-byte, 1=multi-byte)\n   g_dwCodePageProperties: Multi-byte table properties\n   g_adwEncodingParams[0-2]: Code page-specific encoding parameters\n\nCritical Sections:\n   Index 0x19: Protects against concurrent code page changes during table initialization\n\nDependencies:\n   ResolveCodePageIdentifier: Resolve code page to internal ID\n   MapCodePageIdentifier: Generate multi-byte table properties\n   InitializeCharacterTables: Post-initialization table setup\n   InitializeLocaleDataBuffers: Error recovery handler\n   GetCPInfo (Windows API): Retrieve code page info for dynamic initialization\n\nSpecial Cases:\n   - Code page 0: Error path (g_fCodePageInitialized check required)\n   - Preset code pages (0-5): Use g_adwData_6fa9683c tables instead of API\n   - Unknown code pages: Fall back to GetCPInfo API\n   - Single-byte vs multi-byte: g_fMultiByteCodePage determines trail byte handling",
