      "name": "DestroyAllUIControls",
      "signature": "int DestroyAllUIControls(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Destroys all UI controls in the global control array.\n\nThis function iterates through the global control list and calls DestroyUIControl on each control pointer, then clears the control count to zero.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load the control count from the global counter\n2. If count is zero or negative, skip to cleanup\n3. Initialize loop counter to zero and set control pointer to base of array\n4. Loop through each control in the array:\n   - Call DestroyUIControl with current control pointer\n   - Increment loop counter\n   - Advance control pointer by 4 bytes (sizeof pointer)\n   - Compare counter with total count\n   - Jump back to loop if more controls remain\n5. Clear the global control count to zero\n6. Return 1 (success status)\n\nReturns:\n1 on successful completion\n\nNotes:\nThe control array is stored at 0x6fa653c0 and the count is stored at 0x6fa65e34.\nEach array element is 4 bytes (a 32-bit pointer to a UI control structure).\nThe __stdcall convention means the caller cleans up the 4-byte return address.",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
