      "name": "SwapWordArrayBytes",
      "signature": "void SwapWordArrayBytes(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Swap bytes in each word of an array (endian conversion for word array)\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Initialize element_index counter to 0\\n2. Check if element_count is 0; if so, exit immediately\\n3. Loop through each element from 0 to element_count-1:\\n   a. Load word at [pWordArray + element_index*2] into DX:CX\\n   b. Swap bytes: high byte (CH) becomes DL, low byte (CL) becomes DH\\n   c. Increment element_index\\n   d. Write swapped word back to [pWordArray + (element_index-1)*2]\\n   e. Continue while element_index < element_count\\n4. Return to caller\\n\\nParameters:\\nESI: pWordArray - Base address of 16-bit word array (implicit register parameter)\\nEDI: element_count - Number of elements in array (implicit register parameter)\\n\\nReturns:\\nvoid - No return value, array modified in-place\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Empty array (element_count=0): Loop is skipped entirely\\n- Single element: One iteration swaps that element\\n- Array must be writable memory; read-only arrays will cause access violation\\n\\nNote: This function uses implicit register parameters (ESI and EDI) following a custom\\ncalling convention. ESI points to the word array base address, EDI contains the element\\ncount. The function modifies the array in-place by swapping the high and low bytes of\\neach 16-bit word, effectively converting between big-endian and little-endian formats.",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:aa02750a48a531ad710c82c13cc1414e65b66d0283991c00305c553cd6cf1c4f",
