      "comment": "ConvertFileTimeToUnixTime32 - Convert Windows FILETIME to 32-bit Unix timestamp\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call GetSystemTimeAsFileTime to obtain current Windows FILETIME (100-nanosecond intervals since 1601-01-01)\n2. Load FILETIME components: dwLowDateTime and dwHighDateTime from local stack\n3. Add epoch adjustment constant 0x2AC18000 to low DWORD with carry propagation\n4. Add epoch adjustment constant 0xFE624E21 to high DWORD plus carry flag\n5. Divide 64-bit adjusted FILETIME by 10,000,000 to convert 100-nanosecond intervals to seconds\n6. Check if output pointer pTimeOutput is non-null\n7. Store 32-bit Unix timestamp to *pTimeOutput if pointer is valid\n8. Return 32-bit Unix timestamp in EAX\n\nParameters:\n- pTimeOutput: Pointer to __time32_t to receive Unix timestamp, or NULL if only return value needed\n\nReturns:\n- 32-bit Unix timestamp representing seconds since 1970-01-01 00:00:00 UTC\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If pTimeOutput is NULL, function still returns timestamp without storing\n- Epoch adjustment constant 0xFE624E212AC18000 converts Windows epoch (1601) to Unix epoch (1970)\n- Division by 10,000,000 converts 100-nanosecond intervals to seconds\n- Uses __aulldiv for 64-bit unsigned division",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
