      "name": "AcquireSynchronizationLock",
      "signature": "void AcquireSynchronizationLock(void * pLockTarget)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Acquires a synchronization lock for either a custom lock or critical section.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load target address/pointer from function parameter\n2. Check if target is within custom lock array range (0x6fc408d8 to 0x6fc40b38)\n3a. If within custom lock range: calculate array index by subtracting base address and shifting right 5 bits (dividing by 32), add 0x10 offset, call __lock with calculated index\n3b. If outside custom range: treat as CRITICAL_SECTION pointer, add 0x20 offset for structure field, call EnterCriticalSection\n4. Return from function\n\nParameters:\npLockTarget - Target address for lock acquisition. Can be either custom lock address within range [0x6fc408d8, 0x6fc40b38] or CRITICAL_SECTION pointer outside range (offset by 0x20)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function returns after acquiring the appropriate lock type\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic constants 0x6fc408d8 (lock array base) and 0x6fc40b38 (upper bound) define custom lock range. Bit shift right 5 divides offset by 32 for array indexing. Lock array index offset by 0x10. CRITICAL_SECTION offset by 0x20 before Windows API call.\n\nLock Array Layout:\nOffset 0x408d8, Size 0x260 (total), Description: Custom lock array base\nElement: 32 bytes (stride per lock element)",
