      "name": "UnlockFileHandleIfNeeded",
      "signature": "void UnlockFileHandleIfNeeded(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Conditionally releases a file handle lock based on a caller stack flag.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Compare condition flag at [EBP-0x1c] with zero\\n2. If zero, jump to exit_skip_unlock and return without action\\n3. If non-zero, push file handle from [EBP-0x20] onto stack\\n4. Call __unlock_fhandle to release the file lock\\n5. Pop return address (callee cleanup)\\n6. Return to caller\\n\\nParameters:\\nImplicit stack frame parameters accessed via EBP-based offsets:\\n- [EBP-0x1c]: Condition flag (0=skip unlock, non-zero=perform unlock)\\n- [EBP-0x20]: File handle value to unlock\\n\\nReturns:\\nvoid - No return value; operation is for side effects only\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Condition flag at [EBP-0x1c] allows skipping unlock entirely if false\\n- File handle from [EBP-0x20] is pushed as parameter to __unlock_fhandle\\n- Uses __stdcall calling convention (callee cleans stack with PUSH/POP)\\n- Typically called from error cleanup paths in file open operations",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11",
