      "name": "DispatchGameUICommand",
      "signature": "void DispatchGameUICommand(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Dispatches a game UI command by preparing registers and calling the command processor.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 8 bytes on stack for command buffer (2 DWORDs)\n2. Store EAX (command code) at [ESP + 4] offset\n3. Store ECX (parameter) at [ESP] offset\n4. Call ProcessGameUICommand with buffer address in ECX\n5. Clean up stack and return\n\nParameters:\n- EAX (implicit): Command code (0x14-0x17, etc.) indicating which UI action to process\n- ECX (implicit): Parameter value, typically 0 (cleared with XOR before call)\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value, function is a void wrapper\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function is called multiple times from FUN_6fa4eab0 with different command codes in EAX\n- ECX is always cleared (XOR ECX,ECX) before each call\n- Stack buffer provides temporary storage for command parameters\n- Calling convention is __stdcall (RET after ADD ESP,0x8)\n\nStructure Layout:\nStack buffer layout (8 bytes total):\n  Offset  Size  Field Name     Type  Description\n  +0      4     param1         dword Parameter value (ECX)\n  +4      4     commandCode    dword Command code (EAX)",
