      "name": "ValidateNetworkInitializationAndCleanup",
      "signature": "void ValidateNetworkInitializationAndCleanup(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Validates network/Battle.Net initialization state and performs cleanup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load initialization flag from DAT_6fa656c0\n2. Test if flag is zero (not yet initialized)\n3. If uninitialized (EQ path):\n   a. Call GetReturnAddress(0x77) to get stack frame return address\n   b. Call CleanupAndAbort with error message \"Can't connect to Battle.Net\"\n   c. Call _exit(-1) to terminate process (non-returning)\n4. If already initialized (JNZ path):\n   a. Call InitializeCleanupForEntryPoint to register cleanup handlers\n   b. Clear initialization flag at DAT_6fa656c0 = 0\n   c. Clear related global at DAT_6fa656c4 = 0\n   d. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone (void function, __stdcall calling convention)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function either returns normally (if initialized) or terminates process\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic number 0x77 passed to GetReturnAddress likely encodes stack frame depth\n- Function does NOT return if initialization check fails (_exit is non-returning)\n- Two global DWORDs must be cleared atomically before returning\n- Error message comes from hardcoded string at 0x6fa5e256 with offset +0x2e",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
