      "name": "InitializeBattleNetClient",
      "signature": "int InitializeBattleNetClient(void * this, void * pGameState)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initialize Battle.Net client connection by loading Bnclient.dll and obtaining interface pointer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate that pGameState pointer is not NULL; if NULL, call cleanup and abort\n2. Check if Battle.Net client is already initialized at offset +0x221\n3. If not initialized:\n   a. Load Bnclient.dll using LoadLibraryA\n   b. If load fails, get error code via GetLastError, format error message, show MessageBox, return 0\n   c. Call GetProcAddress to locate QueryInterface function in loaded DLL\n   d. If QueryInterface not found, get error code, format error message, show MessageBox, return 0\n   e. Call QueryInterface function to obtain interface pointer\n   f. Store interface pointer in two locations: global DAT_6fa656c4 and pGameState[0x221]\n   g. Call interface initialization method (dereference pointer at offset 0)\n4. Return 1 to indicate success\n\nParameters:\n  pGameState: Pointer to game state structure containing Battle.Net initialization flag at offset +0x221\n\nReturns:\n  1 - Battle.Net client successfully initialized or already initialized\n  0 - Failed to load Bnclient.dll or QueryInterface function\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Function uses implicit ECX register (thiscall convention) for pGameState\n  - If pGameState is NULL, function calls cleanup/abort (never returns normally)\n  - Error messages shown to user via MessageBox for DLL load and QueryInterface failures\n  - Magic offset 0x221 indicates specific field in game state structure",
