      "name": "CheckAndInitializeRenderingState",
      "signature": "int CheckAndInitializeRenderingState(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Checks and initializes the rendering state based on system conditions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call virtual function at offset 0xa0 to check rendering state\n2. If result is non-zero, initialize rendering system\n3. Check if initialization flag is zero and call virtual function at offset 0x68\n4. If that function returns non-zero AND game execution is disabled, return 1\n5. Call virtual function at offset 0x10 (cleanup/reset function)\n6. Call final rendering initialization\n7. Return 1 (success status)\n\nParameters:\n(implicit) - No explicit parameters, operates on global game state\n\nReturns:\nint - Always returns 1 (success status)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Early exit when initialization flag (0x6fa65ea0) is already set\n- Conditional execution based on game execution enabled flag (0x6fa65e60)\n- Virtual function calls through vtable at 0x6fa656c4\n- Magic values: offsets 0xa0, 0x68, 0x10 are vtable function pointers",
