      "name": "DispatchGameCommand",
      "signature": "int DispatchGameCommand(int commandCode, int param2)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Main game command dispatcher and state machine orchestrator.\n\nManages game initialization, UI command processing, and state transitions based on\ncommand codes and execution context. Handles BattleNet UI initialization, game session\nmanagement, and command dispatch for various game modes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if game engine is initialized (call function ptr at DAT_6fa656c4+0x68)\n2. If not initialized, dispatch BattleNet UI initialization and exit\n3. If already started (DAT_6fa65ea4 != 0), return early\n4. Initialize game UI subsystem and begin command processing\n5. Branch on commandCode parameter:\n   - commandCode == 0: Enter alternate command path with additional state checking\n   - commandCode != 0: Process specific command dispatch table (codes 2-8)\n6. Clear game state registers (offsets +0xa1 to +0xb5, 6 dwords total)\n7. Queue final rendering and check for error conditions\n8. If post-game initialization enabled, execute callback dispatcher and session cleanup\n9. Send final command code 0x12 to game UI command processor\n\nParameters:\n  int commandCode - Game state/command identifier (0=init, 1=resume, 2-8=game modes)\n  int param2 - Execution flag or additional command parameter\n\nReturns:\n  int - Status code (0=success/continue, 1=initialized/complete)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  * Magic numbers: 0x12 = final init command, 0x68/0x28/0x60 = function dispatch offsets\n  * State registers cleared at offsets +0xa1,+0xa5,+0xa9,+0xad,+0xb1,+0xb5 from base\n  * Early exit if DAT_6fa65ea4 is already set (prevents double initialization)\n  * Multiple rendering queue callbacks at different code paths (0x6fa4e450, 0x6fa4e400, etc)\n  * Unaffected register EDI contains base context pointer for state structure access",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
