      "name": "IsValidRenderMessageType",
      "signature": "uint IsValidRenderMessageType(uint messageType)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Validates if a message/state type code is in the render system's valid set.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Subtract 2 from input value to normalize range\\n2. Check if normalized value exceeds 0x7d (125)\\n3. If out of range, return 0 (invalid)\\n4. Use normalized value as index into lookup table\\n5. Load byte from lookup table at base 0x6fa518c8\\n6. If byte is non-zero, jump to that offset and return 1\\n7. Return 0 if lookup value is zero\\n\\nParameters:\\n  messageType (EAX): Message/state code to validate\\n\\nReturns:\\n  EAX = 1 if messageType is valid (2,10,11,12,13,126,127), 0 otherwise\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n  - Uses compact lookup table dispatch for space efficiency\\n  - Input range: 0-127 (after ADD EAX,-2 adjustment)\\n  - Valid codes: 2, 10, 11, 12, 13, 126, 127\\n  - Magic offset value: 0x6fa518c8 (lookup table)\\n  - Magic jump table base: 0x6fa518c0",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:7434bd14af7657e748d303431f4b3c342e3e5ed27d3a1d1018e76c79f8a501ff",
