      "name": "SetGameModeFlag",
      "signature": "void SetGameModeFlag(char modeCommand)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Sets game mode flag based on input command code.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Load global game state pointer from DAT_6fa65abc\\n2. Store input command code at offset +0x1ea\\n3. Clear all 7 mode flag bytes (offsets 0x81-0x87)\\n4. Based on command value (0-6), set exactly one corresponding flag byte to 1\\n5. Return (no return value, void)\\n\\nParameters:\\n- modeCommand: char - Command code (0-6) specifying which mode flag to set\\n\\nReturns:\\n  void - No return value\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Command 0: Clears all flags then sets byte at offset 0x81\\n- Commands 1-6: Each sets a unique flag byte (0x83, 0x84, 0x82, 0x85, 0x86, 0x87)\\n- Any command >= 7 results in all flags being cleared with none set\\n\\nStructure Layout:\\nUsed with global state structure accessed via DAT_6fa65abc:\\nOffset  Size  Field Name         Type      Description\\n0x81    1     modeFlag_0         byte      Mode 0 active flag\\n0x82    1     modeFlag_3         byte      Mode 3 active flag\\n0x83    1     modeFlag_1         byte      Mode 1 active flag\\n0x84    1     modeFlag_2         byte      Mode 2 active flag\\n0x85    1     modeFlag_4         byte      Mode 4 active flag\\n0x86    1     modeFlag_5         byte      Mode 5 active flag\\n0x87    1     modeFlag_6         byte      Mode 6 active flag\\n0x1ea   1     lastModeCommand    byte      Last command code received",
