      "comment": "Checks character code and sets global configuration flag\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Verify input parameter is valid (eax_statusCode != -1)\n2. Load first byte from character code string parameter\n3. Subtract 0xAF from byte value to normalize codes\n4. If normalized value equals 0 (original byte 0xAF), set flag to 1 (enabled)\n5. If normalized value equals 1 (original byte 0xB0), set flag to 0 (disabled)\n6. Otherwise, leave flag unchanged and return\n\nParameters:\n- pCharCode: Pointer to character code string buffer\n\nReturns:\n- void: No return value, modifies global DAT_6fa65e7c flag\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If eax_statusCode == -1, function returns without modifying flag\n- Character codes 0xAF and 0xB0 trigger flag modification\n- Any other character code leaves flag unchanged\n- Global flag DAT_6fa65e7c: 1 = enabled, 0 = disabled",
