      "name": "DecodeFlagsToPriority",
      "signature": "uchar DecodeFlagsToPriority(uchar flagsValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "char",
      "comment": "Decode bit flags into a priority value.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Test bit 0 (0x01) - if set, return priority 7 (highest)\\n2. Test sign bit (0x80) - if set, return priority 6\\n3. Test bit 4 (0x10) - if set, return priority 5\\n4. Test bit 3 (0x08) - if set, return priority 4\\n5. Test bit 6 (0x40) - if set, return priority 3\\n6. Test bit 2 (0x04) - if set, return priority 2, else return priority 1\\n7. Return priority value in AL\\n\\nParameters:\\n  flagsValue (unsigned char in AL): Bit flags to decode\\n    - Bit 0 (0x01): Priority 7 flag\\n    - Bit 1 (0x02): Priority 2 flag\\n    - Bit 2 (0x04): Priority 2 flag\\n    - Bit 3 (0x08): Priority 4 flag\\n    - Bit 4 (0x10): Priority 5 flag\\n    - Bit 6 (0x40): Priority 3 flag\\n    - Bit 7 (0x80): Sign flag for Priority 6\\n\\nReturns:\\n  unsigned char: Priority value (1-7)\\n    - 7: Highest priority (bit 0 set)\\n    - 6: Sign bit set (0x80)\\n    - 5: Bit 4 set (0x10)\\n    - 4: Bit 3 set (0x08)\\n    - 3: Bit 6 set (0x40)\\n    - 2: Bit 2 set (0x04)\\n    - 1: Default/low priority (no flags set)\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n  - Only one flag is typically active at a time; priority reflects first matching bit\\n  - Evaluation order ensures deterministic results with priority precedence\\n  - Return values 1-7 encode priority levels for use in scheduling or queue ordering",
