      "name": "RenderUITextWithValidation",
      "signature": "void RenderUITextWithValidation(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Renders UI text with multi-stage validation and coordinate synchronization.\nThis function manages the rendering of text in UI controls by validating window\ndimensions and coordinates through a series of comparison loops. It fetches three\ncoordinate/dimension values and performs iterative rendering until all values\nsynchronize within acceptable ranges.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Fetch initial window value 1 from global state via ValidateAndGetWindowData()\n2. Fetch initial window value 2 from global state via ValidateAndGetWindowData()\n3. Fetch initial window value 3 from global state via ValidateAndGetWindowData()\n4. Loop A: While value3 &lt; value2, render text and re-fetch value3\n5. Loop B: While value2 &lt; value3, render text and re-fetch value2\n6. Loop C: While value2 &lt; value1, render text twice and re-fetch value2\n7. Loop D: While value1 &lt; value2, render text and re-fetch value1\n8. Render final sequence: three consecutive text renders (cleanup/flush)\n9. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone. All state accessed via global pointers at 0x6fa65e50, 0x6fa65e48, 0x6fa65e4c.\n\nReturns:\nvoid. Function produces side effects via RenderTextInUIControl() calls.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Value synchronization loops ensure coordinates converge before final render\n- Multiple RenderTextInUIControl() calls per iteration allow for partial rendering\n- Final three-render sequence may represent buffer flush or multi-layer rendering",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
