      "name": "UpdateUITextRenderingAndValidate",
      "signature": "void UpdateUITextRenderingAndValidate(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Updates UI text rendering and validates window data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize render iteration counter to 50 (0x32)\n2. Loop 50 times, calling RenderTextInUIControl() for each iteration to render text elements\n3. After completing the render loop, call RenderTextInUIControl() one additional time for final UI update\n4. Call ValidateAndGetWindowData() to validate window state and retrieve window data\n5. Store the validation result in global variable DAT_6fa65e58\n6. Return to caller\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No direct return value; window validation result stored in global DAT_6fa65e58\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- The render loop executes exactly 50 times before the final additional render call\n- Window data validation occurs after all rendering is complete\n- Uses __stdcall convention with callee stack cleanup (RET 0x0)",
