      "name": "InitializeModuleArray",
      "signature": "int InitializeModuleArray(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes module array by validating and initializing each module entry.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if module array base pointer (DAT_6fa65e74) is initialized\n2. Load array size from DAT_6fa65e78\n3. For each module index (0 to array_size-1):\n   a. Load module pointer from array[index]\n   b. Validate module pointer is non-NULL (error if NULL)\n   c. Check if module+0x4 field is initialized (error if NULL)\n   d. Call InitializeModule with ordinal 0x1121 and parameter 0\n   e. Load and validate module pointer from array again\n   f. Check if module[0] field is non-NULL (error if NULL)\n   g. Call InitializeModule with ordinal 0x1123 and parameter 0\n   h. Call InitializeModule with ordinal 0x1125 and parameter 0\n   i. Reload array base pointer for next iteration\n4. Call InitializeModule with ordinal 0x1128 (final initialization)\n5. Clear module array base pointer to NULL\n6. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nint - Always returns 1 (success code)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If module array is not initialized, function returns 1 without processing\n- Errors trigger GetReturnAddress to get stack frame info, then CleanupAndAbort\n- Error codes: 0x1120 (module pointer NULL), 0x1122 (module[0] NULL)\n- DAT_6fa65e74 is a global array base pointer (modified/cleared at end)\n- DAT_6fa65e78 is global array element count\n- InitializeModule is called with module-specific ordinals for initialization phases\n\nData Structure:\nModule structure (accessed via array[index]):\nOffset  Size  Field Name              Type    Description\n+0x0    4     module_pointer          void*   Main module pointer/data\n+0x4    4     initialization_flag     int     Non-zero if initialized",
