      "comment": "Counts occurrences of dashes and underscores in a character buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize character count (EAX) to 0\n2. Initialize buffer index (EDX) to 0\n3. Check if buffer length (EDI) is greater than 0\n4. If length <= 0, skip loop and return count\n5. For each character in buffer:\n   a. Load byte from buffer at offset [EDX + ESI]\n   b. Compare byte to 0x2d (dash '-') character\n   c. If equal, jump to char_matched label\n   d. Compare byte to 0x5f (underscore '_') character\n   e. If not equal, skip increment and continue\n   f. At char_matched: increment character count (EAX)\n   g. At loop_continue: increment buffer index (EDX)\n   h. Compare buffer index (EDX) to buffer length (EDI)\n   i. If index < length, continue loop (JL back to loop_start)\n6. Return character count in EAX\n\nParameters:\n  pBuffer - pointer to character buffer (passed in ESI register)\n  nLength - length of buffer to scan (passed in EDI register)\n\nReturns:\n  int - count of dash and underscore characters found in buffer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Magic numbers: 0x2d (dash), 0x5f (underscore), 0x0 (empty/no chars)\n  Empty buffer: nLength <= 0 returns 0\n  Single character: still counts if it matches dash or underscore\n  Used by ValidateObjectName to enforce naming conventions where\n  at most 1 dash or underscore is allowed in object names\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Function uses character-by-character scanning pattern with\n  early termination when all characters are checked. The validation\n  constraint (count < 2) means names can have 0 or 1 special character.",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
