      "name": "ValidateIdentifierFormat",
      "signature": "int ValidateIdentifierFormat(undefined4 pUnicodeSource, int bStrictMode, char * pFirstChar)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Validates identifier format according to naming rules.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract first character from input string\n2. Check if first character is alphabetic (a-z or A-Z)\n3. If not alphabetic, check if it's dash(-) or underscore(_)\n4. If dash/underscore and bStrictMode==0, reject (return 0)\n5. If bStrictMode!=0, convert Unicode source to UTF-8 buffer\n6. Iterate through converted string checking for dashes/underscores\n7. Reject if any dash/underscore found in strict mode\n8. Return 1 if all checks pass, 0 on any validation failure\n\nParameters:\npUnicodeSource: Unicode string object containing identifier source\nbStrictMode: Flag (0=allow dash/underscore in first char, non-0=strict validation of entire string)\npFirstChar: Pointer to first character of identifier string to validate\n\nReturns:\n1: Identifier format is valid\n0: Identifier format is invalid (contains disallowed characters)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
