      "name": "FindAndNavigateListItem",
      "signature": "int FindAndNavigateListItem(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Searches through a collection of items and navigates to first item with specific field value.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize item index counter to 0\n2. Check if item count (DAT_6fa65e30) is valid (>= 0)\n3. Loop through array at DAT_6fa652b8, accessing 4-byte elements indexed by counter\n4. Call GetFirstFieldOrNull() on each item to retrieve field value\n5. If field value equals 4, exit loop with found item in currentItem\n6. Otherwise increment counter and continue loop until counter exceeds total count\n7. If valid item found (currentItem != 0), call ValidateAndGetWindowData() and NavigateListByIndex()\n8. Return 1 to indicate success\n9. If no valid item found, retrieve error return address via GetReturnAddress(0xce6)\n10. Call CleanupAndAbort() with error message and return address\n11. Call _exit(-1) to terminate application\n\nParameters:\n(none) - Function accesses global state through DAT_6fa65e30 (item count) and DAT_6fa652b8 (item array)\n\nReturns:\nReturns 1 if valid list item found and processed successfully\nNever returns on error - calls _exit(-1) to terminate application\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Error code 0xce6 indicates connectivity failure (Battle.net connection)\n- Field value 4 is the target sentinel that indicates list item validity\n- If item count DAT_6fa65e30 is negative, function immediately aborts\n- Array access uses stride of 4 bytes per element (32-bit pointers or integers)",
