      "name": "IsValidCharacter",
      "signature": "bool IsValidCharacter(undefined4 param_1, undefined4 param_2, char * pCharString)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Validates a character for use in identifiers or pathnames.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load character from input string pointer\n2. Check if character is in reserved set (quotes, special chars) using dispatch table\n3. If reserved, return false\n4. If character <= space (0x20), return false\n5. If character >= DEL (0x7f), return false\n6. Otherwise return true for valid ASCII printable\n\nParameters:\nparam_1: Unused context parameter\nparam_2: Unused context parameter\npCharString: Pointer to character string to validate\n\nReturns:\ntrue if character is valid for identifiers (printable ASCII, not reserved)\nfalse if character is reserved, control, or non-ASCII\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Reserved characters: \" # % * , / < > ? \\\n- Space (0x20) and DEL (0x7f) are invalid\n- Only allows ASCII range 0x21-0x7e",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
