      "name": "InitializeGameIntroduction",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameIntroduction(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes game introduction sequence with video playback and Diablo II configuration\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x188 bytes of stack space for buffers\n2. Call FUN_6fa51cb0 to perform preliminary initialization\n3. Validate game state requirements via ValidateGameStateRequirements()\n4. Load configuration pointers based on validation result:\n   - If validation succeeds (result == 0): use DAT_6fa5e1f0/DAT_6fa5e1f4 (valid config)\n   - If validation fails (result != 0): use DAT_6fa5e1e8/DAT_6fa5e1ec (fallback config), set statusCode to 0x2\n5. Call GetOperationDataByType() to initialize operation context\n6. Format video file path using sprintf with template \"s_video__s_D2x_Intro__s_bik\"\n7. Attempt to open and validate game file via OpenAndValidateGameFile()\n8. If file opened successfully:\n   - Call ReleaseFileHandleWithRefCount() to clean up file handle\n9. If file open failed:\n   - Format alternate path using sprintf with template \"s_video__s_D2x_Intro_s_bik\"\n10. Call CallGraphicsVtableWithParam_0x38() with statusCode parameter for graphics initialization\n11. Read Diablo II configuration from \"Diablo II\" registry/config key\n12. Parse configuration values via _sscanf() if key exists\n13. Apply OR mask 0x80 to option value for configuration flag\n14. Format final configuration with magic values (0xd8, 0x94, 0xf6) via sprintf\n15. Write Diablo II configuration to \"Aux Battle.net\" location\n16. Return after adding 0x188 bytes (stack cleanup handled by callee via RET 0x188)\n\nParameters:\nNone - This function takes no parameters\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value. Modifies global game state and configuration.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic configuration values: 0xd8, 0x94, 0xf6, 0x80 (bitwise OR mask)\n- Configuration validation determines which set of global pointers to use\n- File open failure is handled gracefully with alternate video file path\n- Registry/config key lookup may return NULL; _sscanf() handles missing config data",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
