      "name": "ParseBattleNetVersion",
      "signature": "byte ParseBattleNetVersion(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "byte",
      "comment": "Parses Battle.net version configuration from system settings.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calls system function to retrieve Battle.net configuration path/status\n2. If configuration exists (non-zero result), proceeds to parse version string\n3. Sets up stack buffers and initializes parsing parameters with default values\n4. Calls sscanf to parse a version string in format \"%d.%d.%d.%d\" (4 decimal numbers)\n5. Extracts parsing result from stack variable at offset +0x18\n6. Tests bit 0x10 in the parsing result for validity\n7. If valid, returns inverted byte value shifted right by 7 bits (extracts a flag bit)\n8. If invalid or configuration missing, returns 0\n\nParameters:\nNone - function takes no explicit parameters\n\nReturns:\nbyte - 0 if configuration not found or parsing failed; otherwise returns (~result >> 7) & 0xFF\n       extracting a specific bit flag from the sscanf result\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Default Battle.net name is \"Aux Battle.net\" if not configured\n- Default game name is \"Diablo II\" if not configured\n- Version buffer is 100 bytes, allowing for extended version strings\n- Parsing checks for 0x10 bit set, indicating successful version parse operation\n- Return value range is 0-1 depending on extracted flag bit",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:d905bfc2d0065604a81f08218a0f5809876a826c93ee6795702f7015b436dae9",
