      "name": "InitializeNetworkConnections",
      "signature": "uint InitializeNetworkConnections(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes network connections for Diablo II.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Allocate 100-byte buffer on stack for formatted configuration data\\n2. Call external function at 0x1018bca0 to check/initialize network state\\n3. If initialization fails (non-zero return), return 1 (error status)\\n4. Format data using sprintf with magic numbers (0xd8, 0x94, 0xf6, 0x22)\\n5. Call external function at 0x1018be10 to configure network connections\\n6. Return 0 (success status)\\n\\nParameters:\\nNone - function takes no parameters\\n\\nReturns:\\nuint - Returns 0 on successful network initialization, 1 if initial check failed\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Magic numbers 0xd8, 0x94, 0xf6, 0x22 are version or configuration identifiers\\n- Stack buffer size of 100 bytes fixed for formatted configuration string\\n- External functions at 0x1018bca0 and 0x1018be10 are likely ordinal imports\\n- String constants \\\"Diablo II\\\" and \\\"Aux Battle.net\\\" indicate dual-mode network support\\n\\nStack Layout:\\n- Offset 0x0 to 0x63 (100 bytes): formatBuffer for configuration data\\n- Offset 0x64: Calling function return address",
