      "name": "InitializePaletteFileAndTables",
      "signature": "int InitializePaletteFileAndTables(char * paletteVariant)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes palette and color lookup tables from data files.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set global initialization flag to 1\n2. Format base palette file path using wsprintfA\n3. Format variant-specific palette file path with parameter\n4. Compare formatted paths using byte-by-byte string comparison (23 bytes)\n5. Store comparison result (1=match, 0=mismatch) in global flag\n6. Load and initialize palette and color tables from both paths\n7. Return success status\n\nParameters:\n- paletteVariant: Palette variant identifier string (e.g., \"sky\", \"fechar\")\n\nReturns:\n- int: Always returns 1 (success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- String comparison is exact 23-byte match (REP CMPSB with count 0x17)\n- Global flags 0x6fa65e5c and 0x6fa65ad8 track initialization state\n- Path strings are formatted using global data directory prefix\n- Both base and variant paths are passed to InitializePaletteAndColorTables",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
