      "name": "InitializeGameResourceCleanup",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameResourceCleanup(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Systematically releases all game resources and performs cleanup operations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Release 15 primary resource groups by loading ECX from global references and calling ReleaseResourceAndNotify\n2. Call FindAndValidateD2ExpMpq to validate expansion pack presence\n3. If expansion is present, release 4 additional expansion-related resources\n4. Release 26 more resource groups covering core game objects and caches\n5. If DAT_6fa65c10 flag is set:\n   - Call ReleaseResourceAndNotify for special resource\n   - Clear DAT_6fa65c10 flag to zero\n   - Release 2 additional resources\n   - Iterate through 7 arrays of resources (pointers at 0x6fa65cf4, 0x6fa65d08, 0x6fa65d1c, 0x6fa65d30, 0x6fa65d44, 0x6fa65d88, 0x6fa65d74), releasing each item\n   - Release 2 more resources\n   - Call FindAndValidateD2ExpMpq again for second validation\n   - If second validation succeeds, iterate through 2 more arrays (0x6fa65ccc, 0x6fa65ce0) releasing resources\n   - Release final resource\n6. Release final 6 resource groups to complete cleanup\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value; all operations for side effect\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- DAT_6fa65c10 is a feature flag that gates additional cleanup operations\n- Multiple validation checks for expansion pack affect which resources are released\n- Array iteration uses stride of 4 bytes (pointer-sized), typical for object arrays\n- All release operations use ECX as implicit parameter register\n\nCalled By:\nInitialization/cleanup sequences during game startup or shutdown",
