      "name": "CheckGameSyncState",
      "signature": "byte CheckGameSyncState(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "byte",
      "comment": "Checks the current game synchronization state and waits for sync events.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if sync flag (DAT_6fa65e80) is set; return 1 if already synchronized\n2. Get the sync event handle via GetSyncEventHandleOrStatus()\n3. If handle is valid, call GetSyncEventHandleOrStatus() again to get the actual handle\n4. Wait for the sync event using WaitForSingleObject(handle, 0) with zero timeout\n5. If wait returns WAIT_OBJECT_0 (success), call GetCurrentGameState() and process result\n6. Call FUN_6fa518a0() to validate state; return 2 OR'd with state validity (0 or 2)\n7. If wait returns WAIT_TIMEOUT (0x102), return 3 for timeout state\n8. If initial handle check fails, return 2 for error state\n\nReturns:\n1 - Sync already set/connected\n2 - Sync error or wait failed\n3 - Wait timeout on sync event\n0 or 2 - Determined by FUN_6fa518a0() validation (0=valid, 2=invalid)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- DAT_6fa65e80 being non-zero indicates the game is already synchronized\n- GetSyncEventHandleOrStatus() returns 0 for invalid sync state\n- WaitForSingleObject timeout (0x102) indicates event not signaled within deadline\n- Final logic (NEG EAX; SBB EAX,EAX; AND EAX,0x2) converts validation result to 0 or 2",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
