      "name": "InitializeGameUIAndCommands",
      "signature": "uint InitializeGameUIAndCommands(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes game UI controls and processes 6 critical game commands sequentially.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load sky palette and destroy existing UI control widget\n2. Validate command array counter < 0x40 (64 max commands)\n3. Process first game command (address 0x6fa641f0) and store result\n4. Set processed command as current event target\n5. Process second game command (address 0x6fa641c0) and store result\n6. Process third game command (address 0x6fa64160) and store result\n7. Call dispatch_command_handler() to apply command changes\n8. Render UI text in display box\n9. Process fourth game command (address 0x6fa64190) and store result\n10. If TCP/IP string empty, initialize Diablo II TCP/IP settings\n11. Convert stored string to Unicode and process for display\n12. Set processed command as active UI control\n13. Handle double-click text input events\n14. Process fifth game command (address 0x6fa64220) and store result\n15. Set global game state from fifth command result\n16. Process sixth game command (address 0x6fa64250) and store result\n17. Return 1 on success\n\nReturns:\n1 = All commands successfully initialized\nDoes not return = Error: command array overflow or failure (calls _exit(-1))\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Buffer size: 0x40 (64) maximum commands. Exceeding triggers error exit.\n- TCP/IP string: Only initialized if DAT_6fa65ae0 is empty (null/zero)\n- All ProcessGameCommand calls may fail; failures cascade to error handler\n- Function does not return on error path (calls _exit(-1))\n\nStructure Layout:\nCommand Array @ 0x6fa653c0\nOffset    Size  Field Name              Type      Description\n0x0       4     commandArray[0-63]      uint      Game command results stored as 4-byte values\n0x100     4     currentCommand          uint      Latest processed command handle\n0x104     4     tcpString[256]          char[256] TCP/IP connection string buffer",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
