      "name": "PrepareScreenshotSlotWithGatewayInfo",
      "signature": "void PrepareScreenshotSlotWithGatewayInfo(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Prepares screenshot slot initialization with formatted gateway information.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Get window data provider from global pointer at [DAT_6fa656c4 + 0x98]\\n2. Call window data function to obtain current window/gateway data structure\\n3. Extract gateway name from window data using BNGatewayAccess::Name\\n4. Extract name length from window data at offset +0xc\\n5. Copy gateway name bytes to local buffer using CopyMemoryWithAlignment\\n6. Initialize three Unicode string buffers (256 chars each):\\n   - unicodeGatewayName: for converted gateway name\\n   - commandHandlerResult: for command handler response\\n   - formattedDisplayString: for final sprintf output\\n7. Convert gateway name from ANSI to Unicode using Unicode::toUnicode\\n8. Call dispatch_command_handler to get current command/handler text\\n9. Copy command handler result to commandHandlerResult using Unicode::strcpy\\n10. Clear formattedDisplayString buffer (64 dwords = 256 bytes)\\n11. Format string using Unicode::sprintf: sprintf(formattedDisplayString, commandHandlerResult, unicodeGatewayName)\\n12. Convert entire formattedDisplayString to uppercase:\\n    - Get string length using Unicode::strlen\\n    - Loop through each character (ESI = 0 to length-1)\\n    - For each character with value < 0x100, look up uppercase equivalent in _toUpperTable_exref\\n    - Store converted character back to buffer\\n13. Call InitializeScreenshotSlotWithValidation with formattedDisplayString and parameter 0\\n\\nReturns:\\nvoid - No return value, function initializes screenshot slot state as side effect\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- String length obtained via Unicode::strlen called multiple times in loop\\n- Uppercase table _toUpperTable_exref only used for characters < 0x100\\n- Characters >= 0x100 (extended Unicode) passed through unchanged\\n- Window data function pointer is dereferenced from global at [DAT_6fa656c4 + 0x98]\\n- All Unicode strings are 16-bit (2 bytes per character)\\n- Final formatted string passed to InitializeScreenshotSlotWithValidation for rendering/validation",
