      "comment": "Initializes the Battle.net UI by clearing existing controls and creating 4 new command-based UI elements.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Iterate through existing UI control array and destroy all controls\n2. Reset control counter to 0\n3. Create 4 new UI controls by processing game commands:\n   - Command 0x6fa63740 (main interface)\n   - Command 0x6fa61a00 (first secondary)\n   - Command 0x6fa61a30 (second secondary)\n   - Command 0x6fa637d0 (third secondary)\n4. Store each control handle in the control array and set bit flags\n5. Render UI text boxes with dispatch_command_handler calls (x2)\n6. Return success, or call CleanupAndAbort if capacity exceeded (max 4 controls = 0x40 limit)\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Initializes global UI state or terminates on error\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Array capacity is hardcoded as 0x40 (64 slots)\n- Only first 4 controls are created in success path\n- Error path calls _exit(-1) if capacity check fails\n- Global counter DAT_6fa65e34 tracks active control count",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
