      "name": "InitializeUIControls",
      "signature": "void InitializeUIControls(int param)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes three primary UI controls from game command tables.\\n\\nThis function is responsible for setting up the main user interface elements. It first destroys any previously created controls, then creates three new controls in sequence from different command configuration tables (0x6fa638c0, 0x6fa61a60, 0x6fa637d0). Each control is added to the control array, has its entity flags modified, and is integrated into the event dispatch system.\\n\\nThe function also dispatches initial render commands to display the text box UI elements. If insufficient space exists for all three controls (array capacity is 0x40 = 64 elements), the function aborts with error message.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Loop through existing controls in array and destroy each one (if any exist)\\n2. Reset control count to 0\\n3. Create first UI control from table 1 (0x6fa638c0), store in array[0], set as event target\\n4. Modify first control's entity bit flags with value 1\\n5. Check if array has space for second control (count < 0x40)\\n6. Create second UI control from table 2 (0x6fa61a60), store in array[1]\\n7. Modify second control's entity bit flags with value 1\\n8. Check if array has space for third control (count < 0x40)\\n9. Create third UI control from table 3 (0x6fa637d0), store in array[2]\\n10. Modify third control's entity bit flags with value 1\\n11. Dispatch command 0x1430 with null parameters and render text box\\n12. Select second command ID based on parameter: 0x5578 if param != 0, else 0x1431\\n13. Dispatch second command with selected ID and render text box\\n14. If overflow occurs at any capacity check, abort with error message\\n\\nParameters:\\n- param (int): Conditional parameter used to select control ID for second text box display (0x5578 if non-zero, 0x1431 if zero). Purpose unclear from code context.\\n\\nReturns:\\n- void: No return value. Function either completes normally or aborts on error.\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Error condition: If control count exceeds 0x40 (64) capacity, calls CleanupAndAbort with error message pointing to Battle.Net connection error string at offset 0x2e, then exits with status -1\\n- Array capacity: Hard-coded maximum of 0x40 controls\\n- Control tables: Three command tables at fixed addresses (0x6fa638c0, 0x6fa61a60, 0x6fa637d0)\\n\\nGlobal Data Accessed:\\n- DAT_6fa65e34: Control count (incremented as controls created, reset to 0 at start)\\n- DAT_6fa653c0: Control array base address (stores up to 64 control pointers)\\n- DAT_6fa638c0: Command table 1 for first control\\n- DAT_6fa61a60: Command table 2 for second control\\n- DAT_6fa637d0: Command table 3 for third control\\\"",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:bfada389fcea39e1b5cdb89e36937898841ac9294510d85dfe3ba18823e5014f",
