      "name": "DispatchStateChange",
      "signature": "uint DispatchStateChange(int pStateObject)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Dispatches a state change event by extracting a handler pointer and invoking it.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load pStateObject parameter from stack (ESP + 4)\n2. Extract handler function pointer from pStateObject + 0xc offset\n3. Push event parameters: ESI (cleared/0), magic number 0x1408, magic number 0xfab, handler pointer\n4. Call FUN_6fa521b0 with the pushed parameters\n5. Return 1 (success indicator)\n\nParameters:\npStateObject (int): Pointer to state object containing handler pointer at offset +0xc\n\nReturns:\nuint: Always returns 1 (success indicator)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic numbers 0x1408 (5128) and 0xfab (4011) appear to be event type codes or timing constants\n- ESI is explicitly cleared (XOR ESI,ESI) before being pushed, possibly for flags or mode parameter\n- Handler pointer is extracted from offset +0xc of the state object structure\n\nStructure Layout:\nThe pStateObject structure contains at least:\nOffset  Size  Field       Type    Description\n0x0c    4     handler     int *   Function pointer to event handler",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
