      "name": "ProcessGameStateTransition",
      "signature": "int ProcessGameStateTransition(int * pStateData)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Processes game state transitions and manages entity/UI control updates.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate MPQ expansion file access via FindAndValidateD2ExpMpq()\n2. Iterate through unit state timer slots and update each timer (standard or expansion range)\n3. Return 0 if any timer update fails (early exit on error)\n4. Load previous game state ID from global tracker (or -1 if none)\n5. Reset current state tracker to -1 (clear previous state)\n6. If previous state was valid, initialize all game objects via InitializeAllGameObjectTimings()\n7. Validate previous state ID is in valid range (0-6) and dispatch to state initialization\n8. Get current state type from pStateData[0] and map to one of 7 state IDs via cascade comparison\n9. Compare new state ID with previous state ID\n10. If state unchanged OR animation speed equals 1, skip state transition execution\n11. If state changed AND animation speed is 2/3/4, execute state transition via FindAndActivateItemByName()\n12. Store mapped state ID to global state tracker\n13. Notify state observer with current state via FUN_6fa51aa0()\n14. Process state-dependent entity flag updates based on expansion mode and inactive/active state\n15. If state inactive (-1): clear 6 UI entities, deactivate UI controls\n16. If state active: set entity flags with mode indicator, activate UI control with stored value\n17. For expansion mode: set additional flag bits (0x20 mode, 0x40 expansion)\n18. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\npStateData: Pointer to state data structure with at least offset +0xc containing additional parameters\n\nReturns:\n1 on success, 0 if timer update fails\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- State IDs 5 and 6 trigger special expansion flag handling (mode bits 0x20 and 0x40)\n- Animation speed values control state transition execution (1=skip, 2/3/4=execute)\n- Global state tracker (_DAT_6fa64d94) is reset to -1 at start, stores mapped state ID\n- Expansion mode check determines which unit timer range to validate (std vs expanded)\n- Entity flags are set on global entity pointer (DAT_6fa65abc) at offset +0x1eb",
