      "name": "ProcessGameCommandQueue",
      "signature": "void ProcessGameCommandQueue(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Process up to 4 game commands and queue them for dispatch.\n\nThis function implements a fixed-capacity command queue processor that enqueues\ncommands from predefined command structures into a global queue array. The queue\ncapacity is limited to 64 entries (0x40). If the queue reaches capacity before\nall 4 commands can be enqueued, the function aborts with an error message.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if current queue size (DAT_6fa65e34) exceeds 63 (0x3f)\n   - If yes, report queue overflow error and terminate\n2. Process first command from DAT_6fa63590 via ProcessGameCommand\n   - Store result in queue at current index (DAT_6fa653c0[index])\n   - Increment queue size counter (DAT_6fa65e34)\n   - Set command as active target via SetCurrentEventTarget with flag 1\n   - Set entity bit flags to mark as active\n3. Check if queue size < 0x40 before processing second command\n4. Process second command from DAT_6fa635c0\n   - Store in queue, increment counter, set bit flags\n5. Check if queue size < 0x40 before processing third command\n6. Process third command from DAT_6fa635f0\n   - Store in queue, increment counter, set bit flags\n7. Check if queue size < 0x40 before processing fourth command\n8. If all 4 commands enqueued successfully:\n   - Process fourth command from DAT_6fa63620 and enqueue\n   - Call dispatch_command_handler(0,0,0) to trigger processing\n   - Call RenderTextBoxUnicodeText with zero parameters\n   - Return successfully\n9. If queue capacity exceeded at any point, report error and terminate\n\nParameters:\nNone - Operates on global queue state (DAT_6fa65e34) and command buffers\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function never returns on error (calls _exit(-1)). On success,\nprocesses all 4 commands and returns after rendering text box.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic constant 0x3f = 63, indicating queue capacity of 0x40 (64 entries)\n- Queue is sized as dword array: offset = index * 4\n- Command buffers at fixed addresses: 0x6fa63590, 0x6fa635c0, 0x6fa635f0, 0x6fa63620\n- Error message: \"Can't connect to Battle.Net - Try again.\"\n- Each command is marked active via SetCurrentEventTarget and ModifyEntityBitFlags\n\nStructure Layout:\nQueue array (DAT_6fa653c0) contains dword entries at 4-byte intervals.\nEach entry is a game command handle returned from ProcessGameCommand.\nQueue counter (DAT_6fa65e34) tracks number of enqueued commands (0-64).",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
