      "name": "LoadGameDataConfigurationFiles",
      "signature": "void LoadGameDataConfigurationFiles(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Loads and validates game data configuration files in priority sequence.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get default configuration parameters from GetOperationDataByType()\n2. Build primary config file path using sprintf with DATA_LOCAL template\n3. Attempt to open and validate primary config file via OpenAndValidateGameFile()\n4. If primary config fails (non-zero return), release file handle and return early\n5. Call initialize_system_state() to initialize system state structures\n6. If system init fails (zero return), load secondary fallback config:\n   - Build secondary path using DATA_LOCAL template with fallback data at 0x6fa5e0f8\n   - Open and validate secondary config file\n   - If secondary fails, release handle; if succeeds, continue\n7. If system init succeeds (non-zero return), load tertiary config:\n   - Build tertiary path using DATA_LOCAL template with alternate data at 0x6fa5e1b8\n   - Open and validate tertiary config file\n   - If tertiary fails, release handle and return\n   - If tertiary succeeds, continue to cleanup\n8. Release all file handles and return\n\nParameters:\n  None - Uses global structures and unaffected registers (EBX, ESI for buffers)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Priority system: Primary \u2192 System Init \u2192 Secondary/Tertiary fallback\n  - Each config file path is formatted with 8-byte data parameter\n  - File handles tracked via stack variable fileHandle with ref counting\n  - System initialization acts as decision point for config selection\n  - All error cases perform cleanup via ReleaseFileHandleWithRefCount()",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
