      "name": "InitializeGameEntities",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameEntities(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes a collection of game entities with initial command processing and state flags.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Destroy existing UI controls in the entity buffer\\n2. Reset entity count and initialize state flags (entity count = 0, flag at 0x6fa65e40 = 1, flag at 0x6fa65e60 = 0)\\n3. Process first entity command from 0x6fa638c0, store entity handle, set event target, enable bit flag\\n4. Check if entity count (1) exceeds capacity (0x40), if yes, abort with error\\n5. Process second entity command from 0x6fa63e60, store entity handle, enable bit flag\\n6. Check if entity count (2) exceeds capacity, if yes, abort with error\\n7. Process third entity command from 0x6fa63920, store entity handle, enable bit flag\\n8. Check if entity count (3) exceeds capacity, if yes, abort with error\\n9. Process fourth entity command from 0x6fa63e30, store entity handle, increment count\\n10. If count did not exceed capacity: call dispatch_command_handler(), call RenderUnicodeTextInBox(), return success\\n11. If capacity exceeded: call GetReturnAddress(0x60d), call CleanupAndAbort() with error message, call _exit(-1)\\n\\nParameters:\\nNone\\n\\nReturns:\\nvoid - Function returns only on successful initialization; on capacity error, calls _exit(-1) for abnormal termination\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Magic number 0x40 (64): Maximum entity capacity in the initialization buffer\\n- Magic number 0x60d: Return address offset used in error reporting\\n- Magic number -1: Exit code used for abnormal termination due to capacity exceeded\\n- Critical: The function initializes exactly 4 game entities (first 3 with capacity checks, fourth without intermediate check)",
