      "name": "InitializeConnectionUI",
      "signature": "int InitializeConnectionUI(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes the Battle.net connection UI by clearing previous controls and processing three game command sequences.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Loads current UI control count from global variable DAT_6fa65e34\n2. If any controls exist, iterates through and destroys each control in DAT_6fa653c0 array\n3. Resets control counter to zero\n4. Processes first game command from DAT_6fa638c0 via ProcessGameCommand, stores entity handle in array slot 0\n5. Sets event target and entity flags for first command result\n6. Checks if array has space for second command (count < 0x40)\n7. Processes second game command from DAT_6fa63e90, stores entity handle in array slot 1\n8. Sets entity flags for second command result\n9. Checks if array has space for third command (count < 0x40)\n10. Processes third game command from DAT_6fa63ec0, stores entity handle in array slot 2\n11. Sets entity flags for third command result\n12. Calls RenderTextInUIControl to display the initialized UI\n13. Returns 1 to indicate success\n14. If array buffer overflows (would exceed 0x40 items), calls GetReturnAddress, CleanupAndAbort with error message, and exits with code -1\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\n1 = Success, UI initialized with three commands processed and rendered\nDoes not return on error (exits process with code -1)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Maximum 0x40 (64) UI control entries can be stored in DAT_6fa653c0 array\n- Three ProcessGameCommand calls must complete successfully or error handler is triggered\n- All previous UI controls destroyed at start regardless of count\n- Magic constant 0x60d passed to GetReturnAddress for error reporting\n- Error message references \"Battle.Net\" connection failure",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "STR",
