      "name": "ConfigureEventTargetSettings",
      "signature": "void ConfigureEventTargetSettings(int isShowUI, undefined4 reserved1, int eventMode, undefined4 eventFlagsParam1, undefined4 eventFlagsParam2, int textDefaultValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Configures event target settings and bit flags for Battle.net event handling.\n\nThis function initializes one or two event target entities and applies bit flags based on the event mode parameter. It validates the connection status, sets up either a single event target (mode 1) or dual event targets (mode 2), stores configuration values to global memory locations, and optionally renders UI text output.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate connection: If unaff_EBX (connection handle) is 0, abort with error code 0x743\n2. Determine event mode: Set computedEventMode=1 if eventMode==0, else set to 2\n3. Call FUN_6fa52b60 to initialize event handling infrastructure\n4. Branch based on computedEventMode:\n   Mode 1 (computedEventMode==1):\n   a. Retrieve event target entity via FUN_6fa52ba0()\n   b. Set entity as current event target with SetCurrentEventTarget()\n   c. Apply bit flags with ModifyEntityBitFlags()\n   d. Compute flags: 0xd if textDefaultValue==0, else 0x1b\n   e. Store configuration at 0x6fa64414-0x6fa64420\n   Mode 2 (computedEventMode==2):\n   a. Retrieve first event target entity and configure with flag 0xd\n   b. Store at 0x6fa64444-0x6fa64450\n   c. Retrieve second event target entity\n   d. Compute flags: 0xd if textDefaultValue==0, else 0x1b\n   e. Store at 0x6fa64474-0x6fa64480\n5. Call FUN_6fa52ba0 and ModifyEntityBitFlags() again for final configuration\n6. If isShowUI!=0: Call RenderUnicodeTextInBox() to display text\n7. Always call RenderUnicodeTextInBox() at end regardless of isShowUI\n8. Return with stack cleanup (RET 0x18 = 6 parameters \u00d7 4 bytes each)\n\nParameters:\n- isShowUI (int): Flag controlling UI text rendering (0=skip text, non-zero=render text)\n- reserved1 (undefined4): Reserved parameter, not used in this function\n- eventMode (int): Event configuration mode (0=mode 1 single target, non-zero=mode 2 dual targets)\n- eventFlagsParam1 (undefined4): Parameter stored at offset +0xc in mode 1 or +0x18 in mode 2\n- eventFlagsParam2 (undefined4): Parameter stored at offset +0x20 in mode 2 configuration\n- textDefaultValue (int): Determines bit flags when eventMode==0 (0x1b if non-zero, 0xd if zero)\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Connection validation at entry point: If unaff_EBX==0, calls CleanupAndAbort() then _exit()\n- Bit flag encoding: Masks used are 0xd (13) and 0x1b (27) representing event state\n- Global configuration arrays: All writes go to 0x6fa64414-0x6fa64480 region\n- Dual rendering: RenderUnicodeTextInBox() always called twice (once conditional, once unconditional)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
