      "name": "RenderMultilineUIText",
      "signature": "uint RenderMultilineUIText(uint controlId, Unicode * pText, uint flags)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Renders multiline Unicode text in UI control by splitting at newlines.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Create local Unicode buffer (2048 bytes / 1024 Unicode chars)\n2. Initialize buffer by calling Unicode constructor 1024 times (init_loop_start to init_loop_check)\n3. Copy input text into buffer using Unicode::strncpy (copy_text_call)\n4. If buffer is empty, jump to function_return with status 1\n5. Scan through text character by character (line_loop_start)\n6. Check each character for newline (0x0a)\n7. If newline found, replace with null terminator and render line (handle_newline to render_line_call)\n8. Move to next character position (next_char)\n9. Continue until null terminator found (line_loop_check to line_loop_continue)\n10. After main loop, check if there's remaining text after last newline (final_line_check)\n11. If remaining text exists (lineStart < currentPos), render final line (final_render_call)\n12. Return 1 indicating successful render\n\nParameters:\n  controlId (uint): UI control handle/ID to render text into\n  pText (Unicode *): Pointer to null-terminated Unicode text string (may contain newlines)\n  flags (uint): Configuration flags (0 or 4) passed to RenderTextBoxUnicodeText\n\nReturns:\n  uint: Always returns 1 (success status)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Newline character (0x0a) marks line boundaries\n  - Empty input string skips rendering loop entirely\n  - Buffer size is 1024 Unicode characters (2048 bytes)\n  - Last line is rendered only if text exists after previous newline\n  - Unicode text uses 16-bit character encoding (sizeof(Unicode) = 2)\n  - RenderTextBoxUnicodeText called once per line, with flags parameter passed through",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:bf932b2896ebe7330c24a21504d9a9eed80e55cb28c31b406ae340a43001460b",
