      "name": "InitializeBattleNetUIControls",
      "signature": "void InitializeBattleNetUIControls(Unicode * commandHandler, undefined4 callback, int useGameStateMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes Battle.net UI control interface by creating and configuring three primary UI elements.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Destroy any existing UI controls in the global control array\n2. Reset the control counter to zero\n3. Process primary game command (base control) and store result\n4. Set current event target to primary control with flag 1\n5. If capacity allows, process secondary command (adjusted by game state mode parameter)\n6. If capacity allows, process tertiary command (fixed structure)\n7. Set bit flags (0x1) on all three created controls\n8. Initialize UI display with tertiary control, command handler string, and mode flag\n9. Store callback function reference in global state\n10. If capacity exceeded at any point, log error, get return address, and abort\n\nParameters:\n  commandHandler (Unicode*) - Pointer to command handler string/structure from dispatch system\n  callback (undefined4) - Function pointer callback for event handling (typically FUN_6fa4d5d0)\n  useGameStateMode (int) - Boolean flag controlling command offset calculation (0=base, 1=alternate)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value on success. On failure, calls CleanupAndAbort and _exit(-1)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Array capacity limit is 0x40 (64) controls\n  - Secondary control address calculation: (useGameStateMode ? 0xdf + 2 : 0xdf) * 0x30 offset\n  - Uses bit flag 0x1 for control state marking\n  - Function is non-returning on error path (_exit call)\n  - All three controls stored in global array DAT_6fa653c0 with counter DAT_6fa65e34\n\nControl Array Layout:\n  Each element is 4 bytes (undefined4) pointer to UI control structure\n  Base address: DAT_6fa653c0 (dynamic array)\n  Counter: DAT_6fa65e34 (tracks element count)\n  Capacity: 0x40 (64 elements)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:e67748c721d6972bba931bb1f48b01db361e7db3cda4930a05bf23fddcfd8885",
