      "name": "CleanupUIResources",
      "signature": "uint CleanupUIResources(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Performs complete cleanup of UI resources and render state before shutdown.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call initialization function to prepare cleanup context\n2. Reset render state flag (DAT_6fa65dbc) to 0\n3. Reset cleanup status flag (DAT_6fa65dc0) to 0\n4. Install cleanup callback pointer at DAT_6fa65dc8\n5. Call ProcessRenderingQueue with callback to flush pending render operations\n6. Load UI control count from DAT_6fa65e34 into EAX\n7. Check if control count is positive; skip loop if count <= 0\n8. Initialize EDI with base address of UI control array (DAT_6fa653c0)\n9. Loop through each control:\n   a. Call DestroyUIControl with current control pointer\n   b. Increment control index (ESI) by 1\n   c. Advance pointer (EDI) by 4 bytes to next control\n   d. Compare index against control count; repeat if not finished\n10. Clear control count by setting DAT_6fa65e34 to 0\n11. Load and return cleanup status from DAT_6fa65dc0\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nEAX: Cleanup status code (from DAT_6fa65dc0)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If control count (DAT_6fa65e34) is 0 or negative, loop is skipped entirely\n- Control array stride is 4 bytes per element (pointer-sized)\n- All controls must be destroyed in forward iteration order\n- Cleanup status is preserved across loop iterations\n\nControl Array Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name        Type    Description\n0       4     pControl[0]       void*   Pointer to first UI control\n4       4     pControl[1]       void*   Pointer to second UI control\n...     ...   ...               ...     Additional control pointers",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
