      "comment": "Initializes the rendering system by cleaning up UI controls and processing a rendering queue.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calls FUN_6fa54c60 to perform cleanup operations\n2. Queues ProcessRenderingQueue callback function for execution\n3. If callback handler DAT_6fa656c4 exists, invokes function pointer at offset +0x40\n4. Destroys all UI controls in DAT_6fa653c0 array (count: DAT_6fa65e34)\n5. Resets control count to 0\n6. If no rendering queue data exists (DAT_6fa65530 == NULL), sets size to 0xFFFFFFFF and returns\n7. Extracts queue data size from offset +0x4 and validates size < 512 items\n8. If size >= 512, calls error handler CleanupAndAbort with error message and exits\n9. Allocates memory block for array (DAT_6fa65e74) and zeros all bytes\n10. For each item in queue data, allocates and copies two strings into entry structures\n11. Calls FUN_6fa52140 to process each entry\n12. Calls qsort to sort final array by custom comparator FUN_6fa52020\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value. Function either returns normally after sorting or calls exit() on error.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic number 0x200 (512) is maximum queue size - exceeding this causes fatal error\n- Ordinal 0x1168, 0x1173, 0x1179, 0x1186, 0x118b are allocation tracking codes\n- String parsing uses null-terminator detection with length computation\n- Memory is allocated through AllocateMemoryWithTracking for tracking purposes\n- Uses REP STOSD/STOSB for efficient memory zeroing\n- Final qsort uses 4-byte elements (dword entries)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
