      "name": "InitializeBattleNetUIControls",
      "signature": "void InitializeBattleNetUIControls(Unicode * windowName, undefined4 windowParam, int useAlternateConfig)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes Battle.net UI controls by creating game command window controls and setting their event targets. Manages a global array of UI controls with capacity of 0x40 (64) items. Creates 3 UI controls from command data structures selected by connection state and configuration parameter. Sets bit flags on created controls and stores the last window parameter. Aborts initialization if global UI control array capacity is exceeded.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear existing UI controls by iterating through global control array (0x6fa653c0) up to count (0x6fa65e34) and calling DestroyUIControl on each\n2. Reset control count to zero\n3. Check connection state flag at 0x6fa65ad8 to determine which command set to use\n4. If not connected (flag=0): Create first control from DAT_6fa638c0, else create from DAT_6fa63d70\n5. Increment control count and add handle to control array\n6. Set first control as current event target with priority 1\n7. Check if control count (now 1) has reached capacity (0x40)\n8. Calculate second control offset based on useAlternateConfig: (useAlternateConfig==0 ? 0xdf : 0xf8) * 0x30 + 0x6fa60f20\n9. Create second control from calculated command data address\n10. Increment control count and add handle to control array\n11. Check if control count (now 2) has reached capacity (0x40)\n12. Create third control from DAT_6fa63920 (not connected) or DAT_6fa63dd0 (connected)\n13. Increment control count and add handle to control array\n14. For each of the 3 controls, call ModifyEntityBitFlags with flag value 1\n15. Call FUN_6fa52a70 on third control with windowName and zero parameter\n16. Store windowParam in global variable at 0x6fa6552c\n17. Return successfully\n18. If control count reaches capacity at any point before 3 controls created, call GetReturnAddress(0x60d) and CleanupAndAbort with error string, then exit(-1)\n\nParameters:\n- windowName (Unicode*): Name or identifier passed to FUN_6fa52a70 for the third UI control\n- windowParam (undefined4): Parameter stored in global variable 0x6fa6552c after all controls initialized\n- useAlternateConfig (int): When zero, uses command set 0xdf; when non-zero, uses command set 0xf8\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Global control array overflow: If control count reaches 0x40 before 3 controls are created, initialization fails and process aborts with error code\n- Connection state determines which two command data addresses are used (connected vs not connected paths)\n- useAlternateConfig parameter switches between two different second control configurations\n- Global variables modified: 0x6fa65e34 (control count), 0x6fa6552c (window parameter)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
