      "name": "CreateGameDialogUIControls",
      "signature": "void CreateGameDialogUIControls(Unicode * pTitleText, Unicode * pSubtitleText, Unicode * pButtonText, Unicode * pMessageText, uint dialogFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Creates and initializes a game dialog UI control panel with 6 UI elements.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear any previously created dialog controls from global control array (DAT_6fa653c0)\n2. Reset control counter to 0 (DAT_6fa65e34)\n3. Create first control via ProcessGameCommand(0x6fa63c50), store in array[0]\n4. Set event target and bit flags for first control\n5. Create second control via ProcessGameCommand(0x6fa63c80), store in array[1]\n6. Set bit flags for second control\n7. Validate array not full (< 0x40 slots), continue if space available\n8. Create third control via ProcessGameCommand(0x6fa63cb0), store in array[2]\n9. Configure third control with pButtonText parameter\n10. Validate array not full, continue if space available\n11. Create fourth control via ProcessGameCommand(0x6fa63ce0), store in array[3]\n12. Configure fourth control with pSubtitleText parameter\n13. Validate array not full, continue if space available\n14. Create fifth control via ProcessGameCommand(0x6fa63d10), store in array[4]\n15. Configure fifth control with pMessageText parameter\n16. Validate array not full, continue if space available\n17. Create sixth control via ProcessGameCommand(0x6fa63d40), store in array[5]\n18. Configure sixth control with pMessageText parameter and flag 0x4\n19. Store dialogFlags in global DAT_6fa6552c\n20. Return on success or abort with error code 0x60d if array overflows\n\nParameters:\n  pTitleText (Unicode*): Text content for first dialog control\n  pSubtitleText (Unicode*): Text content for fourth dialog control\n  pButtonText (Unicode*): Text content for third dialog control\n  pMessageText (Unicode*): Text content for fifth and sixth dialog controls\n  dialogFlags (uint): Dialog configuration flags stored in DAT_6fa6552c\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function aborts program execution if UI control array overflows (exceeds 0x40 slots)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Control array maximum capacity: 0x40 (64) controls\n  - Each control creation and configuration checked against array bounds\n  - Overflow condition triggers error handler with code 0x60d\n  - First two controls initialized with bit flag 0x1\n  - Sixth control initialized with bit flag 0x4 instead of 0x1\n  - Global counter DAT_6fa65e34 tracks current number of allocated controls",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:b657a199387d0f3f3ee14d246c7097bfa5b32f45ee08e3d6060f5f17336d579d",
