      "name": "InitializeUIControlsWithParameters",
      "signature": "void InitializeUIControlsWithParameters(Unicode * pCommandStr1, Unicode * pParamStr1, Unicode * pParamStr2, uint nConfigValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes UI controls with command strings and optional parameters.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear existing UI control array (DAT_6fa653c0) by destroying all entries up to current count\n2. Reset control counter (DAT_6fa65e34) to 0\n3. Process first required command (0x6fa63b30) via ProcessGameCommand\n4. Store returned handle in control array at index 0 and increment counter\n5. Set current event target to first handle with flag 0x1\n6. Apply bit flags 0x1 to first handle via ModifyEntityBitFlags\n7. Check if counter < 0x40 (max capacity)\n8. Process second required command (0x6fa63b60) via ProcessGameCommand\n9. Store returned handle in control array and increment counter\n10. Apply bit flags 0x1 to second handle\n11. Process third required command (0x6fa63b90) via ProcessGameCommand\n12. Store returned handle in control array and increment counter\n13. Apply bit flags 0x1 to third handle\n14. Call FUN_6fa52a70 with third handle, pParamStr1, and mode 0\n15. Check if pParamStr2 is NULL or points to empty string (word == 0)\n16. If NULL/empty: process default command (0x6fa63bc0), set parameterMode to 0\n17. If provided: create two additional UI controls (0xef and 0xf0), set parameterMode to 4\n18. Process pParamStr2 with final UI control using parameterMode\n19. Store nConfigValue in global DAT_6fa6552c and return\n20. Error handling: if array would exceed 0x40 capacity, call GetReturnAddress, CleanupAndAbort with error message, exit with code -1\n\nParameters:\n- pCommandStr1: Unicode * - First command/data block pointer (0x6fa63b30)\n- pParamStr1: Unicode * - First parameter string to process with third UI control\n- pParamStr2: Unicode * - Optional second parameter string (NULL or pointer)\n- nConfigValue: uint - Configuration value to store in global DAT_6fa6552c\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function does not return a value; either returns normally or calls exit(-1)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic numbers: 0x40 (64 = max UI control array capacity), 0xef (UI control type 1), 0xf0 (UI control type 2), 0x1 (bit flag for ModifyEntityBitFlags), 0x60d (return address offset for error handling)\n- If pParamStr2 is NULL or empty string, function processes single parameter via default command path\n- If pParamStr2 is provided, function creates two additional UI controls and processes parameter with mode 4\n- Function can exit with code -1 if control array would exceed capacity\n- All UI control creation failures or issues will trigger error cleanup",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
