      "comment": "Initializes UI controls with game command data and callback.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Destroy all existing UI controls in global array (max 0x40 slots)\n2. Reset control count to 0 in DAT_6fa65e34\n3. Create first control via ProcessGameCommand(&DAT_6fa63a70)\n4. Set control as event target and modify entity flags\n5. Verify control count < 0x40 before proceeding\n6. Create second control via ProcessGameCommand(&DAT_6fa63aa0)\n7. Modify second control's entity flags\n8. Verify control count < 0x40 before proceeding\n9. Create third control via ProcessGameCommand(&DAT_6fa63ad0)\n10. Modify third control's entity flags\n11. Initialize third control with pParam1 via FUN_6fa52a70\n12. Check control count overflow (> 0x3f); abort if exceeded\n13. Create fourth control via ProcessGameCommand(&DAT_6fa63b00)\n14. Modify fourth control's entity flags\n15. Initialize fourth control with pParam2 via FUN_6fa52a70\n16. Store callback pointer in DAT_6fa6552c\n17. Return successfully or abort on UI array overflow\n\nParameters:\n- pParam1 (Unicode *): First UI parameter string\n- pParam2 (Unicode *): Second UI parameter string\n- pInitCallback (undefined4): Callback function pointer\n\nReturns:\n- void (function does not return on error; calls _exit(-1))\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic number 0x40 (64): Maximum UI control array size\n- Magic number 0x60d (1549): Error line number passed to GetReturnAddress\n- Magic number 0x3f (63): Overflow check (control count > 63 triggers error)\n- Error paths call CleanupAndAbort with line number and _exit(-1)\n- Four controls created in sequence from predefined command tables\n\nStructure Layout:\nGlobal control array DAT_6fa653c0 is indexed array of undefined4 (4-byte control handles)\n- Each element stores entity handle returned by ProcessGameCommand\n- Array size tracked by DAT_6fa65e34 (current count)\n- Maximum 0x40 (64) elements before overflow",
