      "name": "ValidateAndApplyGameStateUpdate",
      "signature": "bool ValidateAndApplyGameStateUpdate(byte * pGameStateData)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "bool",
      "comment": "Validates and applies a game state update from external data.\\n\\nThis function performs state synchronization by comparing input data against\\nstored state and updating game rendering/logic if validation passes.\\n\\nALGORITHM:\\n1. Check current game state via Ordinal_10054()\\n2. If state check passes (returns 0):\\n   - Compare input data against stored state buffer (byte-by-byte comparison)\\n   - If comparison succeeds (states match):\\n     - Check state again via Ordinal_10054()\\n     - If still valid, proceed to finalization\\n   - Clear state flags at offsets +0x229 and +0xd1 if input is empty\\n   - Otherwise, validate game object pointer and type\\n   - Copy input data to storage buffers at +0x229 and +0xd1\\n   - Call rendering and game state processing functions\\n   - Return false if validation/processing fails\\n3. Finalize: process rendering queue and return success/failure status\\n\\nPARAMETERS:\\n- pGameStateData: Input state data buffer (EDI register, __stdcall convention)\\n\\nRETURNS:\\n- bool: true if state update successful, false on validation failure\\n  (returns 1 - (result != 0) from Ordinal_10036)\\n\\nSPECIAL CASES:\\n- Empty input (first byte = 0): clears state without validation\\n- State mismatch: skips update and returns true\\n- Invalid game object (null or type 8): returns false\\n- State processing result != 1-2: returns false\\n\\nSTRUCTURE LAYOUT:\\nThe function accesses a state structure at DAT_6fa65abc with:\\n- Offset +0x229: Primary state buffer (256 bytes)\\n- Offset +0xd1: Secondary state buffer (256 bytes)\\n- Referenced via global pointer, likely part of game context",
