      "name": "UpdateAnimationFrame",
      "signature": "int UpdateAnimationFrame(char * pAnimationData)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Updates animation frame data and refreshes rendering state\nSynchronizes animation state with rendering system by comparing animation data,\ncopying updated buffers, and processing render queue updates.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if animation update is already pending (Ordinal_10054)\n2. If not pending, compare current animation data with stored template\n3. If data differs or no template exists, initialize animation state\n4. Copy animation buffers to two cached locations (0x229, 0xd1)\n5. Apply animation callbacks through render queue processor\n6. Validate animation result (must be in range 0-2)\n7. Return 1 on success, 0 on failure or if update already pending\n\nParameters:\npAnimationData - pointer to animation frame data structure\n\nReturns:\n1 - Animation update successful\n0 - Update skipped (already pending) or validation failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If animation data is null, clears animation state without processing\n- If callback returns type 0x8, treats as no valid animation update\n- Animation result must be <= 2 to succeed",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:3dd89ebc9d7bdc2070280c1adbe9b005e1dc94a7ae244c9e03f90eb57a4197ae",
