      "name": "InitializeAndRenderGameUI",
      "signature": "int InitializeAndRenderGameUI(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes and renders the game UI with command queue processing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize game command queue by calling InitializeGameCommandQueue\n2. Validate command queue has space (0x40 = 64 slots max) before processing\n3. Process up to 6 game commands sequentially, storing return values in queue:\n   - Command 1: DAT_6fa61c70 - Primary game input/state\n   - Command 2: DAT_6fa61ca0 - Secondary game input/state\n   - Command 3: DAT_6fa61cd0 - Tertiary game input/state\n   - Command 4: DAT_6fa61d00 - Quaternary game input/state\n   - Command 5: DAT_6fa61d30 - Quinary game input/state\n   - Command 6: DAT_6fa61d60 - Senary game input/state\n4. For commands 2-3: dispatch command handler and render text in box\n5. Fetch window data structure from function pointer at [DAT_6fa656c4 + 0x98]\n6. Loop through window elements (1 to element_count at [window_data+8]):\n   - Render each UI element with index\n7. Validate and adjust list index based on visible line count and bounds\n8. Clamp index to valid structure range\n9. Call finalization function FUN_6fa53d60\n10. Return success code 1\n\nReturns:\n  1 (success) if all commands processed and UI rendered\n  -1 (via _exit) if command queue overflow detected (queue at 0x40 limit)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Queue size is fixed at 0x40 (64) entries\n  - Error path calls CleanupAndAbort with error string pointer offset by 0x2e\n  - Terminating calls exit(-1) for critical failures\n  - Window element loop only executes if element count > 0\n  - Index validation checks for out-of-bounds conditions before rendering\n\nGlobal Data Structures:\n  Offset  Size  Field Name             Type        Description\n  0x6fa65e30  4    CommandQueueIndex      dword       Current position in command queue\n  0x6fa652b8  256  CommandQueue           dword[64]   Stores command return values\n  0x6fa65500  4    LastProcessedCommand   dword       Result from command 4 (0x6fa61d00)\n  0x6fa656c4  4    WindowDataProvider     function*   Points to function returning window data\n  0x6fa61c70  4    Command1Param          dword       Parameter for first game command\n  0x6fa61ca0  4    Command2Param          dword       Parameter for second game command\n  0x6fa61cd0  4    Command3Param          dword       Parameter for third game command\n  0x6fa61d00  4    Command4Param          dword       Parameter for fourth game command\n  0x6fa61d30  4    Command5Param          dword       Parameter for fifth game command\n  0x6fa61d60  4    Command6Param          dword       Parameter for sixth game command",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
