      "name": "InitializeGameUITextRendering",
      "signature": "uint InitializeGameUITextRendering(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initialize Game UI Text Rendering System\n\nInitializes the UI text rendering subsystem by allocating a large Unicode buffer,\nverifying network connection status, rendering initial UI elements, and processing\ntext tokenization with proper delimiter handling and rendering.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate and initialize 2048-element Unicode buffer via default constructor\n2. Verify connection status by calling FUN_6fa55900 (returns connection pointer)\n3. If no connection, retrieve return address (0x1402), abort with error message, exit(-1)\n4. If connected: render UI controls 50 times (0x32 iterations)\n5. Initialize and render additional UI elements with text rendering\n6. Process text buffer with tokenization loop:\n   - Check for token separator (0x2a = '*')\n   - Compare input text against cached patterns using isAlpha validation\n   - Handle matched and unmatched token cases\n   - Update buffer remaining counter and advance pointers\n7. Continue until all tokens processed\n8. Retrieve window validation data via ValidateAndGetWindowData\n9. Initialize game module with ordinal 0x1456 (priority/resource ID)\n10. Return 1 to indicate successful initialization\n\nParameters:\nNone - function operates on global UI state\n\nReturns:\n1 - Initialization successful\nNever returns on error (calls exit(-1))\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic number 0x32 (50) = default UI render iteration count\n- Magic number 0x400 (1024) = Unicode buffer element count (2048 bytes total)\n- Token separator value 0x2a = asterisk character '*'\n- Ordinal 0x1456 = game module initialization ID\n- Return address ordinal 0x1402 = error message address reference\n- Function uses stack-based local buffer (0xc08 = 3080 bytes allocation)\n\nStructure Layout:\nThe function manages Unicode text buffer with stride pattern of 2 bytes per element\n(0xc08 bytes / 0x400 elements = 2 bytes per Unicode character)\nAdditional buffers created on stack for intermediate text processing (0x100, 0x100)",
