      "name": "ProcessInitialGameCommands",
      "signature": "void ProcessInitialGameCommands(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Processes initial game command sequence by loading and executing three game command structures.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call initialization routine FUN_6fa55d30()\n2. Check if command buffer index (DAT_6fa65e30) is below capacity (0x40 / 64 entries)\n3. For each of 3 command structures (DAT_6fa61040, DAT_6fa61070, DAT_6fa610a0):\n   a. Process command structure via ProcessGameCommand()\n   b. Store 32-bit result in command buffer at [DAT_6fa65e30*4 + 0x6fa652b8]\n   c. Increment command buffer index\n   d. Validate that index remains below 0x40 capacity\n4. After each command result, validate screenshot mode settings via ValidateAndSetScreenshotMode()\n5. If any buffer capacity check fails (index >= 0x40):\n   a. Call GetReturnAddress(0x624) to retrieve error context\n   b. Call CleanupAndAbort() with error string pointer\n   c. Call _exit(-1) to terminate process immediately\n6. On success, call FUN_6fa52bf0() with palette pointer (s_palette_sky_pal_pl2_6fa5e988) for resource initialization\n\nParameters:\nNone - Function operates entirely on global state\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Never returns normally; either completes command processing or exits via _exit(-1)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Buffer overflow protection at 0x40 entries (64 maximum commands)\n- Three separate capacity checks (one before each command)\n- Error handling uses fatal _exit(-1) rather than returning error code\n- Called during game initialization from InitializeGameSession and ExecuteValidatedGameCommands\n- Each command result stored as DWORD in sequential array slots",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
