      "name": "InitializeGameEngineState",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameEngineState(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes the game engine state by processing command queues, loading resources, and configuring audio output.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Call initialization function FUN_6fa55d30\\n2. Check if command queue counter (DAT_6fa65e30) is below 0x40 limit\\n3. Process up to 5 command buffers sequentially:\\n   - DAT_6fa60f80, DAT_6fa60fb0, DAT_6fa61040, DAT_6fa61070, DAT_6fa60fe0\\n   - Each buffer processed via ProcessGameCommand and stored in command result array DAT_6fa652b8\\n   - Increment queue counter after each command\\n4. Load palette file \\\"sky_pal_pl2\\\" via FUN_6fa52bf0\\n5. Validate Diablo II expansion MPQ files via FindAndValidateD2ExpMpq\\n6. Dispatch command handlers 4 times to initialize game state (command 4, params 0,0)\\n7. Render initial text boxes via RenderTextBoxUnicodeText\\n8. Set game state to 0 (initial state)\\n9. Check audio option flag via GetAudioOptionFlag\\n10. If audio enabled, initialize music system via EnableMusicSystem\\n11. On error (queue full): abort with error message via CleanupAndAbort and exit(-1)\\n\\nReturns: void (no return value, may exit via error path)\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Command queue limit: 0x40 (64 entries) - if exceeded, abort with error\\n- Audio initialization: Only EnableMusicSystem called if audio option flag is non-zero\\n- Multiple render operations: RenderTextBoxUnicodeText called twice with same parameters\\n\\nCalling Convention: __stdcall (standard Windows calling convention with stack cleanup)",
