      "name": "InitializeGameCommandProcessor",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameCommandProcessor(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes the game command processing system by queuing and validating multiple game commands.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Initialize game command queue\\n2. Process and queue first command (0x6fa64340) - checks queue size is < 0x40\\n3. Process and queue second command (0x6fa64370) - increments queue index\\n4. Validate screenshot configuration with parameter value 3\\n5. Process and queue third command (0x6fa642b0) - checks queue size\\n6. Call external function at [DAT_6fa656c4 + 0x4c] to get frame count value\\n7. Clamp frame count value to maximum of 100\\n8. Check if queue is full (>= 0x40) - if so, abort with error message\\n9. Process and queue fourth command (0x6fa642e0)\\n10. Dispatch command handler with zero parameters\\n11. Render text box with Unicode text (zero parameters)\\n12. Check if queue is still available (< 0x40)\\n13. Process and queue fifth command (0x6fa64280)\\n14. Dispatch another command handler with zero parameters\\n15. Render another text box with Unicode text (zero parameters)\\n16. Check if queue is still available\\n17. Process and queue sixth command (0x6fa643a0)\\n18. Get frame count from configuration data\\n19. Multiply frame count by scaled percentage value: (frameCount * percentage) / 100\\n20. Store calculated frame count using ValidateAndStoreFrameCount\\n21. Format percentage value to string using sprintf\\n22. Render final text box with Unicode conversion\\n\\nParameters:\\n  None\\n\\nReturns:\\n  None (void). Function never returns normally - either succeeds by RET or aborts via CleanupAndAbort/exit\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n  - Queue overflow protection: If queue reaches 0x40 items, calls GetReturnAddress(0x624) for error context and aborts\\n  - Frame count clamping: Frame count value capped at 100 (0x64)\\n  - Magic numbers: 0x40 = queue capacity, 0x64 = max frame count (100), 0x624 = error context ordinal\\n  - Error handling: Three different queue full check points with identical error handling pattern\\n  - String formatting: Uses sprintf to format percentage value to stack-allocated buffer\\n\\nStructure Layout:\\n  Global Data Accessed:\\n  Offset | Name              | Type    | Purpose\\n  -------|-------------------|---------|--------------------------------------------------\\n  DAT_6fa65e30 | Queue index/counter | dword | Current count of queued commands (capacity 0x40)\\n  DAT_6fa65e68 | Screenshot config   | dword | Configuration value from second command\\n  DAT_6fa65e64 | Command 3 value     | dword | Stored result from third ProcessGameCommand call\\n  DAT_6fa652b8 | Command queue array | dword[] | Array of queued command results (size 0x40)\\n  DAT_6fa656c4 | Frame config ptr    | void*  | Pointer to frame configuration structure",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
