      "name": "ExecuteValidatedGameCommands",
      "signature": "void ExecuteValidatedGameCommands(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Executes a sequence of validated game commands with buffer capacity validation.\n\nThis function processes five sequential game command structures, validating that the\nglobal command buffer (DAT_6fa653c0) has space (< 0x40 entries) before each operation.\nEach command structure pointer is passed to ProcessGameCommand() which returns a command\nresult that is stored in the command buffer array. After collecting all 5 commands, the\nfunction initializes game text rendering context and dispatches command processing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FUN_6fa576c0() for initialization/setup\n2. For each of 5 command structures:\n   a. Check if command buffer index DAT_6fa65e34 < 0x40 (64 max entries)\n   b. If buffer full: call GetReturnAddress(0x60d), dispatch error with CleanupAndAbort(),\n      and exit(-1) to terminate process\n   c. Call ProcessGameCommand(pCommandStruct) to process command structure\n   d. Store result in command buffer at index [DAT_6fa65e34*4 + 0x6fa653c0]\n   e. Increment DAT_6fa65e34 buffer index\n3. Call dispatch_command_handler(0,0,0) to dispatch processed commands\n4. Call RenderTextBoxUnicodeText(0,0,0) to render UI text\n5. Call SetEntityParameterFields(0) to initialize entity parameters\n6. Repeat steps 3-5 for command processing cycles\n7. Return when all commands processed successfully\n\nParameters:\nNone - Function has no parameters; operates on global state\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Never returns normally; calls _exit(-1) on error or completes command execution\n\nCommand Structures:\n- DAT_6fa61d90: First command structure\n- DAT_6fa621b0: Second command structure\n- DAT_6fa621e0: Third command structure\n- DAT_6fa620f0: Fourth command structure\n- DAT_6fa62120: Fifth command structure\n\nGlobal State Modified:\n- DAT_6fa65e34: Command buffer write index (0x0 to 0x40)\n- DAT_6fa653c0: Command buffer array (64 slots, 4 bytes each)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nBuffer overflow protection: Any attempt to write beyond 0x40 entries triggers fatal error\nError code 0x60d passed to GetReturnAddress indicates buffer overflow condition",
