      "name": "InitializeAudioSystem",
      "signature": "int InitializeAudioSystem(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes the audio system with conditional music setup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FUN_6fa55d30 to perform pre-initialization setup\n2. Retrieve audio option flag via GetAudioOptionFlag()\n3. If audio option flag is non-zero (music enabled):\n   a. Set ECX = 1 to indicate music is enabled\n   b. Call EnableMusicSystem() to initialize music playback\n4. Call FUN_6fa57df0 to perform post-initialization finalization\n5. Return 1 (success code)\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nint - Success code (1 for success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Music system is only initialized if the audio option flag is set\n- The RET 0x4 instruction suggests potential implicit parameters or stack adjustment\n- This function is a setup/initialization routine for audio functionality",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
