      "name": "ValidateAndProcessGameFrame",
      "signature": "uint ValidateAndProcessGameFrame(void * pFrameContext)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Validates game frame timing and processes frame data conditionally.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Load frame context parameter from stack\\n2. Call ValidateFrameTiming() to check if frame should be processed\\n3. If validation fails (returns 0), return 1 (success - frame skipped)\\n4. If validation passes (returns non-zero), call ProcessFrameData() with context\\n5. Return the result from ProcessFrameData()\\n\\nParameters:\\n- pFrameContext: void * - Frame data structure pointer, accessed at [ESP+0x8]\\n\\nReturns:\\n- uint: Result code from ProcessFrameData if validation passes, or 1 if validation fails\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Returns 1 as default success when frame processing is skipped\\n- Frame context is passed as parameter to both validation and processing functions\\n- Uses __stdcall calling convention with 4-byte parameter cleanup\\\"",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
