      "comment": "Initializes core game state and command processing queue for D2 engine.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call audio initialization routines (FadeOutAudioParameter, TryFinalizeContext, SetGlobalAudioParameter)\n2. Initialize command processing queue (InitializeGameCommandQueue)\n3. Read D2 MPQ configuration from INI file (game.ini, aux battle.net section)\n4. If MPQ read fails: Format default configuration values (0xd8, 0x94, 0xf6, 0x22)\n5. If MPQ read succeeds: Parse configuration using sscanf to extract 4 difficulty/class values\n6. Determine difficulty type (values 1-7) based on parsed configuration byte flags:\n   - Bit 0 set: difficultyType = 7 (error)\n   - Sign bit set: difficultyType = 6 (nightmare/hell)\n   - Bit 4 set: difficultyType = 5 (hell)\n   - Bit 3 set: difficultyType = 4 (nightmare)\n   - Bit 6 set: difficultyType = 3 (hard mode)\n   - Bit 2 set: difficultyType = 2\n   - Otherwise: difficultyType = 1 (normal)\n7. Validate D2 Expansion MPQ file exists via FindAndValidateD2ExpMpq\n8. If MPQ validation fails: Call error handler FUN_6fa567b0, return 1\n9. Enqueue 7 game commands via ProcessGameCommand with data pointers:\n   - DAT_6fa61880, DAT_6fa618b0, DAT_6fa618e0, DAT_6fa61910, DAT_6fa61940, DAT_6fa61970, DAT_6fa619a0\n10. After command 1: Dispatch pending commands (dispatch_command_handler), render text (RenderUnicodeTextInBox)\n11. Based on difficulty type: Invoke ModifyObjectBitfield 0-4 times to set character attributes\n12. Enqueue final command from DAT_6fa619d0\n13. Return 1 on success, or call CleanupAndAbort with error message and _exit(-1) if command queue full (exceeds 0x40 entries)\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nuint: 1 on success (after successfully queuing all commands), or does not return on error (calls _exit(-1))\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Command queue has fixed capacity of 0x40 (64 entries)\n- If any ProcessGameCommand or queue operation would exceed limit, function calls CleanupAndAbort with error string and terminates\n- Difficulty type encoding matches D2 configuration format from INI file\n- Character bitfield modifications vary by difficulty (cases 1-4 modify bitfield, cases 5-7 skip modification)\n- Default configuration values (0xd8, 0x94, 0xf6, 0x22) used when INI file read fails\n",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
