      "name": "InitializeGameSession",
      "signature": "int InitializeGameSession(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes the game session by loading and processing data files, setting up UI controls, and initializing command handlers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear initialization flag and initialize game resources\n2. Read configuration data from operation data\n3. Load file from disk and validate file signature\n4. Check file BOM (Byte Order Mark) for proper encoding detection:\n   - 0xFEFF indicates UTF-16 BE encoding\n   - 0xFFFE indicates UTF-16 LE encoding (requires byte swap)\n   - No BOM requires ANSI-to-Unicode conversion\n5. Parse Unicode text into lines, handling line breaks (CR/LF) and tabs\n6. Render each processed line to screen with word-wrap handling\n7. Initialize command handlers with 5 game commands in sequence\n8. Return success status (1) when initialization completes\n\nParameters:\nNone - function takes no parameters\n\nReturns:\nint - Returns 0 on error/early exit, 1 on successful initialization\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Memory allocation at multiple stages (file buffer, Unicode buffer, line buffer)\n- Handles three Unicode encodings: UTF-16 BE, UTF-16 LE, ANSI\n- Word wrapping triggered at 0x21C width threshold\n- Processes up to 200 characters per line with tab-to-space conversion\n- 5 command handlers dispatched from hardcoded addresses\n- Cleanup path destroys UI controls if initialization fails",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
