      "name": "InitializeGraphicsState",
      "signature": "void InitializeGraphicsState(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes graphics state by validating game state requirements and configuring graphics display mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call graphics mode initialization (FUN_6fa51cb0)\n2. Initialize graphics display mode to 0 (default)\n3. Validate game state requirements via ValidateGameStateRequirements()\n4. If validation fails (non-zero return), set display mode to 2 (alternate)\n5. Call additional initialization (FUN_6fa54920)\n6. Set up graphics vtable with computed display mode via CallGraphicsVtableWithParam_0x38()\n7. Call finalization routine (FUN_6fa58160)\n\nParameters:\n  None - Uses global game state structures\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Display mode 0: Default/successful validation path\n  - Display mode 2: Failed validation fallback mode\n  - Graphics buffer is 260 bytes, passed to vtable setup function",
