      "name": "InitializeGameEngine",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameEngine(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initialize the game engine including game state, graphics, and resource validation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if network error flag is set; if so, abort with error message\n2. Initialize game state to 0\n3. Call graphics initialization routine (FUN_6fa55d30)\n4. Call graphics mode initialization (FUN_6fa51cb0)\n5. Initialize game state and check if successful\n6. If initialization fails, return early\n7. Validate graphics state requirements\n8. Set up graphics display mode (0 or 2) based on validation result\n9. Call graphics setup with computed parameters\n10. Load game resources (FUN_6fa52940)\n11. If resource loading fails, initialize expansion MPQ validation\n12. Validate expansion data (FUN_6fa528d0)\n13. If validation succeeds, perform post-processing (FUN_6fa52770)\n14. Finalize and exit with state 1\n\nParameters:\n  None - Uses global game state structures\n\nReturns:\n  void - Does not return (calls exit routine at end)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - 0x35b: Network error flag offset in global game state\n  - 0x8d1: Return address parameter for error handling\n  - 0x0/0x2: Graphics display mode values (0=default, 2=alternate)\n  - Graphics initialization can fail and trigger alternate mode",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
