      "name": "ValidateAndDispatchCommand",
      "signature": "uint ValidateAndDispatchCommand(int bInitialize)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Validates command input strings and dispatches command execution or error handling.\n\nValidates three Unicode strings: first string length (2-15 chars), compares second and third strings (case-insensitive), and validates second string length (2-20 chars). If all validation passes, executes the command via FUN_6fa584d0(). On any validation failure, dispatches appropriate error code (0x1460-0x1464) to error handler and displays error message.\n\nParameters:\n  bInitialize: Initialization flag. If non-zero, skips early cleanup and proceeds to string validation. If zero, calls initialization routine FUN_6fa59290() and returns immediately.\n\nReturns:\n  Always returns 1 (uint) indicating function completed.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Load initialization flag from stack parameter\n  2. If flag is zero: call FUN_6fa59290() for cleanup/initialization and exit with return value 1\n  3. Load global UI control references from memory\n  4. Retrieve three Unicode string pointers via ValidateAndGetObjectField() calls\n  5. Validate first string: strlen(pFirstString) must be between 2 and 15 (0x2 < length < 0x10)\n  6. If first string length invalid: dispatch error code 0x1460 or 0x1461 and display error\n  7. Compare second and third strings case-insensitive using stricmp()\n  8. If strings don't match: dispatch error code 0x1462 and display error\n  9. Validate second string: strlen(pSecondString) must be between 2 and 20 (0x2 < length < 0x15)\n  10. If second string length invalid: dispatch error code 0x1463 or 0x1464 and display error\n  11. If all validation passes: call FUN_6fa584d0() to execute validated command\n  12. Restore stack frame (POP EDI, ESI, EBX) and return 1\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Error codes: 0x1460=first string too short, 0x1461=first string too long, 0x1462=string mismatch, 0x1463=second string too short, 0x1464=second string too long\n  String lengths: First (2-15), Second/Third (2-20 for comparison)\n  Uses case-insensitive string comparison (stricmp) for authentication or password validation",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
