      "name": "InitializeGameStateAndUI",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameStateAndUI(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes the game state and UI controls at startup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calls FUN_6fa55d30 to perform initial cleanup\n2. Iterates through control array (DAT_6fa653c0) and destroys each UI control using DestroyUIControl\n3. Resets DAT_6fa65e34 counter to 0\n4. Calls FUN_6fa51cb0 (likely state reset)\n5. Calls InitializeGameState to initialize base game state\n6. If game state initialization successful, calls ValidateGameStateRequirements to verify state\n7. If validation fails (EAX == 0), sets resultStatus to 2 (error flag)\n8. Calls FUN_6fa54920 (state processing)\n9. Calls graphics vtable function at offset 0x38 with stack buffer and resultStatus\n10. Calls InitializeGameState(1) with parameter 1 to finalize initialization\n11. Calls FUN_6fa51cb0 again for final state reset\n12. Calls FUN_6fa58900 for final processing\n13. Returns to caller\n\nParameters:\n  None (implicit parameters passed on stack by caller)\n\nReturns:\n  void (no return value in EAX)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Function uses RET 0x8 indicating caller passes 2 hidden parameters on stack\n  - Stack buffer stackBuffer (260 bytes) used for graphics initialization data\n  - DAT_6fa65e34 is a global counter for active UI controls\n  - resultStatus defaults to 0 (success); only set to 2 on validation failure\n  - Control array is assumed to be array of 4-byte pointers starting at DAT_6fa653c0",
