      "name": "InitializeGameResources",
      "signature": "int InitializeGameResources(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initialize game resources with retry logic.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Cleanup existing resource handles to prevent conflicts\n2. First attempt: call InitializeResourceBuffers with config data (DAT_6fa65abc)\n3. Check if initialization succeeded (status code 0 = failure)\n4. On failure: retry InitializeResourceBuffers with same parameters\n5. Call FUN_6fa599c0 for post-initialization processing\n6. Return success code (1)\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nint - Always returns 1 (success code)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Initialization failure triggers automatic retry once\n- Config data loaded from global DAT_6fa65abc\n- Post-initialization function called regardless of initial retry\n\nStructure Layout:\nThis function manages initialization of core game resource systems through a two-stage process: cleanup of existing state followed by buffer initialization with automatic fallback.",
