      "name": "InitializeGameSystems",
      "signature": "int InitializeGameSystems(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Orchestrates initialization of all core game systems.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize all game object timing systems (animation frames, cooldown tracking)\n2. Initialize first major game subsystem (game mechanics/state)\n3. Initialize second major game subsystem (player/entity management)\n4. Return success status (1)\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nint - Success indicator (1 = success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- No parameters required; operates on global game state\n- Each initialization call must complete successfully for proper game setup\n- Return value is always 1; actual failure state may be internal to subsystems\n\nStructure Layout:\nThis function acts as the orchestration point for a three-phase initialization sequence.\nEach called function initializes distinct game subsystems and their dependencies.",
