      "name": "InitializeGameStateAndRender",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameStateAndRender(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes game state and rendering system with complex branching logic.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate project name string match against stored project path (0x6fa65758)\n2. If project name mismatch, attempt to initialize ordinal 10054 and check result\n3. Call rendering initialization (FUN_6fa54c60) and ordinal 10018 setup\n4. Set rendering state flag (DAT_6fa65e80 = 0)\n5. Branch on project state:\n   - If no project name: Clear project flags at +0x229 and +0xd1, exit\n   - If project name exists: Validate project handler exists via ordinal 10056 at +0x44\n6. If project handler valid and not type 8:\n   - Copy project name to buffers at +0x229 and +0xd1 (0x100 bytes each)\n   - Call ordinal 10035 with handler pointer+1\n   - Process rendering queue via FUN_6fa55740\n   - Check result from FUN_6fa53a40 - if 0 or >=3, early exit\n7. Check ordinal 10036 state value:\n   - If value 0xA-0xC: Dispatch command handler via FUN_6fa55090\n   - If value 2: Process default state\n   - Other values: Dispatch via FUN_6fa59fa0\n8. If ordinal 10054 succeeds:\n   - Initialize game object state: Copy flags, set fields at +0x3bd/+0x3be/+0x3c7\n   - Call ordinal 10039 with mode flags\n   - Process rendering via FUN_6fa53880\n   - If rendering state flag set, exit\n9. Final dispatch: Switch on ordinal 10036 state value with jump table at 0x6fa5a7a0\n10. Initialize rendering state and exit\n\nParameters: None\nReturns: void\nSpecial Cases: Complex Unicode string handling (512-byte buffers), multiple ordinal calls\nfor external library functionality, Unicode constructor initialization for safety\nStructure Layout: Accesses game state at DAT_6fa65abc with fields at +0x229 (project name),\n+0xd1 (project flags), +0x3bd-+0x3be (state flags), +0x1eb (mode flags)",
