      "name": "InitializeDisplayState",
      "signature": "void InitializeDisplayState(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes display/rendering state based on current application state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if initial setup (FUN_6fa519f0) returns 1 and state not yet initialized\n2. If so, call dispatch command handler and return early\n3. Validate and extract object field data, converting to UTF string\n4. Check if state byte at offset 0x1ea is 0x05 or 0x06 and set flag at 0x1eb\n5. Check rendering state flag (0x1eb & 0x20): if set, mark state as 0x1\n6. Check if state has abort flag (0x1eb & 0x04): if yes, call cleanup handler\n7. Process state value (DAT_6fa65ad4) with 4 cases:\n   - Case 0: Setup initial render, set state to 1, clear offset 0x15\n   - Case 2: Similar to 0 but set state to 3 instead\n   - Case 3: Full initialization, copy memory, set state to 4, configure flags\n   - Case 1: Call specialized state handler\n8. Set final rendering flags based on state bits\n9. Initialize rendering system\n\nParameters:\nNone (uses global state DAT_6fa65abc, DAT_6fa65ad4, DAT_6fa65ad0, DAT_6fa65e70)\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Offset 0x1ea contains mode byte (0x05 = special mode A, 0x06 = special mode B)\n- Offset 0x1eb contains control flags (0x20 = render enabled, 0x04 = abort requested)\n- Global state DAT_6fa65ad4 determines processing path (0-3)\n- Final rendering flags at offset 0x205 vary based on state bits\n- 256-byte Unicode buffer allocated on stack for string conversion",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
