      "name": "ProcessGameCommand",
      "signature": "int ProcessGameCommand(char commandCode, char * commandString)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Processes game commands and manages game state transitions\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Copy source string content to game context offset +0xb9\n2. Copy command string parameter to game context offset +0xd1\n3. Store BX register value at game context offset +0x1eb\n4. Call FUN_6fa51aa0 for command preprocessing\n5. Check game state value (DAT_6fa65ad4):\n   - If state == 1 or 3: Call vtable method at DAT_6fa656c4 offset +0x68\n   - If that returns 0: Initialize command queue and rendering\n   - If initialization fails: Return 0 (failure)\n6. If state == 0: Set idle state flag at offset +0x35a = 1, zero offset +0x15\n7. If state == 2: Set state flag at offset +0x35a = 3\n8. If state != 0 and != 2: Check if command string is empty\n   - If empty: Set idle/menu state flags and initialize rendering flags\n   - If non-empty: Process actual command input (unicode conversion, dispatch handler)\n9. Apply rendering flags based on BX register bit 2 and offset +0x1eb bit 5\n10. Initialize rendering state and return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\ncommandCode (char): Command type or trigger flag (0=no command, non-zero=has command)\ncommandString (char *): Pointer to command string to process\n\nReturns:\nint: 0 on failure or special conditions, 1 on successful state processing\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic values: 0x46 (escape key), 0x7b (123), 0x145b/0x145c (command codes)\nRendering flags: 0x4 (base), 0x804 (high quality), 0x100000 (special effect)\nGlobal state indices: 0=idle, 1=loading, 2=game, 3=transition",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
