      "name": "InitializeGameState",
      "signature": "int InitializeGameState(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes game state from configuration data retrieved from an external object field.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Retrieves Unicode configuration string from an object field\\n2. Converts Unicode string to UTF-8 format into a 1024-byte buffer\\n3. Validates string is not empty (null terminator check)\\n4. Parses configuration string using _sscanf format: \\\"%d_%d_%d_%d\\\"\\n5. If parsing fails (not 4 values), resolves network address and uses as fallback\\n6. Applies address/configuration data to game state global buffer\\n7. Clears rendering queue and calls main game command handler (Ordinal_10034)\\n8. Executes rendering queue with specified rendering function pointer\\n9. Checks render result flag (DAT_6fa6550c) to determine success/failure\\n10. If render failed: calls cleanup routines (Ordinal_10026, FUN_6fa52b60)\\n11. If render succeeded: initializes game object timings, display settings, and loads game data\\n12. Returns 1 (success status)\\n\\nParameters:\\nNone\\n\\nReturns:\\nint - Always returns 1 (success code)\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Empty configuration string: function returns early with success\\n- sscanf parsing failure: attempts network address resolution fallback\\n- Network address NULL: calls ConvertStringToUnicodeAndProcess error handler\\n- Render failure (DAT_6fa6550c != 0): triggers cleanup and alternative initialization path\\n- Success case initializes additional game state: DAT_6fa65ad4=2, skill timings, graphics",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:048428000256f0f55a4f95f80309f4a54abb7c8b71aecc73ef6da4eae3275261",
