      "name": "ValidateGameSaveDiskSpace",
      "signature": "uint ValidateGameSaveDiskSpace(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Validates that sufficient disk space exists before saving game data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve current entity mode flags to determine if save is permitted\n2. Build the save game directory path into stack buffer\n3. Scan path string to find directory separator (\\) character\n4. Null-terminate path at directory separator (discard filename)\n5. Query disk statistics for save directory using GetDiskFreeSpaceA API\n6. Calculate total available disk space: (bytes_per_sector) * (sectors_per_cluster) * (free_clusters)\n7. Compare available space against minimum threshold (5000 bytes)\n8. If insufficient space (< 5000 bytes):\n   - Set error code 0x6fa59fa0\n   - Call dispatch_command_handler to retrieve command context\n   - Call FUN_6fa54f90 to process error handler with command and error code\n9. If sufficient space (>= 5000 bytes):\n   - Call ModifyObjectBitfield to update game object state\n   - Call FUN_6fa5a800 to proceed with save operation\n\nParameters:\nNone - Function uses internal state and global pointers\n\nReturns:\nuint - Always returns 1 (success status, regardless of disk space result)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Entity mode flags must be non-zero for save attempt; otherwise skips entire validation\n- Path buffer is 1024 bytes (0x400); search loop enforces bounds check\n- Disk space threshold of 5000 bytes (0x1388) is hardcoded minimum requirement\n- Function returns success (1) even when disk space is insufficient; error handling delegated to error callback\n- GetDiskFreeSpaceA fills output parameters with: sectors_per_cluster, bytes_per_sector, free_clusters, total_clusters",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:c41bb34ce56cbb6834e56e7a32a9cd2e763a37ff29ee74fc1fd02ce6b7f437e4",
