      "name": "CompareObjectFieldsAndModifyBitfield",
      "signature": "void CompareObjectFieldsAndModifyBitfield(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Compares two object fields and modifies a bitfield based on the comparison results.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load two global object references from fixed memory addresses\n2. Validate and retrieve the first Unicode string field using ValidateAndGetObjectField\n3. Validate and retrieve the second Unicode string field using ValidateAndGetObjectField\n4. Call strlen on the first string through function pointer at 0x6fa5c050\n5. Compare string length result: set ESI to 1 if length > 0, else 0\n6. Call strlen on the second string through function pointer at 0x6fa5c050\n7. Compare string length result: set EDX to 1 if length > 0, else 0\n8. Combine results: ESI |= EDX (bitwise OR)\n9. Pass combined boolean result to ModifyObjectBitfield and jump to that function\n10. Function does not return (tail-call to ModifyObjectBitfield)\n\nParameters:\nNone (uses global state at 0x6fa65e84, 0x6fa65e88, 0x6fa65e8c)\n\nReturns:\nIndirect via ModifyObjectBitfield (tail-call, no direct return)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Global memory addresses 0x6fa65e84, 0x6fa65e88, 0x6fa65e8c hold object references\n- Function pointer at 0x6fa5c050 is called with ECX parameter (likely Unicode::strlen)\n- Uses SETG instruction to convert sign comparison to boolean (1 if positive, 0 otherwise)\n- Result is OR'd together: condition is true if EITHER string length is > 0\n- __stdcall convention: stack cleaned by callee",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
