      "name": "HandleGameStateExit",
      "signature": "int HandleGameStateExit(int pGameState)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Handles exiting current game state and transitioning to main menu or previous state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Dispatch initial command handler with state identifier 0x2b5e\n2. Destroy all active UI controls to clear current interface\n3. Enqueue and process game command 0x119, modify entity bit flags\n4. Configure first state transition (0x2b61) with function pointer 0x6fa4f790\n5. Enqueue and process game command 0x11b, modify entity bit flags\n6. Configure second state transition (0x13ef) with function pointer 0x6fa54de0\n7. Enqueue and process game commands 0x11c and 0x11f, modify flags for each\n8. Render Unicode text message to display state change\n9. Return success status (1)\n\nParameters:\npGameState (EDI) - Game state context or identifier, passed implicitly\n\nReturns:\nint - Status code, 1 for success\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic numbers represent command codes: 0x2b5e (dispatch), 0x119, 0x11b, 0x11c, 0x11f (state transitions)\nGlobal addresses store state configuration: 0x6fa64448, 0x6fa64444, 0x6fa64450 (first transition)\n                                          0x6fa64478, 0x6fa64474, 0x6fa64480 (second transition)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
