      "name": "ProcessGameInitializationSequence",
      "signature": "void ProcessGameInitializationSequence(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Processes the game initialization command sequence, executing 10 sequential commands.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Clear initialization flag and initialize command queue structure\\n2. Check if queue position exceeds limit (0x40=64); abort if exceeded\\n3. Execute command 1 from global array (0x6fa64580), store result at queue[pos]\\n4. Dispatch command handler (const 0x2b55) and render text box UI\\n5. Check queue limit before command 2; proceed if within bounds\\n6. Execute command 2-4 sequence with queue position increments and UI updates\\n7. Execute command 5 with field setter flag (0x6fa4fbe0) applied to result\\n8. Execute command 6-7 sequence with nested queue checks and field operations\\n9. Execute command 8 with field setter applied (result stored at 0x6fa65e88)\\n10. Execute command 9 (0x6fa646a0) and final validation sequence\\n11. On queue overflow at any stage: abort with error message and exit code -1\\n12. Otherwise: set active UI control, link structures bidirectionally\\n13. Retrieve and validate two text fields from entity objects\\n14. Apply string length checks and bitfield modifications to entity\\n\\nParameters:\\n  None - All command data accessed through global command array pointers\\n\\nReturns:\\n  void - Function never returns to caller; delegates to final handler or exits via _exit()\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n  Commands 5, 7, 8 trigger special field setter operation (0x6fa4fbe0)\\n  Magic constants 0x2b55-0x2b58 passed to command handlers\\n  Queue overflow boundary at 0x40 (64) checked after each command\\n  Final validation path involves bidirectional structure linking\\n  Text field validation uses string length calculation with bitfield OR\\n  Function must be called only once during game initialization\\n\\nCalling Context:\\n  Called from DispatchGameCommand to orchestrate multi-step game initialization\\n  Expects no parameters; uses global game state and command arrays\\n  On failure, terminates process with CleanupAndAbort error handler",
