      "name": "InitializeBattleNetCommandSequence",
      "signature": "void InitializeBattleNetCommandSequence(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes BattleNet UI controls by processing a sequence of 13 game commands.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check BattleNet initialization status via virtual function call at DAT_6fa656c4[0x68]\n2. If not initialized (return 0), dispatch command handler and return early\n3. If initialized (return non-zero), verify command queue has space (max 64 entries)\n4. Load queue counter from DAT_6fa65e30 and verify counter < 0x40\n5. Process 13 sequential game command requests from static addresses 0x6fa64a90 to 0x6fa64d60\n6. For each command: call ProcessGameCommand, store result in queue array at DAT_6fa652b8[counter*4]\n7. Increment DAT_6fa65e30 counter after each command and verify space for next command\n8. Dispatch UI updates via dispatch_command_handler and RenderTextBoxUnicodeText between groups\n9. Store command results in global registers: DAT_6fa6555c, DAT_6fa65560, DAT_6fa65568, DAT_6fa65564\n10. Configure four bi-directional UI control links via LinkStructuresBidirectional (4 calls)\n11. Perform final BattleNet email validation via ValidateEmailAddress\n12. Abort with error message on queue overflow: \"Can't connect to Battle.Net... Try\"\n\nParameters:\nNone - uses global variables for initialization state and queue storage\n\nReturns:\nvoid - no return value; aborts on queue overflow with _exit(-1)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nQueue overflow limit: 0x40 (64 commands maximum)\nEarly termination: If initialization flag not set, returns after dispatch_command_handler\nCommand source addresses: Sequential pairs at 0x6fa64a90, 0x6fa64ac0, 0x6fa64af0, 0x6fa64b20, 0x6fa64b50, 0x6fa64b80, 0x6fa64bb0, 0x6fa64be0, 0x6fa64c10, 0x6fa64c40, 0x6fa64c70, 0x6fa64d00, 0x6fa64d30, 0x6fa64d60\nGlobal queue array: DAT_6fa652b8 (grows as counter increments)\nOffset calculation: DAT_6fa65abc[0x89] used during command 5 processing\nUI linking: Creates circular reference chain between four command results",
