      "name": "InitializeGameUICommand",
      "signature": "int InitializeGameUICommand(int commandMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes the game UI and processes commands based on mode flag.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Read commandMode parameter from stack\n2. If commandMode is 0, call fallback initialization and return\n3. Retrieve current entity mode flags via GetEntityModeFlags()\n4. If entity mode is inactive, return success (1)\n5. Load 4 Unicode string pointers from global object fields\n6. Compare fourth and third Unicode strings (validation check)\n7. If strings match, initialize Unicode buffer array to default state\n8. If strings don't match, proceed to string conversion:\n   a. Convert first Unicode string to ASCII buffer1 (256 bytes)\n   b. Convert second Unicode string to ASCII buffer2 (256 bytes)\n   c. Convert third Unicode string to ASCII buffer3 (256 bytes)\n   d. Convert fourth Unicode string to unicodeBuffer (512 bytes)\n   e. Call vtable function at DAT_6fa656c4+0x68 for validation\n   f. If validation passes, call vtable function at DAT_6fa656c4+0xc0\n   g. If secondary check passes, initialize UI and return 1\n   h. Otherwise dispatch command, initialize BattleNet UI, return 0\n9. If all checks fail, dispatch command, destroy UI, enqueue game commands\n10. Set global UI state variables with constants (0xd, 0x13ee)\n11. Enqueue additional game commands and set entity flags\n12. Render UI text and return 1\n\nParameters:\ncommandMode (int): Command/mode identifier (0 for fallback, nonzero for standard processing)\n\nReturns:\nint: Status code (1 for success, 0 for alternate path, 1 for error recovery)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic constants 0xd and 0x13ee written to global addresses 0x6fa64414/0x6fa64418\nLocal stack allocation is 0x500 (1280) bytes for string buffers\nRelies on unaffected EDI register for entity handle throughout function\nMultiple validation checks against Unicode string comparisons",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
