      "name": "ValidateAndProcessSaveFile",
      "signature": "undefined4 ValidateAndProcessSaveFile(undefined4 gameMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "int",
      "comment": "Validates and processes a save game file by checking header integrity and file size bounds.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Build the save game file path based on game mode\n2. Format the filename using game mode parameter\n3. Create/open the save file with exclusive access\n4. Return error if file creation fails\n5. Read first 0x2000 bytes of file data\n6. Validate bytes read >= 8 bytes\n7. Check magic number at offset 0x604 (0xaa55aa55)\n8. Get header size from offset 0x608\n9. For files with 0x82-0x2000 bytes: set 0x20 flag, seek to start, write processed data\n10. For files with > 0x14f bytes: set 0x20 flag, compute checksum, seek to start, write\n11. Write result back to file\n12. Close file and return write result or 0 on error\n\nParameters:\n  gameMode (undefined4): Game mode identifier used to construct save file path\n\nReturns:\n  undefined4: Result from WriteFileThunk on success, 0 on validation failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Files smaller than 8 bytes fail validation\n  - Header magic number must match 0xaa55aa55\n  - Header size field must be <= 0x5b or > 0x14f\n  - File size bounds checked: 0x82 for small files, 0x14f for large files\n  - Checksum computation triggered for large files > 0x14f bytes",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:1091b185ddce01bdeed4026c6b0b1b06130c190ff0fa4c83c01ffe353f51586a",
