      "name": "LoadSaveGameCharacter",
      "signature": "uint LoadSaveGameCharacter(int characterIndex, char * characterName)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Loads a save game character file and formats character data for processing.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Validate character name parameter is not empty\\n2. Build the save game file path using character index and name\\n3. Open the save game file for reading\\n4. Read 0x2000 bytes (8KB) of save game data\\n5. Validate magic number (0xaa55aa55) confirming valid save format\\n6. Check version offset field (versionOffset) to determine data layout\\n7. If versionOffset &lt; 0x5c: copy class data from lower version offsets (+0x636 to +0x646)\\n8. If versionOffset &gt;= 0x5c and &lt;= 0x60: copy class data from higher version offsets (+0x698 to +0x6a8)\\n9. Verify file size matches expected bytes for detected version\\n10. Encode character class ID using EncodeValueAsSignedBytes\\n11. Copy class name from source (11 bytes) or use default class names\\n12. Copy second character data block (11 bytes) with experience/mode bytes\\n13. Encode experience value and padding bytes\\n14. Set terminator bytes (0xff 0xff 0xff 0x00)\\n15. Close save game file\\n16. Return 1 on success, 0 on any validation failure\\n\\nParameters:\\n  characterIndex: Character slot number (0-N) to identify which character file\\n  characterName: Character name string to construct save game filename\\n\\nReturns:\\n  1 if character data successfully loaded and formatted\\n  0 if file not found, validation failed, or format error detected\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n  - Empty character name triggers error handler\\n  - Version offset determines data layout (two possible memory locations)\\n  - Default class names used if class name field is null\\n  - File must be exactly 0x2000 bytes and contain valid magic number",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
