      "name": "DeleteFilesInDirectory",
      "signature": "void DeleteFilesInDirectory(char * filePattern, char * basePath)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Deletes all non-directory files matching a pattern in the save game directory.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate that filePattern parameter is not empty\n2. Build the save game directory base path\n3. If basePath exists and is not empty, format directory path and create directories recursively\n4. Format the full search pattern combining directory and file pattern\n5. Call FindFirstFileA to start searching for files\n6. Loop through all matching files with FindNextFileA:\n   a. Format the full file path for current match\n   b. Get file attributes to determine if it's a directory\n   c. If it's a directory (FILE_ATTRIBUTE_DIRECTORY = 0x10), skip to next file\n   d. If it's a regular file, call DeleteFileA to remove it\n   e. If FindNextFileA returns 0 (no more files), exit cleanly\n   f. If DeleteFileA returns 0 (failure), exit with error\n7. Return after all files processed or on first error\n\nParameters:\n- filePattern (ECX): File search pattern (e.g., \"*.sav\")\n- basePath (EAX): Base directory path; NULL or empty uses default\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Empty filePattern: calls CleanupAndAbort with error\n- NULL/empty basePath: skips directory creation\n- INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE: exits silently\n- FindNextFileA = 0: exits silently (no more files)\n- DeleteFileA = 0: exits silently (permission denied)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:5a6b78812534214b6c610cffafceac57",
