      "name": "WriteSaveGameFile",
      "signature": "int WriteSaveGameFile(int nGameStateId)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Writes the current game state to a save game file with checksum validation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 1528 bytes on stack for path and data buffers\n2. Construct save game file path via BuildSaveGamePath()\n3. Format save game filename using sprintf with state ID parameter\n4. Call CreateFileWrapper to create/open file (returns 0 on failure)\n5. Check file handle: if 0, return 0 (failure), otherwise continue\n6. Compute CRC32 checksum of 335-byte (0x14f) game state buffer at 0x6fa65570\n7. Store computed checksum at global address 0x6fa6557c\n8. Write 335 bytes of file header with WriteFileThunk\n9. Close file handle with CloseResourceHandle\n10. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\nnGameStateId: Game state identifier or slot index for save file naming\n\nReturns:\n1 if file was successfully written and closed\n0 if file creation failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Buffer size is fixed at 335 bytes (0x14f) for save game data\n- Checksum computation required before file write\n- File handle validation (non-zero check) determines success/failure path\n- Stack frame 0x5f8 (1528 bytes) includes 1024-byte buffer + 500-byte path + 4-byte checksum\n\nStructure Layout:\nSave game buffer at 0x6fa65570:\nOffset  Size  Field Name        Type      Description\n0x0     4     magic_header      uint      File header magic value\n0x4     4     version           uint      Save game format version\n0x8     4     flags             uint      Save game flags/options\n0xc     4     checksum_crc32    uint      CRC32 checksum of game state\n0x10    323   game_state_data   byte[323] Compressed game state buffer\n0x14f   -     END               -         Total: 335 bytes (0x14f)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
