      "name": "ProcessTimedCommandEvents",
      "signature": "void ProcessTimedCommandEvents(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Processes time-based command dispatch events at 1-second intervals.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear current resource state via ClearResourceState()\n2. Retrieve current tick count from GetTickCount()\n3. Calculate elapsed time since last event: current_ticks - g_LastEventTicks\n4. Check if elapsed time exceeds 1000 ms (0x3e8 milliseconds)\n5. If timeout not exceeded, skip to function exit\n6. If timeout elapsed, dispatch command event:\n   - Push 0 (third parameter, unused)\n   - Push 0 (second parameter, unused)\n   - Push 4 (first parameter, command type/priority)\n   - Load magic number 0x2b39 into ECX\n   - Call dispatch_command_handler(4, 0, 0)\n7. Render text box display using RenderTextBoxUnicodeText()\n8. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic number 0x3e8 = 1000 milliseconds timeout interval\n- Magic number 0x2b39 = Command dispatch identifier/constant\n- Global g_LastEventTicks (0x6fa65ec0) tracks last event time\n- Timeout prevents excessive command processing\n- Called regularly from main game loop for event distribution",
