      "name": "InitializeGameResources",
      "signature": "int InitializeGameResources(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes game resources by validating MPQ files, destroying existing UI controls, and creating/configuring four game entities. Calls dispatch handlers and renders three text boxes on successful initialization.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Validate D2 expansion MPQ availability\\n2. Loop through and destroy all existing UI controls stored in DAT_6fa653c0 array\\n3. Clear the entity control count (DAT_6fa65e34) to 0\\n4. Create first entity via ProcessGameCommand(&DAT_6fa63800), store in controls array\\n5. Set event target for first entity and modify entity bit flags\\n6. Check if entity count < 0x40 (max 64 entities)\\n7. Create second entity via ProcessGameCommand(&DAT_6fa63830), apply same setup\\n8. Create third entity via ProcessGameCommand(&DAT_6fa63860), apply same setup\\n9. Create fourth entity via ProcessGameCommand(&DAT_6fa63890), apply same setup\\n10. Dispatch command handler with parameters (0,0,0) three times\\n11. For each dispatch result, render text box with RenderTextBoxUnicodeText\\n12. Return 1 on success\\n13. On error (too many entities), get return address and call CleanupAndAbort with error message, then exit with code -1\\n\\nParameters:\\n(none) - Function takes no explicit parameters but accesses global state\\n\\nReturns:\\n1 - Success: All resources initialized and entities created\\nDoes not return in error case: Calls _exit(-1) which terminates process\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\nMagic constants:\\n- 0x40 (64 decimal): Maximum entity limit for UI controls array\\n- Magic ordinals: 0x58ce, 0x58cf, 0x58d0 (likely string resource IDs for text boxes)\\n- Error code: 0x60d used as parameter to GetReturnAddress for error handling\\n- Exit code: -1 passed to _exit() on resource creation failure\\n\\nStructure Layout:\\nGlobal Arrays and Pointers:\\n- DAT_6fa653c0: Array base storing entity control pointers (4 bytes per element)\\n- DAT_6fa65e34: Current count of active entity controls (dword)\\n- DAT_6fa63800, 0x6fa63830, 0x6fa63860, 0x6fa63890: Command parameter blocks (approx 48 bytes each based on 0x30 spacing)\\\"",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
