      "name": "InitializeGameCommandHandlers",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameCommandHandlers(int initializationMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes a sequence of 5 game command handlers/UI controls.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Iterate through existing controls in DAT_6fa653c0 array and destroy each one\\n2. Reset control counter DAT_6fa65e34 to 0\\n3. Create first command handler via ProcessGameCommand(&DAT_6fa62f60)\\n4. Store handle in array and increment counter\\n5. Call SetCurrentEventTarget and ModifyEntityBitFlags on first handler\\n6. If counter < 0x40, create second handler via ProcessGameCommand(&DAT_6fa62f30)\\n7. Dispatch command handler with type 7, render UI text, and set bit flags\\n8. If counter < 0x40, create third handler via ProcessGameCommand(&DAT_6fa62ea0)\\n9. If counter < 0x40, create fourth handler via ProcessGameCommand(&DAT_6fa62ed0)\\n10. If counter < 0x40, create fifth handler via ProcessGameCommand(&DAT_6fa62f00)\\n11. Call ModifyObjectBitfield and apply conditional modifications based on initializationMode and EBX register\\n12. If counter < 0x40, create final handler via ProcessGameCommand(&DAT_6fa62f90) and return\\n13. On capacity error, call error handler with code 0x60d and exit with code -1\\n\\nParameters:\\ninitializationMode (int): Mode flag affecting conditional bitfield modifications (compared at 0x6fa4a849)\\n\\nReturns:\\nvoid - Does not return on success; calls _exit(-1) on array capacity exceeded\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Array capacity limit: 0x40 (64 handlers maximum)\\n- Capacity checks occur after each handler creation\\n- Error handler triggered if any capacity check fails (jumps to 0x6fa4a86f)\\n- Conditional logic at 0x6fa4a849-0x6fa4a862 gates second bitfield modification based on initializationMode and EBX value\\n- EBX is unaffected register containing value used in comparison against 0x8 and 0xa\\n\\nControl Array Layout:\\nOffset  Size  Field Name            Type      Description\\n0       4     handler_0             uint32    First game command handler\\n4       4     handler_1             uint32    Second game command handler\\n8       4     handler_2             uint32    Third game command handler\\n12      4     handler_3             uint32    Fourth game command handler\\n16      4     handler_4             uint32    Fifth game command handler (final)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
