      "name": "ProcessGameStateUpdate",
      "signature": "uint ProcessGameStateUpdate(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Processes game state updates for entities and rendering.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if global state (DAT_6fa65ed0) is initialized; reset index if not\n2. Calculate current index offset from global counter minus base offset\n3. Validate index is within valid range [0, DAT_6fa64dbc)\n4. If valid, compute parity flag and call SetScreenshotParameters with parameter flags\n5. Call ModifyEntityStateBitFlags to update entity state\n6. Traverse linked entity list starting at DAT_6fa65ec8, following offset +0x34c until matching DAT_6fa64db0 index\n7. If entity found (currentEntity != NULL):\n   - Call ModifyObjectBitfield three times to update object flags\n   - Check entity flag at offset +0x324 for bit 0x20\n   - If flag set, call ModifyObjectBitfield again\n   - Call ModifyObjectBitfield to update additional state\n   - Check if DAT_6fa65ad4 == 1 and DAT_6fa65ee4 != 0, call ModifyObjectBitfield if both true\n   - Call ClearResourceState to release entity resources\n   - Call RenderTextBoxWithUnicodeConversion(0) to render UI\n   - Return 1 (success)\n8. If entity not found (currentEntity == NULL):\n   - Call ModifyObjectBitfield three times\n   - Call ModifyEntityStateBitFlags\n   - Return 1 (success)\n\nReturns:\n  uint - Always returns 1 (success status)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If DAT_6fa65ed0 is 0, index is reset to 0 before validation\n  - Index parity calculation uses bitwise AND with 0x80000001 for sign detection\n  - Entity traversal uses offset +0x34c to navigate linked structure\n  - Flag check at offset +0x324 masks with 0x20 for specific entity state",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
