      "name": "ValidateIdentifierFormat",
      "signature": "int ValidateIdentifierFormat(char * pString)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Validates if a string matches identifier format requirements.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Calculate string length by scanning to null terminator\\n2. Check if length is between 2-15 bytes (0x2-0xF)\\n3. Verify last character is not dash (-) 0x2d\\n4. Verify first character is not underscore (_) 0x5f\\n5. Return 1 if all checks pass, 0 otherwise\\n\\nParameters:\\n- pString (ESI): Pointer to null-terminated string to validate\\n  Implicit parameter passed in ESI register (unaffected register)\\n\\nReturns:\\n- EAX: 1 if string is valid identifier format, 0 otherwise\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Strings 0-1 bytes long: Invalid (too short)\\n- Strings 16+ bytes long: Invalid (too long)\\n- Strings ending with '-': Invalid (dash suffix not allowed)\\n- Strings starting with '_': Invalid (underscore prefix not allowed)\\n- Valid range: 2-15 bytes, no dash suffix, no underscore prefix\\n\\nStructure Layout:\\nString validation is performed on raw null-terminated C strings:\\n- Input string must be in memory at address in ESI\\n- Each byte checked sequentially until 0x00 terminator found\\n- Field offsets calculated: [ESI+0] = first char, [ESI+length-1] = last char",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
