      "name": "CalculateDaysRemaining",
      "signature": "uint CalculateDaysRemaining(uint expirationTime)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Calculate the number of days remaining until expiration.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve current time by calling __time32() system function\n2. Compare the provided expiration timestamp with current time\n3. If expiration time is less than or equal to current time, return 0 (already expired)\n4. Otherwise, calculate the difference in seconds (expiration - current)\n5. Divide by 86400 (0x15180) to convert seconds to days\n6. Return the number of days remaining\n\nParameters:\n- expirationTime: Timestamp (in seconds since epoch) when the item/effect expires\n\nReturns:\n- uint: Number of days remaining until expiration (0 if already expired or current >= expiration)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Returns 0 if expiration time is in the past or equal to current time\n- Magic constant 0x15180 = 86400 seconds (1 day)\n- Division result truncates to whole days; partial days not counted",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:4f92557449cd8079368c36fb535c6e27c0e19950bda37cba040910be742cabf5",
