      "name": "DispatchCommandByID",
      "signature": "void DispatchCommandByID(uint commandId)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Dispatches command execution based on command ID using jump table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate command ID is within bounds (0-6 for specific cases)\n2. Use jump table at 0x6fa49ef0 to dispatch to appropriate handler\n3. For each case, load command ID constant into ECX (0xfab-0xfa7, 0x2771, 0x2772, or 0x1507)\n4. Call dispatch_command_handler() to execute command (returns result in EAX)\n5. Store result in EDX and prepare output buffer (ESI) in ECX\n6. Jump to indirect handler at 0x6fa5c044 (likely strcpy or similar string operation)\n7. For out-of-bounds IDs (>6), use default case with command ID 0x1507\n\nParameters:\ncommandId (uint) - Command identifier (0-6 for specific commands, >6 for default)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Result is stored via indirect call at 0x6fa5c044\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Command IDs 0-5: Direct cases with handlers for skills/commands\n- Command ID 6: Additional handler case\n- ID > 6: Default case that uses command ID 0x1507\n- Jump table lookup prevents linear case statements",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
