      "name": "CopySkillNameUntilPeriod",
      "signature": "void CopySkillNameUntilPeriod(undefined4 dwUnused, char * pSourceString)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Copies characters from input string to a global destination buffer, stopping at null terminator or period character.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize destination pointer to global buffer at 0x6fa65880\n2. Load first character from source string\n3. Enter loop: read character from source string\n4. If character is null or period, jump to string termination\n5. Copy character to destination buffer\n6. Advance both source and destination pointers\n7. Read next character from source and repeat if non-null\n8. Null-terminate the destination string\n\nParameters:\n  dwUnused: Unused parameter passed in ECX register (fastcall convention)\n  pSourceString: Pointer to source string to copy (in EDX)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Terminates at either null character (normal string end) or period character (skill name delimiter)\n  - Does not validate destination buffer size (assumes caller allocates sufficient space)\n  - Destination always null-terminated regardless of termination condition\n  - Used in skill name parsing where period denotes skill level indicator",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
