      "name": "UpdateLinkedListElement",
      "signature": "void UpdateLinkedListElement(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Updates a linked list element with a specific value.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load the linked list state flag from DAT_6fa65984\n2. Test if the flag is non-zero\n3. If flag is set, load the linked list context from DAT_6fa656fc into ECX\n4. Push the element value (4) onto the stack as a parameter\n5. Call SetLinkedListElementValue with the value parameter\n6. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- The function conditionally calls SetLinkedListElementValue only when DAT_6fa65984 is non-zero\n- The value 4 is hard-coded and passed as the element value parameter\n- DAT_6fa656fc contains the linked list context pointer loaded into ECX register",
