      "name": "InitializeGameCommandSequence",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameCommandSequence(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes six sequential game command entities with boundary checking.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load current command count from DAT_6fa65e34 into EAX\n2. Compare count against limit 0x40 (64); if >= 64, jump to error handler\n3. For each of 6 predefined command structures (at 0x6fa62390, 0x6fa623c0, 0x6fa623f0, 0x6fa62420, 0x6fa62450, 0x6fa62480):\n   - Call ProcessGameCommand() to create entity instance\n   - Store entity handle in global array at 0x6fa653c0[count*4]\n   - Store entity handle in dedicated global variable (DAT_6fa65700, DAT_6fa65994, etc.)\n   - Increment command count counter (DAT_6fa65e34)\n   - Call SetCurrentEventTarget(entity, 1) to mark as current event target\n   - Call ModifyEntityBitFlags(entity, 1) to enable first bit flag (0x1)\n   - Check updated count against 0x40 limit; if overflow, jump to error handler\n4. If all 6 entities processed without overflow, function completes successfully\n5. If count reaches or exceeds 64 at any point, call GetReturnAddress() and CleanupAndAbort() with error message, then call _exit(-1)\n\nParameters:\n(none - __stdcall, no parameters)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - function does not return via normal exit if overflow occurs (calls _exit(-1))\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Array bound limit: 0x40 (64 entities maximum) - 6 entities added = minimum final count of 6\n- Each entity stored at [DAT_6fa65e34 * 4 + 0x6fa653c0] before count increment\n- Error at 0x6fa4b497 calls CleanupAndAbort with error string from 0x6fa5e256 + 0x2e offset\n- Function has unrecoverable error path that terminates entire process\n- Sequential processing ensures specific entity order in results array\n\nStructure Layout:\nGlobal command count (DAT_6fa65e34) starts at unknown base address\nGlobal entity array (DAT_6fa653c0) uses 4-byte entries (32-bit pointers)\nEach entity slot indexed by count value at time of storage",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
