      "name": "CleanupGameResources",
      "signature": "void CleanupGameResources(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Cleans up and shuts down game resources during application termination.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Check if global game state pointer (DAT_6fa65ecc) is initialized\\n2. If initialized, check screenshot state at offset 0x334\\n3. If screenshot state equals 0, clean up screenshot node using value at offset 0x338\\n4. Call InitializeModule with code 0x2a1 to begin shutdown sequence\\n5. Clear global game state pointer to null\\n6. Clear three resource state containers (ClearResourceState \\u00d7 3)\\n7. Modify object bitfield state for five different resource collections\\n8. Validate expansion MPQ file integrity (FindAndValidateD2ExpMpq)\\n9. If validation fails (return value != 0), perform additional cleanup on two object collections\\n10. If validation succeeds, call final entity state modification routine\\n11. Return to caller\\n\\nStructure Layout:\\nGlobal Game State Structure at DAT_6fa65ecc:\\nOffset  Size  Field Name          Type      Description\\n+0x000  0x4   Base pointer        pointer   Game state object base\\n+0x334  0x4   Screenshot state    int       Screenshot cleanup flag\\n+0x338  0x4   Screenshot node     pointer   Screenshot data to cleanup\\n\\nParameters:\\nNone - Function operates on global game state variables\\n\\nReturns:\\nvoid - No return value, performs cleanup as side effect\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Magic number 0x2a1: InitializeModule code for shutdown sequence\\n- Screenshot cleanup conditional: Only executed if state at +0x334 equals 0\\n- Multiple ClearResourceState calls: Ensures complete state cleanup for all managers\\n- Repeated ModifyObjectBitfield calls: Clears flags across five separate collections\\n- Conditional branching on MPQ validation: Determines additional cleanup requirements",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
