      "name": "UpdateOrCreateCacheEntry",
      "signature": "void UpdateOrCreateCacheEntry(void * this, void * pSourceBuffer, uint dataSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Updates or creates a cache entry with the given data buffer indexed by string hash.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compute string hash from input buffer (via ComputeStringHash)\n2. Search linked list of cache entries starting at global head (DAT_6fa65ef4)\n3. If entry with matching hash found: deallocate old data, allocate new buffer, copy data\n4. If no matching entry found: allocate new entry node (16 bytes), allocate data buffer, copy data\n5. Set expiration time to current tick + 300000ms (5 minutes)\n6. Insert new entry at head of linked list\n\nParameters:\n  this (ECX): Pointer to source buffer containing data to cache\n  pSourceBuffer (Stack[0x4]): Alternative parameter location (unused in main logic)\n  dataSize (Stack[0x8]): Size of data buffer to copy in bytes\n\nReturns:\n  void (callee cleanup: RET 0x4)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - String is hashed via ComputeStringHash with magic parameters 0,0\n  - Cache entries expire after 300000ms (5 minutes) from current GetTickCount()\n  - Data copy uses DWORD loop (SHR by 2) followed by byte-wise loop (AND with 3)\n  - List uses offset +0xc for next pointer, +0x4 for data pointer, +0x8 for expiration\n\nStructure Layout (Cache Entry):\n  Offset 0x00 (4 bytes): Hash value\n  Offset 0x04 (4 bytes): Pointer to data buffer\n  Offset 0x08 (4 bytes): Expiration tick (current_tick + 300000)\n  Offset 0x0c (4 bytes): Pointer to next entry (linked list chain)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
