      "name": "InitializeGameStartupSequence",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameStartupSequence(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes the game startup sequence after authentication completes.\n\nThis function is called during the login/startup phase (when DAT_6fa65eb8 transitions from 2 to 3) to set up the core game state and render the initial loading screen. It performs a sequence of initialization steps that must complete in order before the game enters the main game loop.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set startup flags: DAT_6fa65ec4 = 1 (startup active), DAT_6fa65eb8 = 0 (phase 0)\n2. Clear all resource state by calling ClearResourceState()\n3. Initialize command handler with ID 4 via dispatch_command_handler(4, 0, 0)\n4. Render loading screen text box at position (4, 0, 0)\n5. Modify object bitfield properties by calling ModifyObjectBitfield()\n6. Check if DAT_6fa65984 != 0 (cleanup element pending)\n7. If pending, call SetLinkedListElementValue(4) to process the cleanup element\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, function operates through side effects on global state\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- The function uses a state machine pattern via DAT_6fa65eb8 to coordinate initialization phases\n- DAT_6fa65984 acts as a pending flag for cleanup operations that must complete after startup\n- The dispatch_command_handler and RenderTextBoxUnicodeText are called with hardcoded value 4, indicating command ID or UI element ID 4",
