      "name": "InitializeEntityCharacterAndRenderUI",
      "signature": "int InitializeEntityCharacterAndRenderUI(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initialize entity character state, allocate game unit structures, apply stat modifiers, and render UI elements.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate MPQ file availability and check game state initialization\n2. If validation fails, trigger game state update and return success\n3. Initialize bitfield flags for UI screen management (multiple ModifyEntityStateBitFlags calls)\n4. Loop through entity chain at DAT_6fa65ec8 until reaching the target entity by index\n5. Copy source entity data to DAT_6fa65ecc buffer (0x350 bytes)\n6. Clear next pointer in copied entity to break chain\n7. Branch on entity state value (1, 2, or other):\n   - State 1: Clear resource state directly\n   - State 2: Skip unit allocation, proceed to UI rendering\n   - Other: Allocate new unit structure based on class and flags\n8. If unit allocation returns zero, initialize fallback memory area with padding bytes\n9. Apply character stat modifiers and compute final bitfield flags based on entity flags\n10. Initialize Unicode buffers and format entity name string\n11. Dispatch command handler and build UI text output (command name + entity type + text buffer)\n12. Render Unicode text in UI\n13. Check final validity flag and apply final bitfield operation if needed\n14. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\nNone (uses global game state variables)\n\nReturns:\nint: Always returns 1 (success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Handles allocation failure by initializing fallback memory structure\n- Different entity state values (1, 2, other) trigger different initialization paths\n- Bitfield flags computed based on multiple entity flag bits (0x4, 0x8, 0x20)\n- Unicode conversion applied to entity name for display\n- Final check on bit 0x20 of entity flags determines if final bitfield operation occurs\n\nStructure Layout (Entity Buffer at DAT_6fa65ecc, 0x350+ bytes):\nOffset  Size  Field Name              Type    Description\n0x300   16    unit_slot_data          char[]  Unit initialization buffer\n0x310   16    unit_type_data          char[]  Unit type/attribute buffer  \n0x320   1     unit_class              byte    Character class (0-7)\n0x324   2     entity_flags            word    Flags controlling initialization (bits 0x4,0x8,0x20)\n0x330   4     entity_state_value      int     State discriminant (1=direct, 2=skip alloc, other=alloc)\n0x334   4     entity_status           int     Status field (0=allocated, 1=ready, 2=error)\n0x338   4     unit_pointer            dword   Pointer to allocated unit structure\n0x34c   4     next_entity_pointer     dword   Next entity in chain (cleared after copy)\n",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
