      "name": "ResetGameScreenshotsAndAudio",
      "signature": "void ResetGameScreenshotsAndAudio(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Resets all screenshot nodes and audio system state during game shutdown.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load first screenshot linked list from global DAT_6fa65ec8\n2. If list is non-null, iterate through all nodes:\n   - Retrieve next node pointer from current node at offset +0x34c\n   - Call CleanupScreenshotNode on screenshot data at offset +0x338 with flag 1\n   - Call InitializeModule(0x52d, 0) to reset audio subsystem for this node\n   - Move to next node and continue loop until null\n3. Clear all screenshot-related global state variables:\n   - DAT_6fa65ec8 (first screenshot list head)\n   - DAT_6fa65ed0 (screenshot counter or state)\n   - DAT_6fa65ed4 (screenshot state variable)\n   - DAT_6fa65ee4 (screenshot state variable)\n4. Check if second screenshot structure at DAT_6fa65ecc exists\n5. If exists, check if field at offset +0x334 is zero (validation flag):\n   - If zero, call CleanupScreenshotNode on data at offset +0x338 with flag 1\n6. Call InitializeModule(0x2a1, 0) to finalize audio subsystem shutdown\n7. Clear second screenshot structure pointer (DAT_6fa65ecc = 0)\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- First screenshot list is traversed until null terminator found\n- Second screenshot structure has conditional cleanup based on validation flag at +0x334\n- Magic value 0x52d (1325) used for audio subsystem reset per-node\n- Magic value 0x2a1 (673) used for final audio subsystem shutdown\n- All global state cleared regardless of whether lists were populated",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:12c1b146b21572fe6692e3bffd1041e1cb9abf086c03d9d4b4884929a04d591f",
