      "name": "SearchAndActivateListElement",
      "signature": "void SearchAndActivateListElement(char * pSearchString)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Searches a linked list for a string match and activates the corresponding element.\n\nThis function iterates through a table of pointers in DAT_6fa65e74, dereferencing each\npointer to get a linked list element. It compares the element's value against the search\nstring parameter passed in EBX using case-insensitive comparison. When a match is found,\nthe corresponding list element is activated.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if global DAT_6fa65984 is non-zero (list enabled flag)\n2. Initialize slot index counter (ESI) to 0\n3. Compare slot index against list size in DAT_6fa65e78\n4. If slot index >= size, exit with element value of 0\n5. Load element table address from DAT_6fa65e74\n6. Get pointer from table at index [ESI * 4]\n7. Check if pointer is null; if null, abort with error message\n8. Dereference pointer to get first element value (offset 0)\n9. If element value is 0, exit loop\n10. Call CompareStringsIgnoreCase(pSearchString, elementValue, 0x7fffffff)\n11. If comparison returns 0 (match found), call SetLinkedListElementValue(1)\n12. Increment slot index ESI and repeat from step 3\n\nParameters:\nEBX (implicit): Pointer to null-terminated search string for case-insensitive match\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Activates matching list element as side effect\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If DAT_6fa65984 is 0, function exits immediately (list disabled)\n- If any element pointer is NULL, aborts with error \"Can't connect to Battle.Net\"\n- Uses 0x7fffffff as maximum length for string comparison\n- Compares against first value in each list element\n\nStructure Layout:\nList Element (inferred):\nOffset 0, Size 4, Value, Pointer/dword, Element value or string pointer",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
