      "name": "ClearCharacterCacheAndCleanup",
      "signature": "void ClearCharacterCacheAndCleanup(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Deallocates all character cache entries from the linked list and clears the cache head pointer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load cache list head from global DAT_6fa65ef4\n2. If cache list is empty (head is null), skip deallocation loop\n3. For each cache entry in linked list:\n   a. Load next pointer from offset +0xc before deallocation\n   b. Deallocate data buffer (pointer at offset +0x4) - line 0x10c\n   c. Deallocate cache entry node itself - line 0x10d\n   d. Move to next entry and repeat until list is empty\n4. Clear cache head pointer to null\n5. Call FUN_6fa52070 for additional cleanup\n\nParameters:\n   None (void function)\n\nReturns:\n   void (callee cleanup: RET 0x0)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n   - Cache entries must be deallocated in correct order: data buffer first, then node\n   - Next pointer must be saved before node deallocation to avoid use-after-free\n   - Global DAT_6fa65ef4 is the head of a linked list of 16-byte cache entry nodes\n   - Line numbers 0x10c and 0x10d are memory pool deallocator identifiers\n\nStructure Layout (Cache Entry Node):\n   Offset 0x00 (4 bytes): Hash value\n   Offset 0x04 (4 bytes): Pointer to data buffer (must deallocate first)\n   Offset 0x08 (4 bytes): Expiration tick value\n   Offset 0x0c (4 bytes): Pointer to next entry in linked list (16 bytes total)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
