      "name": "SearchStringInList",
      "signature": "int SearchStringInList(char * searchString)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Searches for a string in a global list of strings using case-insensitive comparison.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize loop counter (ESI) to 0\n2. Compare counter with list count at DAT_6fa65e78\n3. If counter >= count, jump to return not found (handles empty list)\n4. Load array base pointer from DAT_6fa65e74\n5. Access array element at [base + counter * 4] to get string pointer\n6. Check if pointer is null; if so, call CleanupAndAbort with error message\n7. Load string value from pointer (first DWORD at pointer address)\n8. If value is 0 (null terminator), jump to return not found\n9. Compare current string with searchString using CompareStringsIgnoreCase\n10. If comparison returns 0 (match found), jump to return 1\n11. Increment counter and repeat from step 2\n\nParameters:\nsearchString (EDI) - Pointer to null-terminated string to search for\n\nReturns:\nEAX = 1 if string found in list, 0 if not found or list is empty\nAborts with error message if any array element is a null pointer\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Uses global array at DAT_6fa65e74 with count at DAT_6fa65e78\n- Case-insensitive comparison via CompareStringsIgnoreCase\n- Null pointer in array triggers fatal error with abort message\n- Empty list (count = 0) returns 0 immediately",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
