      "name": "CreateAndInitializeUnit",
      "signature": "int CreateAndInitializeUnit(char * pUnitName, char * pUnitPath, int nUnitType, char nUnitClass)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Creates and initializes a new game unit entity with memory allocation and global list management.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 3012 bytes (0xbc4) for unit structure via AllocateMemoryWithTracking\n2. Initialize rendering component at offset +0x100 (256 bytes)\n3. Initialize inventory component at offset +0x100 to +0x2FF\n4. Zero out unit state array at offset +0x300 to +0x30F (16 dwords)\n5. Zero out linked list pointers at offset +0x310 to +0x31F\n6. Copy unit class flag to offset +0x320\n7. Initialize unit attributes at offsets +0x322 through +0x330\n8. Set unit type at offset +0x334\n9. Allocate and initialize unit data via AllocateAndInitializeUnit\n10. Store return value at offset +0x338\n11. Perform initialization routines on allocated unit (offsets +0x338)\n12. Link unit into global unit list by traversing to end and inserting\n13. Increment global unit counter at 0x6fa65ed0\n14. Call finalization routine\n15. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n- pUnitName: char * - Pointer to unit name string\n- pUnitPath: char * - Pointer to unit path/type string\n- nUnitType: int - Unit type identifier\n- nUnitClass: char - Unit class byte flag\n\nReturns:\n- int - 1 on successful creation, 0 on failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Global unit list initialized at 0x6fa65ec8 (NULL initially)\n- Each unit linked via offset +0x34c (next pointer)\n- Memory allocation size: 0xbc4 = 3012 bytes\n- Unit counter at 0x6fa65ed0 tracks active units\n- Returns 1 (true) in EAX indicating success\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name              Type     Description\n0x0     -     [allocation start]      -        Memory block start\n0x100   0x100 RenderComponent         data     Rendering/display data (256 bytes)\n0x200   0x100 InventoryData           data     Item/inventory storage (256 bytes)\n0x300   0x10  StateArray              dword[4] Unit state flags (4 dwords)\n0x310   0x10  LinkedListData          dword[4] List management pointers (4 dwords)\n0x320   0x1   ClassFlag               byte     Unit class identifier\n0x322   0x8   Attributes              word[4]  Unit attribute fields (4 words)\n0x32e   0x3   Reserved1               byte[3]  Reserved bytes\n0x331   0x7   Reserved2               byte[7]  Padding\n0x338   0x4   UnitPointer             dword    Pointer to allocated unit data\n0x34c   0x4   NextInList              dword    Next unit in global list\nTotal size: 0xbc4 (3012 bytes)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
