      "name": "ManageEntityDisplayRenderCycle",
      "signature": "int ManageEntityDisplayRenderCycle(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Manages the entity display rendering cycle with frame-rate controlled updates.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load global entity display counter (0x6fa64dbc) and current frame index (0x6fa65ed4)\n2. Calculate combined value: displayCounter + frameIndex\n3. Compare against maximum frame count (0x6fa65ed0)\n4. If sum >= max: skip rendering and return (early exit optimization)\n5. Load current entity slot index (0x6fa64db0)\n6. Compare against (max frame count - 1) boundary check\n7. If slot index < boundary: increment slot index and update global\n8. Increment frame index counter (0x6fa65ed4)\n9. Call RenderEntityDisplayScreen() to render current state\n10. Call InitializeEntityCharacterAndRenderUI() to update character display\n11. Return 1 (success status)\n\nParameters:\nNone - operates entirely on global state variables\n\nReturns:\nint - Always returns 1 (success status)\n\nGlobal Variables:\n- 0x6fa64dbc: Entity display counter (incremented per cycle)\n- 0x6fa64db0: Current entity/slot index (incremented when within bounds)\n- 0x6fa65ed4: Frame index counter (incremented every call)\n- 0x6fa65ed0: Maximum frame count (upper bound for counter)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- When displayCounter + frameIndex >= maxFrameCount: rendering is skipped entirely\n- Slot index increments only when less than (maxFrameCount - 1)\n- Both rendering functions are called together as a unit when condition is met",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:1592552c42ab9a2b4c1a3bf040a3859bf26c5752e35516c74617fe9af0fc6927",
