      "name": "CreateUnitFromDispatchedCommand",
      "signature": "void CreateUnitFromDispatchedCommand(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Dispatches a command and creates a new unit with initialization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Push ECX to save callee-saved register\n2. Load context constant 0x2b3b into ECX register (game context ID)\n3. Call dispatch_command_handler() with context to retrieve unit name string\n4. Load global unit counter from 0x6fa65ed0 into ECX\n5. Prepare unit class byte (0x12) and type code (0x2) on stack\n6. Get address of stack-allocated structure parameter (offset +0x8)\n7. Push unit name result (EAX) and structure address as parameters\n8. Store class/type value at [ESP + 0x10]\n9. Store global unit counter value at global 0x6fa64db8\n10. Call CreateAndInitializeUnit() with parameters: unit name, class/type structure pointer, type code 0x2, class code 0x12\n11. Pop ECX to restore register\n12. Return (stdcall: callee pops return address)\n\nParameters:\nNone - this is a standalone initialization function\n\nReturns:\nvoid - function returns no value, used for unit creation side effects\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic constant 0x2b3b is the game context ID passed to command dispatcher\n- Magic constant 0x2 is the unit type code passed to unit creation\n- Magic constant 0x12 (18 decimal) is the unit class identifier\n- Global 0x6fa65ed0 tracks active unit count (copied to 0x6fa64db8)\n- Local variable unitClassAndType is stack-allocated (offset +0x8 from ESP after PUSH)\n\nStack Layout:\nOffset  Size  Description\n+0x0    0x4   Saved ECX (callee-saved)\n+0x4    0x4   Return address\n+0x8    0x4   unitClassAndType parameter (class/type structure)",
