      "name": "CreateDefaultGameUnit",
      "signature": "void CreateDefaultGameUnit(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Creates a default game unit with dynamically selected type based on current game state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call dispatch_command_handler() with magic value 0x1419 to retrieve unit name string\n2. Store returned name pointer in ESI for later use\n3. Check global game state variable at 0x6fa65ad4 for value 1\n4. If state == 1, use magic value 0x141b to get default unit type via dispatch_command_handler()\n5. If state != 1, use magic value 0x141a (fallback unit type) via dispatch_command_handler()\n6. Load global unit counter from 0x6fa65ed0 into ECX (unit context)\n7. Store the unit counter value at global address 0x6fa64db4 (unit context storage)\n8. Call CreateAndInitializeUnit() with parameters:\n   - Parameter 1 (ESI): name pointer from step 1\n   - Parameter 2 (EAX): unit type value from step 4 or 5\n   - Parameter 3: constant 1 (success indicator)\n   - Parameter 4: constant 0xc (12 - unit class flag)\n9. Return with cleanup (POP ESI, RET)\n\nParameters:\nNone - This is a parameterless initialization routine.\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, but creates a unit as a side effect.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic values 0x1419, 0x141a, 0x141b are dispatch command codes for unit creation\n- Global state at 0x6fa65ad4 controls unit type selection (acts as game mode flag)\n- Unit counter at 0x6fa65ed0 incremented by CreateAndInitializeUnit()\n- Context value 0x6fa64db4 set before unit creation (game session tracking)\n- Always passes parameters (1, 0xc) to CreateAndInitializeUnit() indicating:\n  - nUnitType = 1 (base unit type)\n  - nUnitClass = 0xc (12 - character class identifier)",
