      "name": "ProcessAndInitializeCharacterData",
      "signature": "void ProcessAndInitializeCharacterData(uint expansionFlags, char * pConfigData, int enableCaching)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Processes and initializes character data from a configuration structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract configuration parameters from pConfigData (max count, character type byte)\n2. Validate expansion data using FindAndValidateD2ExpMpq()\n3. If validation fails, initialize default unit via dispatch_command_handler()\n4. Iterate through character count up to min(maxCharCount, configMaxCount)\n5. For each character: extract expansion ID (if type 0x19), scan name string (null-terminated)\n6. Scan path string (null-terminated), calculate offsets for each data region\n7. Call CreateAndInitializeCharacter with extracted character data\n8. On creation failure: decrement counter and call ClearCharacterCacheAndCleanup()\n9. If caching enabled, call UpdateOrCreateCacheEntry with total data size\n10. Check slot count threshold and set cache flag if condition met\n11. Compare expansion counts and initialize expansion unit if needed\n12. Call InitializeEntityCharacterAndRenderUI() for final setup\n\nParameters:\n- expansionFlags: Expansion/mode flags passed to lower-level functions\n- pConfigData: Pointer to character configuration structure containing character count, type, and character data\n- enableCaching: Flag to enable caching of character data in cache system\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Handles type 0x19 (expansion character) which has additional expansion ID field at offset +9\n- String scanning uses null-termination to find boundaries\n- Maximum character count is limited by min(maxCharCount from config, maxAllowed)\n- Cache update only occurs if enableCaching != 0\n- Expansion unit creation triggered when configured count exceeds slot count",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:8896339ac9df06a4ccc51c020c0d6c84001fb81140728e696ff82399129a1c98",
