      "name": "ProcessGameInitializationStateMachine",
      "signature": "int ProcessGameInitializationStateMachine(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Manages game initialization through a multi-stage state machine.\n\nThis function coordinates the transition between four initialization states:\n- State 1 (initial): Main game loop - processes character data and synchronizes game state\n- State 2 (transitioning): Initialization phase - performs buffer encoding and module setup\n- State 3 (module init): Module initialization - initializes game modules and configuration\n- State 0 (running): Normal execution - handles ongoing game state updates\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check initialization state stored in global DAT_6fa65eb8\n2. If state != 1:\n   - If state == 2: Execute initialization sequence with time-based UI updates (1000ms threshold)\n     - Call ClearResourceState to reset current resources\n     - Check game sync state via CheckGameSyncState\n     - If sync complete (return 0): Initialize buffer encoding via InitializeBufferEncoding\n     - If successful, transition to state 3 and call GetCurrentGameState/InitializeGameStartupSequence\n     - Return 1 to continue processing\n   - If state == 3: Execute module initialization sequence\n     - Call ClearResourceState to reset resources\n     - Call InitializeGameModule to set up game modules\n     - Retrieve global game state via GetGlobalGameState\n     - Transition to state 0 (normal operation)\n     - If DAT_6fa65984 != 0, call SetLinkedListElementValue(4)\n     - Process character data via ProcessAndInitializeCharacterData\n     - Return 1 to continue\n   - Otherwise: Return 1 (invalid state, no processing)\n3. If state == 1 (main loop):\n   - If DAT_6fa65984 != 0, call SetLinkedListElementValue(4)\n   - Call SearchAndActivateListElement to activate list items\n   - Compare character state against cached state at DAT_6fa65abc+0x229\n   - If states match and no pending updates: Proceed to callback dispatch\n   - If mismatch or pending updates: Jump to state transition (LAB_6fa4d02c)\n   - Call DispatchCallbackOrVirtualFunction for event processing\n   - Clear character data if no active character (pbVar1 == 0)\n   - Otherwise: If DAT_6fa656c4 != 0, copy character state and call ProcessObjectStateUpdate\n4. Transition to state 2 via DAT_6fa65eb8 = 2\n5. Update time checkpoint via _DAT_6fa65ec0 = GetTickCount()\n6. Return 1 to indicate continued processing\n\nParameters:\n(void) - Function takes no parameters, operates on global game state\n\nReturns:\nint - Always returns 1 to indicate state machine should continue processing\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Time-based UI refresh: When 1000ms elapsed, triggers UI update via dispatch_command_handler(4,0,0)\n- Character comparison uses byte-by-byte string comparison to detect state changes\n- If no query object available (DAT_6fa656c4 == 0), skips ProcessObjectStateUpdate\n- If query result has type 8, skips state copy operations (protection check)\n- State 0 (normal): Continues looping without state change until next event\n\nGlobal Dependencies:\nDAT_6fa65eb8 - Current initialization state (0=running, 1=main, 2=init, 3=modInit)\nDAT_6fa65ec0 - Last time checkpoint for 1000ms refresh throttle\nDAT_6fa65ebc - Current character/entity pointer\nDAT_6fa65abc - Game state structure base (contains +0x229 state cache, +0xd1 flags)\nDAT_6fa65984 - List element state flag\nDAT_6fa65e80 - Output state flag (cleared each frame)\nDAT_6fa656c4 - Query object factory/cache\nDAT_6fa656fc - List element context",
