      "name": "InitializeGameStateAndRenderUI",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameStateAndRenderUI(void * this)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes game state and renders the UI based on game mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear the screen rendering flag (DAT_6fa65ee4 = 0)\n2. Check the game state variable (DAT_6fa65ad4)\n3. If state is 1 (new game initialization):\n   - Clear all resource state\n   - Render text box with unicode conversion (parameter 0)\n   - Initialize game session and load current zone\n   - Initialize entity, character, and render UI\n   - Render entity display on screen\n   - Return\n4. If state is 0, 2, or 3 (game load/resume modes):\n   - Reset game screenshots and audio subsystem\n   - Validate Diablo II expansion MPQ files\n   - If MPQ validation fails (result == 0), create default unit\n   - Load saved game character data\n5. Initialize entity, character, and render UI\n6. Render entity display on screen\n\nParameters:\n- (implicit in EDI) Game context pointer or session data\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- State value 1 represents new game initialization\n- States 0, 2, 3 represent different load/resume scenarios\n- If FindAndValidateD2ExpMpq() returns 0, creates default unit as fallback\n- All paths converge to render UI at completion",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:c4cfe50e41a730a76ebe0d3b3a30563f6c1ab30d31f1efb6fedf5eb985d834e1",
