      "name": "ExecuteEntityCommand2",
      "signature": "int ExecuteEntityCommand2(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Executes command type 2 on the currently selected entity.\n\nThis is a wrapper function that invokes ProcessSelectedEntityCommand with a hardcoded command byte of 2. Command 2 typically represents a specific game action for the selected entity (such as selection confirmation or a predefined action).\n\nAlgorithm\n1. Push command byte 2 onto stack as parameter\n2. Call ProcessSelectedEntityCommand(2) to process the command on selected entity\n3. Move return value 1 (success) into EAX register\n4. Return to caller with RET 0x4 (callee cleanup)\n\nParameters\nNone - function takes no parameters; uses hardcoded command byte 2\n\nReturns\nint - Returns 1 to indicate successful command execution/queuing\n\nSpecial Cases\n- Function always succeeds (returns 1) regardless of whether entity selection is valid\n- Actual command processing and validation happens in ProcessSelectedEntityCommand\n- If no entity is selected, ProcessSelectedEntityCommand handles the validation",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:a1e8adb786cf8251774bd6f7c18a0ee8c62596c4ff57e443af06d1e1cf86ebf7",
