      "name": "InitializeGameCommandQueue",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameCommandQueue(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes the game command queue by processing three startup commands.\n\nThis function is called during game initialization to set up the command queue with startup commands from fixed memory locations. It processes exactly three commands in sequence and stores their results in a command queue array. The function enforces a maximum queue size of 64 commands and aborts with an error if this limit is exceeded.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FUN_6fa55d30() to perform initial setup\n2. Check if command queue counter is less than 0x40 (64)\n3. If at limit, retrieve return address and call error handler\n4. Process first startup command from 0x6fa610a0\n5. Store result in command queue array and increment counter\n6. Check if new counter is at limit; if so, jump to error handler\n7. Process second startup command from 0x6fa61040\n8. Store result in command queue array and increment counter\n9. Check if new counter is at limit; if so, jump to error handler\n10. Process third startup command from 0x6fa61070\n11. Store result in command queue array and increment counter\n12. Load palette (sky_pal.pl2) for rendering\n13. Call FUN_6fa510c0() to complete game initialization\n14. On command queue overflow, call CleanupAndAbort with error message and exit with code -1\n\nParameters:\n(none) - No parameters. Function operates on global data structures.\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function does not return on normal execution; continues to next initialization step via JMP to FUN_6fa510c0. On error (queue full), calls _exit(-1) and never returns.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Command queue size: Maximum 64 entries (0x40)\n- If any command fills the queue, error handler is called immediately\n- Three commands are always processed in order: 0x6fa610a0, 0x6fa61040, 0x6fa61070\n- Last instruction is a JMP (not RET), indicating tail-call optimization to next initialization stage\n\nData Structures:\n- Command queue array at 0x6fa652b8: array of uint32, indexed by counter at 0x6fa65e30\n- Each command source is a pointer to a command structure at fixed addresses\n- Each result is a uint32 status or return value from ProcessGameCommand",
