      "name": "InitializeUnicodeArray",
      "signature": "void InitializeUnicodeArray(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes a static wide-character array by calling default constructors on each element.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load base address of static Unicode array (u_Testv104_6fa65f08)\n2. Initialize loop counter to 0x700 (1792 elements)\n3. Set current pointer to array base address\n4. Loop: Call Unicode::_default_constructor_closure_ on current wchar_t element\n5. Increment pointer by 2 bytes (size of wchar_t)\n6. Decrement loop counter\n7. Continue loop while counter != 0\n8. Return to caller\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value, modifies static data in place\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Array size: 0x700 (1792) wide characters = 3584 bytes total\n- Element size: 2 bytes per wchar_t\n- Constructor called: Unicode::_default_constructor_closure_\n- Static data location: 0x6fa65f08 (u_Testv104_6fa65f08)\n\nPurpose:\nThis function is a static initializer that ensures all elements in the Unicode array are properly constructed before program execution begins.",
