      "name": "InitializeFileStreamTables",
      "signature": "undefined4 InitializeFileStreamTables(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initialize file stream and descriptor tables for C runtime library\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Determine initial table size: 0x200 (512) if g_dwFileStreamCount is 0, otherwise min 0x14 (20)\n2. Allocate memory for file stream table: size * 4 bytes (array of pointers)\n3. If allocation fails, retry with minimum size 0x14 (20 entries)\n4. If retry fails, return error code 0x1a (allocation failure)\n5. Copy stream structure template pointers from g_StreamStructureTemplates (0x6ff7e340 to 0x6ff7e5c0)\n6. Initialize each table entry with template pointer, advancing by 0x20 (32) bytes per template\n7. Initialize file descriptor validity table from g_FileHandleStateArray\n8. For each descriptor, calculate bucket index using (index >> 5) and offset using (index & 0x1f) * 0x24\n9. Mark descriptors with invalid handles (-1 or 0) as 0xffffffff in g_FileDescriptorTable\n10. Return 0 on success\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\n0x1a - Memory allocation failed for stream table\n0x00 - Success, all tables initialized\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- g_dwFileStreamCount of 0 triggers maximum allocation (512 entries)\n- Fallback allocation size is 0x14 (20 entries minimum)\n- Stream templates are 0x20 (32) bytes each\n- Descriptor entries are 0x24 (36) bytes each, organized in buckets of 32\n- Invalid handle values are -1 (INVALID_HANDLE) or 0 (uninitialized)\n\nGlobal Variables:\ng_dwFileStreamCount @ 0x6ffa8260 - DWORD table size (input/output)\ng_ppFileStreamTable @ 0x6ffa7240 - Pointer to allocated stream table\ng_StreamStructureTemplates @ 0x6ff7e340 - Array of FILE structure templates\ng_FileDescriptorTable @ 0x6ff7e350 - Validity table for file descriptors\ng_FileHandleStateArray @ 0x6ffa7140 - Array of handle state structures",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.11b",
      "method": "NOP",
