      "name": "InitializeGameConfiguration",
      "signature": "int InitializeGameConfiguration(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Initializes game configuration and core game state by setting up configuration parameters and calling initialization routines.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call ResetGameStateAndUIControls to clean up any existing state\n2. Call CopyMemoryWithAlignment to configure game data with \"ProjectD2\" and \"Diablo_II\" settings\n3. Call additional game initialization routine\n4. Return success status (1)\n\nParameters:\nNone - Called with no parameters using __stdcall calling convention\n\nReturns:\nint - Returns 1 (success) after successful initialization\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- First parameter (0x7fffffff) appears to be a configuration limit or max value\n- Configuration strings \"ProjectD2\" and \"Diablo_II\" identify the game project\n- \"Preferred_Realm\" setting configured with null value during initialization\n- Function uses __stdcall convention with RET 0x4 indicating 4 bytes of stack cleanup\n\nNotes:\nThis is a high-level initialization wrapper that orchestrates game startup by calling lower-level configuration and state management routines. It appears to be called during game launch to establish the initial game environment.",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
