      "name": "ProcessRenderingSynchronization",
      "signature": "int ProcessRenderingSynchronization(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Synchronizes rendering initialization with game state\n\nMonitors rendering-enabled flag and coordinates with a synchronization event.\nReturns success (1) after initializing rendering state. Uses WaitForSingleObject\nwith timeout to wait for an event handle, validating the result before proceeding.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if rendering is enabled (DAT_6fa65e60)\n2. If enabled, set initialization flag and call InitializeRenderingState\n3. If not enabled and initialization not already done:\n   - Call Ordinal_10049 twice to get event status and handle\n   - Wait for the event with WaitForSingleObject (timeout 0)\n   - If wait successful, call cleanup (Ordinal_10036) and validate state\n   - If wait returns WAIT_TIMEOUT (0x102), mark as valid\n4. Call InitializeRenderingState and return success\n5. Return 1 on all paths\n\nParameters:\nNone\n\nReturns:\nint - Always returns 1 (success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- DAT_6fa65e60: Rendering enabled flag\n- DAT_6fa65e80: Initialization state flag (prevents duplicate initialization)\n- Ordinal_10049: Event status/handle retrieval function\n- WaitForSingleObject return values:\n  - 0: Event signaled (normal completion)\n  - 0x102: WAIT_TIMEOUT (timeout occurred)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:b65549732f7add9ff9660b3b35b0e36d45e5dbc08840ee37e1d103043b5daaff",
