      "name": "InitializeHeaderStringHash",
      "signature": "void InitializeHeaderStringHash(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes the hash value for the \\\"Header\\\" string.\\n\\nThis function computes and stores the string hash for \\\"Header\\\" in a global variable. The hash is computed using a custom hash function to enable fast string matching during parsing operations.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Push two zero parameters for hash function (flags and offset)\\n2. Push address of \\\"Header\\\" string constant\\n3. Call ComputeStringHash to compute the hash value\\n4. Store result in global hash storage location\\n5. Return to caller\\n\\nParameters:\\nNone\\n\\nReturns:\\nvoid - No return value\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Hash value stored at 0x6fa65f04 is used globally for comparisons\\n- String \\\"Header\\\" is a constant located at 0x6fa5ea10\\n- Uses __stdcall convention with callee cleanup",
