      "name": "ProcessGameInitialization",
      "signature": "uint ProcessGameInitialization(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "uint",
      "comment": "Manages game initialization and connection state transitions\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if game object at 0x6fa656c4 is initialized; return 0 if not\n2. Verify no reentrant call by checking flag at 0x6fa65ea8; abort if already in progress\n3. Set reentrance guard flag (0x6fa65ea8=1) and initialization flag (0x6fa65eb0=1)\n4. Call virtual function at +0x10 offset on game object to perform initial callback\n5. If callback returns 0: reset state, process UI command at [ESP+0x4], return result\n6. If callback succeeds: set flag 0x6fa65ea4=0, call FUN_6fa4fc40, process rendering queue\n7. Check initialization state flag (0x6fa65294):\n   - If not initialized: check game state at +0x4c offset\n   - If state != 0x66: initialize command processor, check state again\n   - If state == 0x65: process character data from +0x48 offset\n   - If no result: write registry values, initialize session, terminate process\n   - If has result: process UI command with result code 0x12\n8. If already initialized: set flag 0x6fa65be0=1, destroy UI controls, return 0\n9. Handle various error conditions with cleanup and virtual function calls\n\nReturn Values:\n- 0: Normal success or uninitialized state\n- 1: Game state check true (negative result converted)\n- UI command result: Varies by state path\n\nGlobal State Modified:\n- 0x6fa65ea8: Reentrance flag (1 during processing, 0 on exit)\n- 0x6fa65eb0: Initialization flag\n- 0x6fa65294: State flag\n- 0x6fa65ea4, 0x6fa65be0: State tracking flags\n- Registry writes to \"Diablo II\" keys\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Reentrance protection: Function aborts with exit(-1) if already processing\n- Multiple error paths with cleanup\n- Virtual function dispatch pattern (indirect calls via +0x10, +0x4c, +0x48, +0x28, +0x68)\n- State machine with 5+ branches based on game initialization state",
