      "name": "ToggleBit6FlagInStructure",
      "signature": "uint ToggleBit6FlagInStructure(void * pGameState)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined4",
      "comment": "Toggles bit 6 (0x40) of a flag field in a game structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load the game state pointer from global data location 0x6fa65abc\n2. XOR the word-sized flag at offset +0x1eb with 0x40 to toggle bit 6\n3. Return 1 to indicate success\n\nParameters:\npGameState: void * - Implicit parameter, global game state pointer at 0x6fa65abc\n\nReturns:\nuint - Always returns 1 (success code)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nThe function uses a global pointer rather than accepting pGameState as a parameter.\nBit 6 (0x40) is toggled regardless of other bits in the flag field.\nThe operation is a classic bit-flip pattern: field ^= 0x40\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name     Type    Description\n+0x1eb  2     flag_field     ushort  Bit 6 is toggled to enable/disable feature",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "NOP",
      "index": "NOP:d247edf8e2fc845b60fb73f3fa730cb84cd8748f29dbd4dd83675d070cc46c2b",
