      "name": "InitializeGameUIAndCommands",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameUIAndCommands(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes game UI controls and command objects based on game mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Destroy all existing UI controls in the control array (DAT_6fa653c0)\n2. Reset UI state variables: clear control count (DAT_6fa65e34), set active flag (DAT_6fa65e40=1), clear UI dirty flag (DAT_6fa65e60=0)\n3. Determine game mode from DAT_6fa65ad8 (0 = local mode, non-zero = Battle.Net mode)\n4. For Battle.Net mode (DAT_6fa65ad8 != 0):\n   - Create first command from DAT_6fa63d70, store in control array, set as event target\n   - Create second command from DAT_6fa63e00, store in control array\n   - Create third command from DAT_6fa63dd0, store in control array\n5. For local mode (DAT_6fa65ad8 == 0):\n   - Create first command from DAT_6fa638c0, store in control array, set as event target\n   - Create second command from DAT_6fa638f0, store in control array\n   - Create third command from DAT_6fa63920, store in control array\n6. For each created command, set entity bit flags to 1 (enable/activate)\n7. Dispatch command handler to process all commands\n8. Render Unicode text in UI box\n9. Set UI render callback to FUN_6fa52a60 (DAT_6fa6552c)\n10. If control array overflows (count >= 0x40), retrieve error code 0x60d, abort with error message\n\nParameters:\nNone - function operates on global UI control structures and game mode flags\n\nReturns:\nNone - void function\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Max controls: 0x40 (64) UI controls allowed in array DAT_6fa653c0\n- Abort on overflow: If array fills during command creation, calls CleanupAndAbort with error code 0x60d and exits\n- Mode-dependent creation: Command creation addresses vary based on Battle.Net vs local game mode\n- Global state arrays: Control references stored in DAT_6fa653c0 with count in DAT_6fa65e34",
