      "name": "ProcessMainGameCommands",
      "signature": "void ProcessMainGameCommands(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Processes up to 10 sequential game commands from the input queue.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if network connection is active (DAT_6fa656c4)\n2. If active: Set disconnect flags, clear entity flags at +0x35d and +0x37d, invoke disconnect handler\n3. Clear game state via FUN_6fa55d30 and load sky palette\n4. Load command counter from DAT_6fa65e30 (enforces 0-63 entry limit via 0x40 check)\n5. For each of 10 command sources (0x6fa63f80 through 0x6fa64130):\n   - Call ProcessGameCommand() to fetch next command\n   - Store result in command array DAT_6fa652b8 at [counter * 4]\n   - Increment counter and validate against 0x40 limit\n   - For certain commands: call dispatch_command_handler() and RenderUnicodeTextInBox()\n   - Commands 6-7: Call ModifyEntityStateBitFlags() twice for entity state update\n   - Command 8 (0x6fa64100): Call SetGlobalState() with command result (gates subsequent ops)\n   - Command 9 (0x6fa64130): Call ValidateAndClearScreenshotRegionBounds() and InitializeTimerCallback()\n   - Command 10 (0x6fa64010): If success, jump to FUN_6fa52560(); otherwise handle error\n6. On failure at any step: Call GetReturnAddress(0x624), CleanupAndAbort(), then _exit(-1)\n\nParameters:\n  None - uses 10 global command source addresses\n\nReturns:\n  void - Never returns on normal completion (jumps to FUN_6fa52560)\n  On error: Terminates process with exit code -1\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Magic Numbers:\n    0x40 = Command queue size limit (64 entries)\n    0x624 = Error code passed to GetReturnAddress for error handling\n    0x35d, 0x37d = Entity flag offsets in context structure for disconnect\n    0x13fd, 0x1401, 0x1402, 0x1403 = Dispatcher parameter values for command handlers\n  Array Indexing: Uses stride of 4 bytes per entry (ECX*0x4 offset into DAT_6fa652b8)\n  Command Dependencies: Each command depends on counter < 0x40; failure exits immediately\n  State Gates: Command 8 result gates all subsequent operations via SetGlobalState()\n  Final Command: Command 10 succeeds when all 10 commands fit within 0x40 limit\n\nStructure Access:\n  DAT_6fa65abc = Main context pointer\n    Offset +0x35d: Disconnect flag byte\n    Offset +0x37d: Disconnect flag byte\n  DAT_6fa656c4 = Network connection state pointer\n  DAT_6fa65e30 = Command queue counter (0-63)\n  DAT_6fa652b8 = Command result array (stride 4 bytes per entry)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
