      "name": "InitializeUIAssets",
      "signature": "void InitializeUIAssets(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "undefined",
      "comment": "Initializes UI assets by building localized file paths and loading asset pointers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Format image asset file paths using wsprintfA with format string and DATA_GLOBAL path\n2. Call BuildLocalizedFilePath to convert format string to full file path\n3. Store returned pointer in global UI asset variable (e.g., DAT_6fa65be4 for blizzard logo)\n4. For expansion-dependent assets: Call FindAndValidateD2ExpMpq to check D2X.mpq existence\n5. Select asset variant: if expansion detected (result != 0), use LoD/expansion path; else use classic path\n6. Format variant path using wsprintfA with conditional format string\n7. Build localized path and store in corresponding global variable\n8. Repeat for all 40 UI asset categories (logos, buttons, backgrounds, dialogs, etc.)\n9. Total assets loaded: ~44 global pointers across categories\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Expansion-dependent assets: Trademark, Title Screen, Credits, Realm Buttons (4 checks)\n- Conditional asset block: Cinematic assets only loaded if expansion detected (block 0x6fa5325b-0x6fa532f1)\n- Mixed string functions: Uses wsprintfA and _sprintf interchangeably for formatting\n- Common assets: Core UI elements (buttons, backgrounds) always loaded regardless of expansion\n\nReturns: void (modifies global variables only)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
