      "name": "ReportSecurityError",
      "signature": "void ReportSecurityError(int errorType)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Runtime security error handler that reports buffer overrun or unknown security failures.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize SEH (Structured Exception Handling) and XOR stack cookie validation\n2. Check if custom callback handler (DAT_6fa6513c) is registered\n3. If callback exists: Push parameters and call callback function, then set error marker\n4. If callback null: Determine error message strings based on errorType (1=buffer overrun, other=unknown)\n5. Call GetModuleFileNameA to retrieve the executable filename\n6. If GetModuleFileNameA fails: Copy fallback text \"<program_name_unknown>\"\n7. Check if filename length + description exceeds 60 characters (0x3c)\n8. If exceeds limit: Truncate filename and append \"...\" ellipsis marker\n9. Calculate required buffer size: filename + 11 + ESI value + 12 + 3 bytes, aligned to 4-byte boundary\n10. Allocate stack space via __chkstk probe\n11. Build complete error message by concatenating: error_description + separator + \"Program \" + filename + separator + error_details\n12. Display message box with constructed message and \"Microsoft Visual C++ Runtime Library\" title\n13. Call __exit(3) to terminate process with status code 3\n\nParameters:\nerrorType (int) - Error type indicator: 1 for buffer overrun detection, any other value for unknown security failure\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function never returns; always terminates the process via __exit(3)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- DAT_6fa6513c callback: When non-null, invokes custom error handler before building message\n- Filename truncation: If module filename too long, appends \"...\" instead of full path\n- ESI register value: Contains size constant (0xd4 for unknown error, 0xb9 for buffer overrun)\n- Stack allocation: Uses dynamic __chkstk to probe large stack allocation\n- Process termination: Always exits with code 3 regardless of error type",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:9edd5270653ada86eeecdcb3502d3803",
