      "name": "ExtendFileWithZeros",
      "signature": "void ExtendFileWithZeros(uint fileDescriptor, uint targetSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Extends a file to a specified size by padding with zero bytes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Save current file position using __lseek_lk(fd, 0, SEEK_CUR)\n2. Seek to end-of-file using __lseek_lk(fd, 0, SEEK_END) to get current size\n3. Calculate bytes needed: targetSize - currentEOF\n4. If bytes needed < 0: File is larger than target, seek to targetSize and call SetEndOfFile to truncate\n5. If bytes needed == 0: File is already correct size, no operation needed\n6. If bytes needed > 0: Pad file with zeros in 4KB chunks:\n   a. Clear 4KB buffer with memset\n   b. Switch file to binary mode using __setmode_lk(fd, 0x8000)\n   c. Enter write loop: write min(bytesNeeded, 4KB) to file repeatedly\n   d. On write error with code 5 (access denied), map to errno 13 (EACCES)\n   e. Restore original file mode using __setmode_lk(fd, savedMode)\n7. Restore original file position using __lseek_lk(fd, savedPosition, SEEK_SET)\n8. All errors indicated via errno, no return value\n\nParameters:\n  fileDescriptor: File descriptor from open() call\n  targetSize: Target file size in bytes to extend or truncate to\n\nReturns:\n  void; all errors reported via errno global variable\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If initial position seek fails, returns early with file unchanged\n  - If EOF seek fails, returns early with file unchanged\n  - If file already at target size, performs no I/O\n  - If file larger than target, uses SetEndOfFile for fast truncation\n  - If file smaller than target, pads in 4KB chunks for efficiency\n  - Restores file mode to binary after write loop to preserve original mode\n  - Maps Windows access denied error (5) to POSIX EACCES (13)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
