      "name": "RenderEntityDisplayScreen",
      "signature": "void RenderEntityDisplayScreen(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Renders the entity display screen showing character stats, skills, and information.\n\nThis function handles the primary rendering pipeline for displaying entity information\non screen. It validates game data, renders character details with Unicode text conversion,\nmanages skill tier displays, and handles various entity state types with appropriate\nvisual rendering modes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate game MPQ data integrity via FindAndValidateD2ExpMpq()\n2. Initialize display state: get base Y offset from global offset table\n3. Process entity slots: iterate through active slot counter with state initialization\n4. For each iteration, clear resource state and initialize system state\n5. Check display rendering condition (global state flags)\n6. Iterate through entity chain (linked via offset 0x34c)\n7. For each entity, determine if it falls within valid rendering range\n   - If outside range: store zero validation status\n   - If within range: calculate relative slot index\n8. Set entity rendering properties and object display flags\n9. Handle three entity state types:\n   - Type 1: Special mode render with conditional panel display\n   - Type 2: Standard render mode with flag-based property display\n   - Type 0: Full character display with skill information\n10. For standard display mode: render skill tier name, character name, level, and flags\n11. Calculate skill cooldown remaining time and render with appropriate display style\n12. Render entity panel with conditional special states (enchantment, special ability)\n13. Advance to next entity in chain and repeat from step 6\n\nParameters:\nNone - function operates on global game state data\n\nReturns:\nvoid - renders to screen via RenderTextBoxUnicodeText and RenderTextBoxWithUnicodeConversion\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic values: 0x100 (buffer size), 0x15180 (cooldown divisor, approximately 90000 frames)\n- 0x5d pixel Y-offset increment between rendered entities\n- Entity flags offset 0x324 checked for bit masks: 0x8 (inventory), 0x4 (property mode), 0x20 (special effect)\n- Skill tier offset 0x322 contains encoded skill information (16-bit value)\n- State type value 0x7 triggers parameter field modification with 0xfffffffb",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:ed37b08eb9684c545f86e51c77f3dc33",
