      "name": "ResetGameStateAndUIControls",
      "signature": "void ResetGameStateAndUIControls(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Resets game state and UI controls\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if controls array is initialized (DAT_6fa65ad4 == 1)\n2. If initialized, iterate through all controls in array at DAT_6fa653c0\n3. For each control, call DestroyUIControl to clean up resources\n4. Set control count (DAT_6fa65e34) to 0\n5. Call InitializeGameState to reinitialize game state\n6. Always set global flag DAT_6fa65984 to 0\n7. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\nNone - called without parameters using __stdcall convention\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If DAT_6fa65ad4 != 1, skips UI control cleanup\n- Array at DAT_6fa653c0 contains pointers to UI control objects\n- Each iteration increments pointer by 4 bytes (sizeof(pointer))\n- Loop processes exactly DAT_6fa65e34 control objects\n- Always sets cleanup flag DAT_6fa65984 to 0 on exit\n\nStructure Layout:\nGlobal Variables:\nOffset | Type     | Name           | Description\n-------|----------|----------------|---------------------------\n       | int      | DAT_6fa65ad4   | Initialization flag (1=initialized)\n       | int      | DAT_6fa65e34   | Control count / array size\n       | int*[]   | DAT_6fa653c0   | Control object array base\n       | int      | DAT_6fa65984   | Cleanup/reset flag",
