      "name": "ProcessAnimationFrame",
      "signature": "uint ProcessAnimationFrame(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Searches linked list of animation nodes and updates animation frame state.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Initialize counter to zero and get first animation node from global\\n2. Loop through animation node linked list (offset +0x34c to next)\\n3. Compare counter with global index (DAT_6fa64db0) to find target node\\n4. When target found, check if Unicode name at +0x100 is valid\\n5. Convert Unicode name to Windows format using buffer\\n6. Call UpdateAnimationFrame to process animation\\n7. If update returns zero, dispatch command handler and initialize UI\\n8. If update returns non-zero, increment frame counter and continue\\n9. Otherwise finalize animation and return success\\n\\nParameters:\\nNone (uses global animation context)\\n\\nReturns:\\n0 - Animation list is empty or animation not found\\n1 - Animation frame processed successfully\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- Empty animation list returns 0\\n- Invalid Unicode name at offset +0x100 skips processing\\n- Animation update failure (non-zero return) triggers command dispatch and UI init\\n- Uses static buffer (256 bytes) for Unicode conversion\\n\\nStructure Layout:\\nAnimation node layout (from assembly):\\nOffset  Size  Field Name        Type      Description\\n+0x100  2     unicodeName       Unicode   Unicode string for animation name\\n+0x34c  4     nextNode          ptr       Pointer to next animation in linked list",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:493e14c842c0b8c652856cfdf9941332",
