      "name": "InitializeGameState",
      "signature": "int InitializeGameState(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initialize game state and rendering systems\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call first state management function from vtable at DAT_6fa656c4 + 0xc\n2. If result is non-zero, initialize rendering state\n3. Check if initialization flag (DAT_6fa65ea0) is zero\n4. If flag is zero and second vtable function (DAT_6fa656c4 + 0x68) returns non-zero\n5. Check if game execution is disabled (g_gameExecutionEnabled == 0)\n6. If game execution is disabled, call rendering initialization\n7. Return success status (1)\n\nReturns:\n1 on success\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Function always returns 1 regardless of initialization success\n- Conditional rendering initialization based on state flags\n- Uses function pointers from game state vtable",
