      "name": "ProcessGameUICommand",
      "signature": "int ProcessGameUICommand(int * pCommandRecord)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Processes game UI initialization commands and dispatches to appropriate handlers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate three Unicode string buffers (512 chars each = 2048 bytes total)\n2. Extract command ID from pCommandRecord->dwCommandId (EDI+0x0)\n3. Perform switch dispatch on command ID (cases 0x0 through 0x1b)\n4. For command-specific cases: set configStringId and handlerType flags\n5. For cases 6/10 (custom UI): validate param at pCommandRecord->pCustomData (EDI+0x4)\n6. Retrieve three configuration strings via dispatch_command_handler() into buffers\n7. Dispatch to appropriate handler based on handlerType:\n   - Type 0: InitializeBattleNetUIControls(primary, callback, 1)\n   - Type 1: InitializeUIWithGameCommands(tertiary, primary, callback)\n   - Type 2: InitializeUIControlsWithParameters(tertiary, primary, secondary, callback)\n8. If shouldDispatchCallback: call DispatchCallbackOrVirtualFunction and invoke virtual at offset +0x10\n9. Return 0\n\nParameters:\n- pCommandRecord: Pointer to command structure containing:\n  - Offset +0x0: dwCommandId (UI initialization command type, range 0-27)\n  - Offset +0x4: pCustomData (optional pointer for custom UI data, NULL for most commands)\n\nReturns:\n- 0 on all paths (void return encoded as int)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Command 0x1b (31): Special handling for UTF8 conversion with dispatch integration\n- Cases 6/10 (BattleNet UI): Validate pCustomData is not NULL before processing\n- Invalid command: Falls through to default case, returns without initialization\n- Magic numbers: 0x147c-0x1481 are string resource IDs, 0x2bb0-0x2bb2 for special cases\n\nCallback Invocation:\n- Conditional callback dispatch based on shouldDispatchCallback flag (set false for some command groups)\n- Virtual function invoked from DAT_6fa656c4 at offset +0x10 (likely vtable entry)",
