      "name": "InitializeRenderingSystem",
      "signature": "int InitializeRenderingSystem(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes the rendering system by invoking virtual method and state setup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load global rendering context pointer from 0x6fa656c4\n2. Load rendering parameters address (0x6fa5e256) into ECX\n3. Call virtual method at offset 0xb8 in rendering context object\n4. Call InitializeRenderingState function to complete initialization\n5. Return 1 to indicate successful initialization\n\nReturns:\n1 - Initialization completed successfully\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- RET 0x4 indicates __stdcall convention with hidden parameter on stack\n- Global at 0x6fa656c4 must be initialized before this function is called\n- Called from FUN_6fa4fe00 during game initialization sequence",
