      "name": "UpdateUIControlState",
      "signature": "void UpdateUIControlState(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Updates the UI control state by dispatching a command handler and rendering status text.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if global flag DAT_6fa65548 is enabled; exit if not set\n2. Call dispatch handler at offset 0x80 in DAT_6fa656c4 to get command result\n3. Use switch table (cases 0-6) to convert command to status code 0x1433-0x1439, default to -1\n4. Call ClearResourceState() to reset UI state\n5. If status code is not -1 (valid), dispatch command handler with zero parameters\n6. Render text box with Unicode text rendering\n7. Retrieve current tick count and calculate elapsed time since DAT_6fa65558\n8. Format elapsed time in 250ms intervals (0-19 range) using sprintf\n9. Call ClearResourceState() again\n10. Render final text output in UI control\n\nParameters: none\n\nReturns: void (no return value)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic number 0x10624dd3 is used for time calculation precision\n- Time interval 0xfa (250ms) divides time into 20 buckets (0-19)\n- Result -1 indicates invalid command, which skips rendering\n- Character buffer is 256 bytes on stack for formatted time string\n\nStructure Layout:\nGlobal state used:\n  DAT_6fa65548: Control enable flag\n  DAT_6fa65550: Current status code result\n  DAT_6fa65558: Reference tick count\n  DAT_6fa656c4: Handler object pointer (+0x80 offset for dispatch)\n  DAT_6fa6554c: UI control object\n  DAT_6fa5c364: GetTickCount function pointer\n  DAT_6fa5e9e0: Format string pointer\n  DAT_6fa5e9e8: String constant",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
