      "name": "UpdateUIElementsOnTextChange",
      "signature": "void UpdateUIElementsOnTextChange(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Validates and processes an email-format string with '@' and '.' delimiters.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve Unicode string from object field via ValidateAndGetObjectField()\n2. Calculate string length using Unicode::strlen()\n3. If string length > 0:\n   a. Convert Unicode string to UTF-8 buffer (256 bytes max) using toUtf()\n   b. Search for '@' symbol (0x40) in converted string using FindCharInString()\n   c. If '@' found, search for '.' (0x2e) after '@' position\n   d. Validate positions: buffer < '@' position and '@'+1 < '.' position\n   e. If all validations pass, calculate string length via CalculateStringLength()\n4. Modify object bitfield using ModifyObjectBitfield()\n5. Return void\n\nReturns:\nvoid\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Email format requires '@' followed by '.' with valid spacing\n- Both '@' (0x40) and '.' (0x2e) symbols must exist and be properly positioned\n- String must be non-empty (length > 0)\n- Maximum UTF-8 buffer size is 0x100 (256 bytes)\n- Sets EBX=1 if email validation succeeds, EBX=0 on failure",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:8e50fd0ce47114b4062a09e96cb3e1f9",
