      "name": "ValidateAndCompareObjectLengths",
      "signature": "uint ValidateAndCompareObjectLengths(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Validates and compares the lengths of two object fields.\n\nThis function retrieves two Unicode string fields from global object pointers,\nmeasures their lengths using strlen, and modifies a bitfield based on whether\nboth strings are non-empty.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load first object field pointer from global address 0x6fa65e84\n2. Load second object field pointer from global address 0x6fa65e88\n3. Call strlen on first field and set flag if length > 0\n4. Call strlen on second field and set flag if length > 0\n5. Combine both flags using bitwise OR\n6. Call ModifyObjectBitfield with combined flag result\n7. Return success (1)\n\nReturns:\nuint - Always returns 1 (success)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Both flags are combined with OR, so modification happens if either string is non-empty\n- Function uses __stdcall calling convention with 4-byte parameter cleanup",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:fb081a2aaf05ed297201ad0533db6863",
