      "name": "InitializeGameConfigConstants",
      "signature": "void InitializeGameConfigConstants(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes game configuration constants when system state is ready.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Call system initialization function\\n2. Check if initialization status equals 9\\n3. If status equals 9:\\n   a. Load configuration value 0x22B into EAX register\\n   b. Load configuration value 0x23F into ECX register\\n   c. Initialize 15 global configuration constants with specific values\\n   d. Use preloaded values for some constants (0x22B and 0x23F)\\n4. Return to caller\\n\\nReturns:\\n  void - No return value\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n  Status check: Only initializes constants if initialization status == 9\\n  Magic numbers: 0x9B, 0x14E, 0x184, 0x1BA, 0xF0, 0x158, 0x9C, 0x1FA, 0x22B, 0x23F, 0x253, 0x46, 0xEE\\n  Register optimization: Values 0x22B and 0x23F are preloaded into registers for reuse",
