      "name": "InitializeCharacterCreationUIResources",
      "signature": "void InitializeCharacterCreationUIResources(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initialize UI resources for character creation screen with localized file paths\\n\\nALGORITHM:\\n1. Check initialization guard variable (DAT_6fa65c10) to skip if already initialized\\n2. Build localized path for MediumSelButtonBl UI element via wsprintfA\\n3. Call BuildLocalizedFilePath() to resolve path and cache in DAT_6fa65c30\\n4. Validate D2 expansion installed via FindAndValidateD2ExpMpq()\\n5. Select character creation path based on expansion (suffix 's' for expansion)\\n6. Build and cache paths for CharacterCreate UI element (expansion variant)\\n7. Build and cache paths for fire, textbox, and clickbox base UI elements\\n8. If expansion present, build and cache 12 class-specific UI assets (Assassin, Druid variants)\\n9. Build and cache 15 base character class UI assets (Amazon, Necromancer, Barbarian, Sorceress, Paladin, Assassin variants)\\n10. Set initialization guard and return\\n\\nPARAMETERS:\\nNone - operates on global UI resource cache variables\\n\\nRETURNS:\\nvoid - initializes global variables DAT_6fa65c10 through DAT_6fa65db0\\n\\nSPECIAL CASES:\\n- Guard variable DAT_6fa65c10 prevents duplicate initialization\\n- Expansion detection affects character class asset loading\\n- Local buffer pathBuffer[260] holds temp localized paths before caching\\n- All paths built using wsprintfA and BuildLocalizedFilePath pair pattern\\n- Cache addresses are dispersed through data segment for per-UI-element storage\\n\\nSTRUCTURE LAYOUT:\\nNot applicable - function operates on scattered global cache variables rather than a structure",
