      "name": "CheckSaveGameExists",
      "signature": "int CheckSaveGameExists(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Checks if a save game file exists on disk\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call BuildSaveGamePath() to construct the save game directory path\n2. Format the full save game filename using sprintf with the template string at 0x6fa5dd60\n3. Call FindFirstFileA() to search for the formatted filename\n4. Compare result with INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE (0xffffffff)\n5. If handle is valid (file found): Call FindClose() to close the handle and return 1\n6. If handle is invalid (file not found): Return 0 without closing handle\n\nReturns:\n1 if save game file exists, 0 if file does not exist\n\nParameters:\nNone - function uses global game state initialized by BuildSaveGamePath()\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- No parameters are used; all data comes from previously initialized global state\n- FindClose() is only called when a valid file handle is obtained (file exists)\n- Magic number -0x1 (0xffffffff) is the INVALID_HANDLE_VALUE constant used by Windows API",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:2629e4468351b00800a26386b86123ba",
