      "name": "ToggleGameStateFlag",
      "signature": "bool ToggleGameStateFlag(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Toggles bit 2 (flag 0x4) in the game state control field at offset 0x1eb of the global game structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load pointer to global game state structure from address 0x6fa65abc\n2. XOR the ushort value at offset +0x1eb with 0x4 to toggle bit 2\n3. Return 1 (success/true)\n\nReturns:\nbool - Always returns 1 (success)\n\nPurpose:\nThis function toggles a control flag in the game state, affecting some aspect of game behavior or UI state. The flag is stored in a 16-bit field and bit 2 controls the toggled feature.",
