      "name": "InitializeBattleNetConnection",
      "signature": "int InitializeBattleNetConnection(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initialize Battle.Net connection by searching for a valid connection slot\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load upper bound counter from DAT_6fa65e30\n2. Initialize slot search index EDI to 0\n3. Loop through connection slots starting at DAT_6fa652b8 with 4-byte stride\n4. For each slot, call GetFirstFieldOrNull to check slot status\n5. If returned value is 4, break loop (slot not ready)\n6. Otherwise increment slot index and continue until index exceeds upper bound\n7. If valid slot found (ESI != 0), validate it with ValidateAndGetWindowData\n8. If validation succeeds (return > 0), navigate list by calling NavigateListByIndex with count-1\n9. Return 1 on success, or call error handler with Battle.Net message on failure\n\nParameters: (implicit) - Function uses __stdcall convention with 4-byte stack cleanup\n\nReturns: int - 1 on successful connection initialization, calls _exit(-1) on failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If DAT_6fa65e30 is less than 0, jumps directly to error handler\n- If no valid slot found in loop, jumps to error handler\n- Error message: \"Can't connect to Battle.Net. Try again later.\"\n- Return address for error handler taken from stack via GetReturnAddress(0xccf)",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:98e5aac9c58ee1f946ab7db1dcd5a239",
