      "name": "UpdateUIElementsOnTextChange",
      "signature": "void UpdateUIElementsOnTextChange(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Validates local IP address and dispatches command handler if valid.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Retrieve local IP address string via GetLocalIPAddress()\n2. Clear resource state via ClearResourceState()\n3. Initialize comparison counter to 10 (max bytes to compare)\n4. Set expected match flag to true\n5. Perform byte-by-byte string comparison with reference data at 0x6fa5e0a8 using REPE CMPSB\n6. Continue comparing until counter reaches 0 or byte mismatch found\n7. If IP address matches: dispatch command handler and render unicode text in UI box\n8. If IP address doesn't match: render error text in UI control\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function performs side effects (UI rendering and command dispatch) but returns no value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Comparison is limited to first 10 bytes of IP string\n- Magic number 0x1404 passed to dispatch_command_handler() indicates command type\n- EDX register set to 0x0 for valid IP (success), 0x1 for invalid IP (failure) when calling ModifyObjectBitfield()\n- Reference IP data stored in read-only memory at 0x6fa5e0a8",
