      "name": "ProcessAndRenderScaledFrameText",
      "signature": "void ProcessAndRenderScaledFrameText(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Processes frame timing percentage and renders scaled text display.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear the current resource state\n2. Retrieve the frame percentage value from state object (capped at 100)\n3. Validate and get the base frame count from game state\n4. Calculate scaled frame count: (baseFrameCount * percentage) / 100\n5. Store the calculated scaled frame count in game state\n6. Format frame percentage into a string buffer using sprintf\n7. If text rendering is enabled, render the formatted text as unicode\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Updates game state and renders UI as side effects\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Frame percentage is capped at maximum value of 100 to prevent overflow\n- If rendering flag at 0x6fa65e64 is 0, text rendering is skipped\n- Uses fixed-point division with magic multiplier 0x51eb851f for scaling",
