      "name": "EnqueueGameCommand",
      "signature": "int EnqueueGameCommand(int commandIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Enqueues a game command from the command array for processing.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load and compare global command queue counter (DAT_6fa65e34) against limit 0x40 (64)\n2. If counter >= 64, call GetReturnAddress(0x60d) to get error location\n3. Call CleanupAndAbort with error message and return address, then exit with code -1\n4. Calculate command structure pointer: commandIndex * 3 * 16 (0x30) + base array DAT_6fa60f20\n5. Call ProcessGameCommand with calculated command structure pointer\n6. Load current queue counter (DAT_6fa65e34) into ECX\n7. Store result from ProcessGameCommand into DAT_6fa653c0[counter] using ECX*4 offset\n8. Increment ECX and write back to DAT_6fa65e34\n9. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\ncommandIndex - Command index parameter passed implicitly in EAX (or via calling convention)\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Function returns no explicit value to caller, but result of ProcessGameCommand is stored in queue array\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Magic number 0x40 (64): Maximum command queue size limit\n- Magic number 0x30 (48): Command structure size calculated as index * 3 * 16 bytes\n- Magic number 0x60d (1549): Error location code for fatal abort\n- If queue exceeds maximum capacity, function calls fatal error handler without recovery\n- Global DAT_6fa65e34 tracks current queue count and is incremented after each enqueue",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:01fa949902417ef1493255e929e43fe1",
