      "name": "LoadAndApplyRenderingConfig",
      "signature": "uint LoadAndApplyRenderingConfig(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Loads and applies rendering configuration from config data buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 512-byte stack buffer for configuration data\n2. Call ReadConfigDataBuffer() to load configuration into buffer\n3. Check return value (-1 indicates failure):\n   - If failure: jump to check_rendering_flag to evaluate existing state\n   - If success: examine first byte of configuration buffer\n4. Check sentinel byte value:\n   - If 0xAF (-0x51): Set DAT_6fa65e7c = 1, call InitializeRenderingState(), return 1\n   - If 0xB0 (-0x50): Set DAT_6fa65e7c = 0, continue to flag check\n   - Otherwise: Jump to check_rendering_flag\n5. Check DAT_6fa65e7c (rendering state flag):\n   - If non-zero: Jump to call_initialize_rendering\n   - If zero: Check DAT_6fa65e60 (secondary flag)\n6. Check DAT_6fa65e60:\n   - If zero: Return 1\n   - If non-zero: Call InitializeRenderingState()\n7. Return 1 (success status)\n\nReturns:\nAlways returns 1 (success). The function always succeeds regardless of\nconfiguration read result or initialization outcome.\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Sentinel bytes 0xAF and 0xB0 control rendering state initialization\n- Function always returns 1 even if configuration read fails\n- If read fails, behavior depends on existing DAT_6fa65e7c and DAT_6fa65e60 flags\n- DAT_6fa65e7c acts as a rendering state flag (0=disabled, 1=enabled)\n- DAT_6fa65e60 appears to be a secondary rendering control flag",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:7c4c1725c01481276475329890911f07",
