      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Processes resource state by extracting a resource reference and clearing related state.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load parameter from stack (pResourceObject)\n2. Extract resource reference from offset +0xc within the resource object\n3. Pass resource reference and constants (0x140c, 0xfa8) to ProcessResourceState handler\n4. Return success status (1)\n\nParameters:\n- pResourceObject: Pointer to resource object structure with state info at offset +0xc\n\nReturns:\n1 (indicates successful processing)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Accesses offset +0xc from parameter structure\n- Uses magic constants 0x140c and 0xfa8 as arguments to handler function\n- Always returns success (1)\n\nStructure Layout:\nOffset 0x00: [unknown fields]\nOffset 0x0C: Resource reference (dword) - extracted and passed to handler",
