      "name": "DispatchResourceCommand",
      "signature": "int DispatchResourceCommand(int * pCommandData)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Dispatches a resource command to the resource management system with fixed command codes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load command data structure pointer from stack parameter\n2. Extract command/resource ID from offset +0xc within command data\n3. Set up stack frame for function call with three arguments:\n   - First argument: extracted ID from pCommandData[+0xc]\n   - Second argument: constant 0xfa7 (resource handler code 4007)\n   - Third argument: constant 0x140a (resource command code 5130)\n4. Load constant 0x4 into ESI register (likely return status flag)\n5. Call FUN_6fa521b0() to process resource command with these parameters\n6. Set return value to 1 (success status)\n7. Restore stack frame and return via RET 0x4 (caller cleanup of 1 param)\n\nParameters:\n  pCommandData (int*) - Pointer to command data structure containing resource information\n                        Accessed at offset +0xc to retrieve command/resource ID\n\nReturns:\n  int - Always returns 1 indicating successful dispatch\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  Magic numbers: 0xfa7 (4007) is the resource handler code, 0x140a (5130) is the command code\n  All commands are dispatched through FUN_6fa521b0 with the same fixed codes\n  Return value is always 1 regardless of actual command result\n\nStructure Layout:\n  Offset  Size  Field Name        Type      Description\n  +0x0    4     [unknown]         dword     Command structure base\n  +0xc    4     commandId         dword     Resource/command identifier",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
