      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Process a resource command by extracting the command ID and executing the associated handler.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract the command parameter from the input structure at offset +0xc\n2. Push magic values 0x1409 and 0xfa9 as configuration parameters\n3. Call the resource handler function with the command ID and configuration\n4. Return success status (1)\n\nParameters:\n  pCommandData (void*): Pointer to command data structure containing command ID at offset +0xc\n\nReturns:\n  uint: Always returns 1 (success status)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - The magic values 0x1409 and 0xfa9 appear to be resource type/subtype identifiers\n  - Uses __stdcall convention with 4-byte parameter cleanup",
