      "name": "ValidateAndProcessStateData",
      "signature": "int ValidateAndProcessStateData(int * pStateData)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Validates MPQ expansion file and processes game state data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FindAndValidateD2ExpMpq() to check expansion file access\n2. If validation fails (returns 0), return 0 immediately\n3. Load pStateData pointer from stack (parameter at ESP+0x4)\n4. Extract value at offset +0xc from pStateData structure\n5. Load ESI=5 (state identifier or context flag)\n6. Call FUN_6fa521b0() with three pushed magic values and extracted parameter\n7. Set EAX=1 (success flag)\n8. Return 1 to caller\n\nParameters:\npStateData: Pointer to state data structure with parameter stored at offset +0xc\n\nReturns:\n1 on success (expansion file valid and state processed)\n0 on failure (expansion file validation failed)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nMagic values 0x57f6 and 0x2771 are pushed as part of state processing parameters.\nESI register is set to 0x5 before calling FUN_6fa521b0, suggesting game state ID or mode identifier.\nCalled only when current state type matches specific constant (DAT_6fa654f0).",
