      "name": "ValidateAndProcessExpansionState",
      "signature": "uint ValidateAndProcessExpansionState(int * pStateData)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Validates MPQ expansion files and processes expansion-specific state initialization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FindAndValidateD2ExpMpq() to check expansion file availability\n2. If validation fails (returns 0), return 0 immediately\n3. If validation succeeds, load pStateData[3] from parameter at offset +0xc\n4. Push parameters ESI, 0x57f7 (constant), 0x2772 (constant), and pStateData[3]\n5. Call FUN_6fa521b0() to process expansion state with these parameters\n6. Set ESI=6 (register constant, likely count or mode)\n7. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\npStateData: Pointer to state data structure; pStateData[3] (offset +0xc) contains expansion-specific state value to process\n\nReturns:\n0 if MPQ expansion validation fails; 1 if state processing succeeds\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Constants 0x57f7 and 0x2772 are passed to FUN_6fa521b0() for state identification\n- This function is only called when game state type 6 is active (expansion-specific state)\n- Early return on MPQ validation failure prevents further processing of invalid expansion state",
