      "name": "DestroyAllUIControls",
      "signature": "void DestroyAllUIControls(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Destroys all UI controls in the global control array and resets the control count to zero.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Load the current UI control count from DAT_6fa65e34\\n2. If count is greater than 0, initialize loop to iterate through all controls\\n3. For each control in the array starting at DAT_6fa653c0:\\n   - Call DestroyUIControl with pointer to current control\\n   - Increment loop index\\n   - Move to next control (add 4 bytes to pointer for next element)\\n   - Continue until all controls processed\\n4. Clear the global control count by setting DAT_6fa65e34 to 0\\n\\nData Structures:\\n- DAT_6fa653c0: Array of UI control pointers (4 bytes per element)\\n- DAT_6fa65e34: Global counter tracking number of active UI controls\\n\\nReturns:\\nvoid - Function performs cleanup only, no return value\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\n- If control count is 0 or negative, loop is skipped and count is set to 0\\n- Array access uses pointer arithmetic (EDI+4) for consecutive controls\\n- Control count is always reset to 0 after destruction, regardless of actual controls destroyed",
      "name_source": "LoD/PD2",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:ac49e22c446f134ba5af5014e5fd00ec",
