      "name": "InitializeGameAndEnterMainLoop",
      "signature": "int InitializeGameAndEnterMainLoop(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes game state flag and enters the main game loop.\\n\\nAlgorithm:\\n1. Set the initialization flag (DAT_6fa65e40) to 1 to indicate game is running\\n2. Call the main game loop function (FUN_6fa59290) which handles:\\n   - Connection validation and disconnection handling\\n   - Command queue initialization and processing\\n   - UI rendering and text output\\n   - Audio system initialization\\n   - Game state setup and initialization\\n3. Return success status (1) to caller\\n\\nReturns:\\nReturns 1 (TRUE) to indicate successful initialization and main loop execution.\\n\\nSpecial Cases:\\nThis function always returns success (1) regardless of game state. The actual \\ngame loop execution and error handling occurs in FUN_6fa59290. If the game \\ninitialization fails, FUN_6fa59290 calls exit(-1) and does not return to this \\nfunction.",
