      "name": "InitializeGameState",
      "signature": "int InitializeGameState(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes the game state by resetting UI elements and loading game data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call InitializeAllGameObjectTimings() to set up game object timing data\n2. Call FUN_6fa55d30() to destroy existing UI controls and reset game state\n3. Call FUN_6fa4d5d0() to initialize game data structures, game objects, UI elements, and load game configuration\n4. Return 1 to indicate successful initialization\n\nReturns:\n  EAX = 1 - Always returns success code\n\nPurpose:\nThis function performs a complete game state initialization sequence, typically called during game startup or when reloading game data. It clears any existing UI state, reinitializes all game data structures, and prepares the game for play.",
